#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "US ballistic vest"
msgid "US ballistic vest"
msgid_plural "US ballistic vests"
msgstr[0] "US防彈背心"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "US ballistic vest"
msgid ""
"A ballistic vest with specialized pockets on the front, back, and sides to "
"hold armor plates.  While this plate carrier is still protective even without "
"inserts, it's too soft to effectively stop high-energy projectiles on its own."
msgstr "一件胸前、背后及身侧有专门装甲板口袋的防弹背心。虽然口袋不插入装甲板依旧能够提供少许防护，但它太软，无法阻挡高速子弹。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of variant "US ballistic vest" of item "US ballistic vest"
msgid ""
"This version is patterned in multi-environment camouflage, and was "
"standard-issue for the US Army."
msgstr "这个型号采用多环境迷彩，是美国陆军使用的制式版本。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "US ballistic vest"
msgid "SWAT ballistic vest"
msgid_plural "SWAT ballistic vests"
msgstr[0] "特警防彈背心"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of variant "SWAT ballistic vest" of item "US ballistic vest"
msgid ""
"This version is colored black, and was once used by specialized police "
"forces.  \"SWAT\" is emblazoned on the back."
msgstr "这个型号是纯黑色版本，曾经由特种警察部队使用。背面印着SWAT字样。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "US ballistic vest"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "US heavy ballistic vest"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "light ballistic vest (mag pouches)"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "light ballistic vest (storage pouch)"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "light ballistic vest (shoulder pouch)"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "hard armor vest"
msgid "Pocket for a large armor plate."
msgstr "大裝甲板口袋"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "US ballistic vest"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "US heavy ballistic vest"
msgid "Pocket for a medium armor plate."
msgstr "中裝甲板口袋"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "EOD jacket"
msgid_plural "EOD jackets"
msgstr[0] "拆彈防護衣"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "EOD jacket"
msgid ""
"A thick armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for "
"use by explosive ordnance disposal technicians.  It features a central pocket "
"for a large plate, and near complete coverage in fragmentation resistant "
"materials.  Aside from the plate, it offers insufficient protection from "
"ballistic threats."
msgstr ""
"一件由凯夫拉、芳纶和泡沫衬垫构成的厚重防护夹克，供排爆技术员使用。它具有一个用于插入大型防护板的口袋，并几乎完全覆盖防破片材料。除了防护板之外，它对子弹的防"
"护不足。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "EOD jacket"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid "Pocket for a huge armor plate."
msgstr "巨型装甲板口袋"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid_plural "tactical EOD jackets"
msgstr[0] "战术拆弹防护夹克"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid ""
"An armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for use "
"by explosive ordnance disposal technicians in 'non-permissive environments'.  "
"It is lighter than normal EOD armor to allow for wearing a plate carrier "
"beneath it.  It features two pockets in the arms covering the deltoids for "
"additional optional protection."
msgstr ""
"一件由凯夫拉、芳纶和泡沫衬垫构成的防护夹克，供排爆技术员在“非许可环境”中使用。与普通EOD拆弹部队盔甲防护服相比，它更轻便，可以在里面穿防弹衣。它在袖子上"
"覆盖三角肌的位置有两个口袋，用于提供额外的可选保护。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid "Pockets for deltoid armor plates."
msgstr "肩部装甲板口袋"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "EOD fragmentation plate"
msgid_plural "EOD fragmentation plates"
msgstr[0] "EOD 碎片化防護板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "EOD fragmentation plate"
msgid ""
"A polygonal fragmentation plate with a slightly concave profile, made of thin "
"layers of steel, UHMW polyethylene, foam, and Kevlar.  Though certified to "
"provide protection from fragmentation, it will not provide much protection "
"from firearms.  This is intended to be inserted into an EOD suit, and can't "
"be worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"具有微凹輪廓的多邊形碎片化防護板，由薄層鋼、超高分子量聚乙烯、泡沫和克維拉製成。雖然經過認證可以提供防碎片保護，但它無法提供太多針對槍支的保護。它設計成插入"
"爆炸物處理（EOD，Explosive Ordnance Disposal）套裝中，不能單獨穿戴。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ESAPI ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "ESAPI ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "ESAPI ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of ceramic. "
" Its inner surface is coated with UHMW polyethylene and is labeled \"TOP\", "
"while the outer surface is labeled \"STRIKE FACE\".  This is intended to be "
"worn in a ballistic vest, and can withstand several high-energy rifle rounds "
"before breaking."
msgstr ""
"具有微凹輪廓的多邊形防彈板，由陶瓷製成。其內表面塗有超高分子量聚乙烯並標記為「頂部」，而外表面標記為「打擊面」。它設計成放在防彈背心中，並且可以在破裂前承受"
"幾發高動能步槍子彈。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soft stab panel"
msgid_plural "soft stab panels"
msgstr[0] "軟性防刺防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "soft stab panel"
msgid ""
"A soft armor insert designed to protect against stab wounds.  While it's not "
"great protection, it incurs no additional encumbrance.  This is intended to "
"be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr "一个柔软的防弹背心插板，用来防刺伤。虽然防护称不上优秀，但同时也不会增加多少累赘。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，无法直接穿着。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "steel ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "steel ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "鋼製防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A concave ballistic plate made of hard steel, designed to stop small-caliber "
"rounds.  \"NIJ III A PROTECTION\" is etched into the back of the plate.  This "
"is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its "
"own."
msgstr "一块带凹面的硬质钢防弹板，用来阻挡小口径子弹。插板背面蚀刻着\"NIJ III A级防护\"的字样。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，无法直接穿着。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "heavy steel ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "heavy steel ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "重型鋼製防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "heavy steel ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A heavy concave ballistic plate made of tempered steel, designed to stop "
"small-caliber rounds.  \"NIJ III PROTECTION\" is etched into the back of the "
"plate.  This is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be "
"worn on its own."
msgstr "一块沉重的带凹面的回火碳钢防弹板，用来阻挡小口径子弹。插板背面蚀刻着\"NIJ III 级防护\"的字样。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，无法直接穿着。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scrap ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "scrap ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "廢料 ESAPI 防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "scrap ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"A flat piece of salvaged steel, crudely cut and bent into the shape of an "
"ESAPI ballistic plate.  It's wrapped in rags to cover the sharp edges.  "
"Better than nothing, but it's heavier than the real thing, and not very "
"strong.  This is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be "
"worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"一塊回收的扁平廢鋼，經過粗糙切割並彎曲成增強型輕武器防護插件（ESAPI，Enhanced Small Arms Protective "
"Insert）防彈板的形狀。它用碎布包覆著鋒利的邊緣。總比沒有好，但它比真正的防彈板重，而且不是很堅固。它設計成插入防彈背心中，不能單獨穿戴。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mild ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "mild ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板（低碳鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "mild ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"Mild steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more professionally "
"done than scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用低碳鋼鍛造成防彈板。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "medium ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "medium ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板（中碳鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "medium ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"Medium steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more professionally "
"done than scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用中碳鋼鍛造成防彈板。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "high ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "high ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板（高碳鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "high ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"High steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more professionally "
"done than most scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用高碳鋼鍛造成防彈板。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hard ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "hard ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板（硬化鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "hard ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"Hardened steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more "
"professionally done than most scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of "
"jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用硬化鋼鍛造成防彈板。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "tempered ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "tempered ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESAPI 防彈板（回火鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "tempered ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"Tempered steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more "
"professionally done than most scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of "
"jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用回火鋼鍛造成防彈板。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "deltoid ballistic plates"
msgid_plural "deltoid ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "三角防弹板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "deltoid ballistic plates"
msgid ""
"A pair of NIJ Level III ballistic plates with a concave profile, made of UHMW "
"polyethylene.  \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  These plates "
"are designed to be worn in the shoulder pockets of suitable plate carriers or "
"combat shirts, and can resist several high-energy rifle rounds before "
"breaking.  Deltoid plates such as these are very infrequently worn due to "
"their marginal utility in improving survivability."
msgstr ""
"一对NIJ III级防弹板,具有凹面轮廓,由超高分子量聚乙烯制成。外表面印有\"STRIKE "
"FACE\"字样。这些防弹板设计用于在适合的防弹衣或战斗衬衫的肩部口袋中插入,可以在破裂之前抵抗多发步枪子弹。由于在提高生存能力方面的实用性有限,"
"这种防弹板很少被使用。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ESBI ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "ESBI ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "ESBI 防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "ESBI ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of ceramic. "
" \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  This is designed to be "
"worn in the sides of a plate carrier, and can withstand several high-energy "
"rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr "具有微凹輪廓的多邊形防彈板，由陶瓷製成。其外表面上印有「打擊面」字樣。它被設計成放入在裝甲板載體的側面，並且可以在破裂之前承受幾發高動能步槍子彈。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scrap ESBI plate"
msgid_plural "scrap ESBI plates"
msgstr[0] "廢料 ESBI 防彈板"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "scrap ESBI plate"
msgid ""
"A flat piece of salvaged steel, crudely cut and bent into the shape of an "
"ESBI ballistic plate.  It's wrapped in rags to cover the sharp edges.  Better "
"than nothing, but it's heavy, and not very strong.  This is intended to be "
"inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"一塊回收的扁平廢鋼，經過粗糙切割並彎曲成增強型側彈道插件（ESBI，Enhanced Side Ballistic "
"Insert）防彈板的形狀。它用碎布包覆著鋒利的邊緣。總比沒有好，但它比真正的防彈板重，而且不是很堅固。它設計成插入防彈背心中，不能單獨穿戴。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mild ESBI plate"
msgid_plural "mild ESBI plates"
msgstr[0] "ESBI 防彈板（低碳鋼）"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "mild ESBI plate"
msgid ""
"A hexagonal piece of mild steel forged into a side plate and padded with "
"synthetic fabric.  While it is more professionally done than scrap plates, it "
"still has a fair amount of jerry-rigging."
msgstr "用低碳鋼鍛造的六角形側向防彈板，並有合成纖維內襯。雖然它比廢料防彈板做得更專業，但它仍然有相當多偷工減料的痕跡。"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "medium ESBI plate"
msgid_plural "medium ESBI plates"
