#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
#. ~ Description of variant "The Complete Guide to Pitching" of item "The
#. Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid ""
"A detailed guide for baseball pitchers that combines time-tested techniques "
"and information mixed with a common sense approach to pitching."
msgstr "一本關於棒球投手的詳盡指導。教你如何使用各種技巧組合來進行投球。"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "The Ultimate Guide to Knife Throwing"
msgid_plural "copies of The Ultimate Guide to Knife Throwing"
msgstr[0] "飞刀终极指南"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of variant "The Ultimate Guide to Knife Throwing" of item
#. "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "A precise handbook for someone who wants to win a throwing tournament."
msgstr "一本口袋书，为那些想赢得投掷锦标赛的人所编写。"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "Guide to Knife & Ax Throwing"
msgid_plural "copies of Guide to Knife & Ax Throwing"
msgstr[0] "刀&斧投掷指南"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Guide to Knife & Ax Throwing" of item "The
#. Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid ""
"A small, simple guide on how to throw a projectile, with different "
"techniques, guides, and tricks."
msgstr "一本袖珍，简单的指南书，告诉你如何通过不同的技巧、手法来抛出你的暗器。"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "Knife & Tomahawk Throwing: The Art of the Experts"
msgid_plural "copies of Knife & Tomahawk Throwing: The Art of the Experts"
msgstr[0] "飞刀与战斧：投掷的艺术"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Knife & Tomahawk Throwing: The Art of the
#. Experts" of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid ""
"A small book on the long history of projectile throwing and the people "
"building the sport.  It serves as a guide for someone who wants to get into "
"it, with useful drills and diagrams."
msgstr "一本小书，介绍投掷物的漫长历史，以及人们是如何将它变成一项运动的。它也可以作为学习投掷的指南书，附有实用的练习和丰富的图画说明。"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "The Science of Baseball"
msgid_plural "copies of The Science of Baseball"
msgstr[0] "棒球科学"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of variant "The Science of Baseball" of item "The Complete
#. Guide to Pitching"
msgid ""
"The author and several experts cover topics like what makes a ball break, "
"bounce, and fly; how material science and physics work together to make the "
"bat function; how hitters use physics, geometry, and force to connect; "
"baseball injuries; and much more."
msgstr "作者和一些专家探讨什么使棒球停止、弹起或击飞；材料科学与物理学如何解释球棒的击球效果；击球手如何运用物理学、几何学与连接力；棒球的受伤；以及其他许多话题。"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid "The Complete Knife Throwing Guide"
msgid_plural "copies of The Complete Knife Throwing Guide"
msgstr[0] "飞刀投掷完全指南"

#: data/json/items/book/throw.json
#. ~ Description of variant "The Complete Knife Throwing Guide" of item "The
#. Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid ""
"A tiny, though still comprehensive manual of knife throwing from experienced "
"knifemaker."
msgstr "一关于飞刀投掷的手册，很薄但写得很详尽，由有经验的飞刀投掷者编写。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "How to Trap Anything"
msgid_plural "copies of How to Trap Anything"
msgstr[0] "《來做陷阱》"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "How to Trap Anything"
msgid "A worn manual that describes how to set and disarm a wide variety of traps."
msgstr "手冊中介紹了如何設置和解除各式各樣的陷阱。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Trapper's Life"
msgid_plural "issues of Trapper's Life"
msgstr[0] "《陷阱生活》"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "Trapper's Life"
msgid ""
"An in-depth magazine about trapping game.  There are lots of articles and "
"diagrams that explain simple trap designs."
msgstr "一本深度的陷阱比賽雜誌。有很多的文章和圖表， 講解簡單的陷阱設計。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Modern Trapper"
msgid_plural "copies of The Modern Trapper"
msgstr[0] "《現代陷阱製作》"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "The Modern Trapper"
msgid "An extensive volume that details numerous methods of trapping game."
msgstr "一本充滿詳盡內容的書， 內容說明了各種製作陷阱的方法。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations"
msgid_plural "copies of FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations"
msgstr[0] "陆军手册20-32：地雷与反地雷"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations"
msgid ""
"A hefty military field manual about mine-warfare principles, the mechanics of "
"different types of mines/IED's, and countermine operations."
msgstr "一本沉重的军事战地手册，讲述了地雷战中的原则、不同类型的地雷和简易爆炸装置的机械原理，以及应对地雷的方法。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Booby Traps, IEDs, Mines and You: A Primer"
msgid_plural "copies of Booby Traps, IEDs, Mines and You: A Primer"
msgstr[0] "诡雷、地雷、简易爆炸物与你"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "Booby Traps, IEDs, Mines and You: A Primer"
msgid ""
"A light military field manual about booby traps, IEDs, mines and how to avoid "
"being blown up by them."
msgstr "一本简明军用野战手册，讲解诱饵陷阱、临时爆炸物（IED）、地雷以及你应该如何安全地与它们相处。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ The spelling is intentionally archaic, as this form is commonly used in
#. the titles of books.
msgid "The Compleat Trapper"
msgid_plural "copies of The Compleat Trapper"
msgstr[0] "《完全陷阱手冊》"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "The Compleat Trapper"
msgid ""
"An in-depth book about trapping game animals, covering methods both modern "
"and ancient."
msgstr "一本深入教導誘捕動物的書籍， 包含了古今中外的各種方法。"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Trapper's Companion"
msgid_plural "copies of The Trapper's Companion"
msgstr[0] "《陷捕者良伴》"

#: data/json/items/book/traps.json
#. ~ Description of "The Trapper's Companion"
msgid ""
"A folksy guide to trapping wild game using time-tested methods.  A bit "
"in-depth for the beginner, it can provide a wealth of information to a "
"knowledgeable trapper."
msgstr "經過時間歷練的一本平易近人的誘捕指南。對初學者有點深， 但是它可以提供關於陷阱的豐富知識。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "Boxing Monthly"
msgid_plural "issues of Boxing Monthly"
msgstr[0] "《鬥陣月刊》"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of "Boxing Monthly"
#. ~ Description of variant "Boxing Monthly" of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"An exciting monthly magazine about boxing.  There are lots of large, colorful "
"photos of pugilistic exploits."
msgstr "一本血脈僨張的拳擊月刊。裡面刊載了相當大量關於拳擊手戰果的相片。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "Feral Fighting"
msgid_plural "copies of Feral Fighting"
msgstr[0] "野性格斗"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Feral Fighting" of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"A brutal book about using dirty tricks to disrupt your enemies, and using "
"this advantage to knockout or even kill them."
msgstr "一本野蛮的格斗书，教你如何用下三滥的招数干扰你的对手，进而利用优势击倒、甚至杀掉你的对手。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "Stand And Deliver"
msgid_plural "copies of Stand And Deliver"
msgstr[0] "架势与出击"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Stand And Deliver" of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"\"A Street Warrior's Guide To Tactical Combat Stances\", this book provides "
"plenty of information about how stance changes your movement, and how to use "
"each of them with maximum effect."
msgstr "\"一本街头格斗的架势指南书\"，这本书提供了许多信息，讲解移动与架势的关系，以及怎样才能将架势作用最大发挥。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "First Strike: End a Fight in Ten Seconds or Less!"
msgid_plural "copies of First Strike: End a Fight in Ten Seconds or Less!"
msgstr[0] "一击致胜：10秒内结束战斗"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "First Strike: End a Fight in Ten Seconds or
#. Less!" of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"Despite having a pretty odd name, this book provides a lot of information "
"about fighting techniques, and different tactics and skills you need to "
"obtain to use them properly."
msgstr "虽然名字挺奇葩，但这本书还算有些关于战斗的干货，以及要想正确用出这些技巧你所需的战术和技能。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "Street Lethal: Unarmed Urban Combat"
msgid_plural "copies of Street Lethal: Unarmed Urban Combat"
msgstr[0] "致命街头：徒手城市格斗"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Street Lethal: Unarmed Urban Combat" of item
#. "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"This book contains lot of images showing how to use different attacks in "
"close quarters, but someone has hand-written \"lame\" on the cover."
msgstr "这本书内含许多图片，展示了近身战时可以运用的一系列攻击，但有人在封面上手写了一行\"弱爆了\"。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid "Nuclear Strike!"
msgid_plural "copies of Nuclear Strike!"
msgstr[0] "核拳杀物！"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Nuclear Strike!" of item "Boxing Monthly"
msgid ""
"\"Turn your fist into a weapon of mass destruction!\"  This book details "
"different training programs to train your body overall and to temper your "
"hands and nerves into unstoppable forces."
msgstr "\"把你的拳头练成大规模杀伤性武器！\" 本书详细介绍了多种身体训练计划，将你的手和神经锻炼成不可阻挡的力量。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid_plural "copies of 101 Wrestling Moves"
msgstr[0] "《摔角招式 101》"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of "101 Wrestling Moves"
#. ~ Description of variant "101 Wrestling Moves" of item "101 Wrestling
#. Moves"
msgid ""
"It seems to be a wrestling manual, poorly photocopied and released on "
"spiral-bound paper.  Still, there are lots of useful tips for unarmed combat."
msgstr "這似乎是一個摔跤手冊，品質不良的照片裝訂在扭曲的紙張上。不過，有很多有用的徒手格鬥技巧。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "Turn Your Fists Into Sledgehammers!"
msgid_plural "copies of Turn Your Fists Into Sledgehammers!"
msgstr[0] "一拳八十！八十！"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Turn Your Fists Into Sledgehammers!" of item "101
#. Wrestling Moves"
msgid ""
"A detailed explanation of how to train your hands, arms and fists to crush "
"the heads of your opponents, with lot of photos and instructions."
msgstr "用手、臂和拳头打爆对手脑袋的详细教学，附有大量照片和说明。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "Unleash Hell"
msgid_plural "copies of Unleash Hell"
msgstr[0] "恶魔格斗"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Unleash Hell" of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid ""
"A book with a creepy image of death with a scythe on the cover, it guides the "
"user on different attacks that can be combined to overwhelm and destroy your "
"enemy in seconds."
msgstr ""
"一本封面有恐怖带大镰刀的死神形象的书，教你各种不同的攻击，可以组合起来发挥出压到行的效果，在几秒钟内打倒敌人。\n"
"－\"我将🥜👿\""

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "Knockout: The Ultimate Guide to Sucker Punching"
msgid_plural "copies of Knockout: The Ultimate Guide to Sucker Punching"
msgstr[0] "烂人拳击终极指南"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Knockout: The Ultimate Guide to Sucker Punching"
#. of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid ""
"This book shows how to use sucker punches - fast and unexpected attacks - to "
"take advantage in a street fight.  Not as useful as before, but it still "
"contains solid information about certain skills and trainings."
msgstr ""
"这本书介绍街头混混常用的拳法 － 用快速且出人意料的攻击占据优势。可能现在没有街溜子给你打了，但其中关于某些技能训练的内容还挺靠谱的。\n"
"\"摆烂拳法\""

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "Killer Instinct: Unarmed Combat for Street Survival"
msgid_plural "copies of Killer Instinct: Unarmed Combat for Street Survival"
msgstr[0] "杀手本能：安全经历一场街头徒手格斗"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Killer Instinct: Unarmed Combat for Street
#. Survival" of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid ""
"A shabby book about possible street dangers the author met in his long life, "
"ways to deal with them, and the skill set that such situations require."
msgstr "这本旧书记录了作者在他一生中经历过的街头威胁，如何进行相应的应对，以及需要你有一些什么能力。"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid "The Bigger They Are, The Harder They Fall"
msgid_plural "copies of The Bigger They Are, The Harder They Fall"
msgstr[0] "块头越大摔得越重"

#: data/json/items/book/unarmed.json
#. ~ Description of variant "The Bigger They Are, The Harder They Fall" of
#. item "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid ""
"This book explains simple rules that you need to rely on to fight an enemy of "
"different constitution, with techniques and tactics."
msgstr "这本书解释了你在不同情况下与敌人战斗时需要注意的规则，并提供了技巧和战术。"

#: data/json/items/book/videos.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "abstract video"
msgid_plural "abstract videos"
msgstr[0] "虚拟视频"

#: data/json/items/book/videos.json
#. ~ Description of "abstract video"
msgid "An abstract video file, implemented as a book."
msgstr "一个虚拟的视频文件，实现方式与书籍相同。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "children's book"
msgid_plural "children's books"
msgstr[0] "《兒童讀物》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "children's book"
msgid ""
"A little book for little readers.  The colorful cartoon characters and sweet "
"stories contained herein belong to a different time, before the dead walked "
"and the world moved on."
msgstr "一本給小朋友的小書。有著豐富色彩的卡通角色與甜蜜的故事， 顯然不是這個時間點的產物。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "book of fairy tales"
msgid_plural "books of fairy tales"
msgstr[0] "《童話故事集》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"An amusing collection of folklore featuring the usual cast of fairies, "
"goblins, and trolls."
msgstr "一本趣味民間故事集， 通常由小仙子、哥布林和巨魔主演。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This fairy tale is about a wolf who eats so much salted meat she becomes "
"trapped in the butcher's cellar."
msgstr "这个童话故事讲的是一只狼吃了太多咸肉，最终被困在屠夫的地窖里。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"In this traditional story of beastly intrigue, a clever fox convinces an "
"elderly lion to kill a derogatory wolf."
msgstr "在这个传统童话故事中，一只狡猾的狐狸说服一只年长的狮子杀死一只恶毒的狼。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "An illustrated fairy tale book about a conversation between a mouse and a cat."
msgstr "这是一本有插图的童话书，讲述的是老鼠和猫之间的对话。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This illustrated fairy tale relates how a city mouse did visit his cousin in "
"the country, and how each regarded the other's quality of life."
msgstr "这个童话小说讲述了一只城市老鼠拜访他在乡下的表亲的，以及他们如何看待对方的生活质量的故事。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "A fable in which the jackal wins the day via clever foolishness."
msgstr "一个童话寓言故事，讲述了一只豺狼如何用自身聪明的愚蠢赢得了胜利。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"A slave mistakenly wanders into a lion's den - thus begins a fable which "
"demonstrates mutual dependence regardless of size or status."
msgstr "一个奴隶误打误撞闯进了狮子的巢穴——由此而展开一段寓言故事，其寓意为不论两者大小或地位如何，都有相互依赖的需要。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"An amusing collection of stories featuring \"Goldilocks and The Three Bears\" "
"on the cover."
msgstr "一本有趣的童话故事集，封面上写着《金姑娘和三只小熊》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"A well illustrated fairy tale about a war between the birds and the beasts, "
"with particulars on the wartime conduct and eventual fate of the bat."
msgstr "这是一本有着不错插图的童话故事书，讲述了鸟类和野兽之间的战争，着重描绘蝙蝠在战争之中的行为和最终命运。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This book, titled \"The Rattlesnake's Vengeance\" is a collection of Cherokee "
"myths and legends.  \"285D\" is hand-written in pencil on the title page."
msgstr "这本书名为《响尾蛇的复仇》，是切诺基族神话和传说的故事集。标题页上用铅笔手写了\"285D\"。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "This fairy tale book is a regional variant of \"Jack and the Beanstalk.\""
msgstr "这本童话书中讲述了一个《杰克和豌豆》故事的本地变体。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This fairy tale book is titled \"Little Red Cap.\"  It details a red-cloaked "
"child's various encounters with talking wolves."
msgstr "这本童话书的标题是《小红帽》。它描述了一个穿红斗篷的小女孩与一只会说话的大灰狼的各种遭遇。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"A collection of ghost stories warning about the dangers of stealing from the "
"dead."
msgstr "一本关于鬼怪的童话故事集，警告读者从死者身上偷东西的危险。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"An Irish fairy tale in which a Celtic poet marries a princess who has been "
"cursed with the head of a pig."
msgstr "一个爱尔兰童话故事，讲述了一个凯尔特诗人娶了一个被诅咒长成猪头的公主。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"A book of Italian fairy tales translated into English.  The cover features an "
"orange fairy juggling a lemon, a lime, and a tangerine."
msgstr "一本將義大利童話的英譯本。封面上有一隻柳橙仙子正在用檸檬、萊姆、橘子雜耍。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "A book of fables about people who change into birds."
msgstr "一本关于变成鸟的人的童话书。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This compendium of amusing folk tales about the devil is titled \"Hell's "
"Kettle: Legends of the Devil.\""
msgstr "一本关于魔鬼的有趣的民间故事集录，标题为《地狱的水壶：魔鬼的传说》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This charming book of Swedish fables is titled \"The Glass Mountain and the "
"Princess.\""
msgstr "一本迷人的瑞典童话书，标题为《玻璃山和公主》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"A collection of fairy tale stories warning against the consequences of "
"extreme greed."
msgstr "一本童话故事集，警告了读者过度贪婪的下场。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This fable book is titled \"The Rabbit Herd.\"  Inside are woodcut "
"illustrations of a peasant boy playing his flute for a mob of mischievous "
"hares."
msgstr "这本寓言书的题目是《野兔群》。书中画着一幅农家男孩为一群淘气的野兔吹长笛的木版画插图。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "This book is titled \"The Thieving Pot: Folktales of the Arab World.\""
msgstr "一本标题为《偷东西的罐子：阿拉伯世界的民间故事》的故事书。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "A book of legends collected by Traveller Johnny Cassidy in the 1960s."
msgstr "一本童话故事集，由乔尼·卡西迪于1960年代收集。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "A book by the Brothers Grimm, titled \"Eve's Unequal Children.\""
msgstr "一本格林兄弟的童话书，书名为《夏娃的孩子们》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "This book of fables expands upon the legend of the Seven Sleepers of Ephesus."
msgstr "这本童话书基于艾弗所之七圣童的传说改编扩写而成。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"In this fairy tale, a strong man frightens an ogre by squeezing water out of "
"a stone."
msgstr "在这个童话故事中，一个强壮的小裁缝把石头里的水挤出来吓唬巨人。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid "This book of rustic folk tales bears the title \"How to Shout Down the Devil.\""
msgstr "这本乡村民间故事书的标题为《如何大叫来吓跑魔鬼》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"The title of this book is \"Village Folk-tales of Ceylon.\"  It includes "
"fables about logical errors and foolish misjudgments of the Kadambawa men."
msgstr "这本书的标题是《锡兰的乡村民间故事》。它里面包含了关于斯里兰卡的卡达姆巴瓦人的逻辑错误和愚蠢误判的童话故事。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"This book of folk tales is titled \"The Girl with the Ugly Name, and Other "
"Stories.\""
msgstr "这本民间故事书的标题是《一个有丑陋名字的女孩，和其他故事》。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Snippet of item "book of fairy tales"
msgid ""
"Titled \"The Fleeing Pancake\", this collection of silly folk tales is "
"suitable for small children."
msgstr "标题为《逃走的松饼》的民间童话故事集，适合讲给小孩子听。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Adorkable Girl"
msgid_plural "copies of The Adorkable Girl"
msgstr[0] "呆萌女孩"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "The Adorkable Girl"
msgid ""
"When a therapist's daughter transfers to a new school, she decides to change "
"her personality type.  As her social life begins to blossom, can she maintain "
"a healthy boundary between her home life and her public persona?"
msgstr "当心理医生的女儿转到新学校时，她决定改变自己的性格类型。当她的社交生活开始蓬勃发展时，她能否继续保持家庭生活和公众形象之间的健康界限呢？"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Becoming Jackson"
msgid_plural "copies of Becoming Jackson"
msgstr[0] "成为杰克逊"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Becoming Jackson"
msgid ""
"When Jackson gains the mystical talent to alter his appearance on command, "
"will he be able to recognize himself in his own mirror?"
msgstr "当杰克逊获得能够改变自身外貌的神秘天赋时，他还能在镜子中继续认出自己吗？"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Nothing Burned"
msgid_plural "copies of Nothing Burned"
msgstr[0] "无人烧伤"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Nothing Burned"
msgid ""
"A teenage influencer becomes fast friends with someone who may or may not be "
"an actual demon."
msgstr "一位青年意见领袖交到了一个新密友。这个朋友很可能（是/不是）一只真正的恶魔。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "High and Low"
msgid_plural "copies of High and Low"
msgstr[0] "天国与地狱"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "High and Low"
msgid ""
"In this work of adolescent fiction, a young Gemini discovers that the "
"astrology section of his small town newspaper is eerily preminiscent.  His "
"efforts to uncover the oracle reveal more than the stars could have predicted."
msgstr "在这本青少年小说中，一位双子座的年轻人发现，他小镇的报纸上的占星学部分充满了可怕的预兆。他努力发掘其中的神启，结果揭开的真相比观星所能预测还要可怕得多。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Fire When You See My Eyes"
msgid_plural "copies of Fire When You See My Eyes"
msgstr[0] "当你看到我眼中的火焰"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Fire When You See My Eyes"
msgid ""
"In a cataclysmic future, advanced technology gives parents access to video "
"footage of every moment of their teenage children's lives."
msgstr "故事发生在翻天覆地的未来，高度发达的科技让父母可以随时随地通过视频监控他们叛逆期孩子的生活。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Peanut Butter Bruised"
msgid_plural "copies of Peanut Butter Bruised"
msgstr[0] "《花生醬製品》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Peanut Butter Bruised"
msgid ""
"In this work of young adult fiction, a woman raised on food stamps falls in "
"love with a young cook.  More importantly, she falls in love with the idea of "
"becoming a professional chef."
msgstr "在这部青年小说中，一位靠食品券长大的女人爱上了一位年轻的厨师。更重要的是，她爱上了成为一名专业厨师的想法。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Ready When You Are"
msgid_plural "copies of Ready When You Are"
msgstr[0] "《當你準備好》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Ready When You Are"
msgid ""
"When three teenage girls ditch class to drive cross-country together, they "
"get a strong dose of life lessons on the road.  This work of young adult "
"fiction explores how friendships evolve in early adulthood."
msgstr "三个十几岁的少女们一起逃课去开车巡游全国，她们在一路上被生活上了不少课。这份青年小说深入探讨了友谊如何是在青少年时期发生演变的。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Study of a Boy"
msgid_plural "copies of Study of a Boy"
msgstr[0] "《男孩觀察記》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Study of a Boy"
msgid ""
"A high school sophomore's personal journal is stolen and then leaked on "
"social media.  When it goes viral, he is forced to contend with simultaneous "
"fame and betrayal."
msgstr "一个高二学生的个人日记被偷，然后被泄露到社交媒体上。当它走红时，他被迫同时与名声和背叛作斗争。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Summer Variables"
msgid_plural "copies of Summer Variables"
msgstr[0] "夏季变量"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Summer Variables"
msgid ""
"In this book written primarily for young adults, a woman's modest summer "
"internship results in an incredible discovery that attracts the attention of "
"unsavory elements."
msgstr "在这本主要为年轻人写的书中，一位少女在参加一次不太重要的暑期实习时有了一次令人难以置信的发现，吸引了一些不良分子的注意。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ ISBN 9780385755887
#. ~ Item name
msgid "In a Dark Place"
msgid_plural "copies of In a Dark Place"
msgstr[0] "《黑暗之地》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ ISBN 9780385755887
#. ~ Description of "In a Dark Place"
msgid ""
"Markia dreams about the future.  Theo longs for the past.  Together can they "
"find a way to live in the now?"
msgstr "马基亚梦想着未来。西奥渴望着过去。他们能一起找到一种生活在当下的方式吗？"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ ISBN 9780385755924
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Betrayal Takes Two"
msgid_plural "copies of Betrayal Takes Two"
msgstr[0] "《狼狽為奸》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ ISBN 9780385755924
#. ~ Description of "Betrayal Takes Two"
msgid ""
"A hard cover book for older teens.  The two main characters pull a cruel "
"prank on their classmates, and are brought together both by their frantic "
"efforts to avoid being caught and their shared sense of guilt."
msgstr "一部专为大一点的青少年编写的精装小说。书中讲述了两个主角对他们的同学做恶作剧，以及为了避免被抓所做出的疯狂闹剧和他们共同的负罪感让他们成为挚友的故事。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "coming of age novel"
msgid_plural "coming of age novels"
msgstr[0] "《成長小說》"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "coming of age novel"
msgid ""
"A classic tale about growing up, portraying one young man's funny and "
"poignant experiences with life, love, and sex."
msgstr "一本關於成長的經典寓言故事， 描述一位年輕男子在生活、愛、和性的有趣和淒美的經驗。"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Pantheon: The Story of an Iranian Youth"
msgid_plural "copies of Pantheon: The Story of an Iranian Youth"
msgstr[0] "万神殿：一个伊朗青年的故事"

#: data/json/items/book/young.json
#. ~ Description of "Pantheon: The Story of an Iranian Youth"
msgid ""
"A hard cover graphic novel about a young girl living in Iran during the "
"1980's, seeing the world change around her as Iraq invaded her country."
msgstr "一部精装图画小说，内容是关于1980年代一个生活在伊朗的年轻女孩，在国家受到伊拉克入侵时，对周遭世界变迁的见闻。"

