#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&To: monica evers\n"
"Subject: Interest in property\n"
"\n"
"Hello, Monica!  I got your information from Tony because I'm in talks to buy "
"one of your properties out of town.  I have a small development firm ready to "
"break ground, but I was wondering if you had any details on radioactive "
"materials or other geology in the area?  I know this is a strange question "
"but certain things will prevent me from building at all.\n"
"\n"
"Also, given the recent developments in the area since the listing, would it "
"be possible to reduce the price at all?  I asked Tony but he said he would "
"have to run it by you.  Thank you."
msgstr ""
"&发往：莫妮卡•埃弗斯\n"
"主题：对房产感兴趣\n"
"\n"
"你好，莫妮卡！我从托尼那里得到了你的信息，因为我想要购买你在城外的一处房产。我有一个小型开发公司准备破土动工，但我想知道你是否有关于该地区放射性物质或其他地"
"质信息的任何细节？我知道这是个奇怪的问题，但某些东西会让我根本无法建造。\n"
"\n"
"另外，鉴于该地区自上市以来最近的发展情况，是否有可能降低价格？我问过托尼，但他说必须由你来决定。谢谢你。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&From: monica evers\n"
"Subject: RE: Interest in property\n"
"\n"
"Thanks for reaching out!  I'm glad Tony gave you my details because that bit "
"of land has been on my mind for a long time.  He's an amazing broker.  It's "
"hard to get attention on a lot this size and this far out of town unless "
"there's oil underneath, but Tony knows everyone!  Since I haven't had a buyer "
"in a while, I'm willing to come down maybe another thousand but that's it.\n"
"\n"
"I apologize, but I'm afraid I don't have any information on radiation or "
"magnetism in the area, only basic topographical data the survey team "
"collected after I first bought the property, which I can definitely send, if "
"you like.  Thank you again for your interest!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：莫妮卡•埃弗斯\n"
"主题：回复：对房产感兴趣\n"
"\n"
"谢谢你的联系！我很高兴托尼给了你我的详细资料，那块地已经让我挂念很长一段时间了，他是一个了不起的经纪人。除非下面有石油，否则这么大的一块地很难引起人们注意，"
"但托尼认识所有人。由于我已经有一段时间没有买家了，我愿意再降1000美刀，但仅此而已。\n"
"\n"
"我很抱歉，但我恐怕没有任何关于该地区的辐射或磁力的信息，只有我第一次买下该土地后调查小组收集的基本地形数据，如果你愿意，我一定可以寄给你。再次感谢你的关注！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&From: Ryan\n"
"Subject: RE: Airport Facility\n"
"\n"
"yes its possible.  most airports have tunnels underneath for staff and others "
"to move around.  obviously ordinary people cant go in and most airports are "
"just normal but there are definitely some international hubs of travel with "
"hidden chambers in them and some even with tunnels out to the surrounding "
"area.  so elites dont have to go anywhere else to do their work and risk "
"being seen.  they have to be staffed by spies or people who dont know whats "
"really going on."
msgstr ""
"&来自：瑞安\n"
"主题：回复：机场设施\n"
"\n"
"是的，这是有可能的。大多数机场下面都有隧道，供工作人员和其他人活动。但显然，普通人不能进去。大多数机场只是普通的，但肯定有一些国际旅行中心，里面有隐藏的房间"
"，有些甚至有隧道通往周围地区。原本是为了让精英们不用冒着被人看到的风险去其他地区工作，只有贴身间谍或者不知情的人能进入那里。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&To: Ryan\n"
"Subject: RE: RE: Airport Facility\n"
"\n"
"He only goes to the airport and nowhere else.  I think he has to be one of "
"the people running it.  I remember bragg_eagle saying there were managers in "
"Denver who would spend time where normal employees couldn't go and I don't "
"see ANYONE else going in there.  He dresses like a construction worker or "
"something.  It's not like anything I've ever seen at an airport."
msgstr ""
"&发往：瑞安\n"
"主题：回复：回复：机场设施\n"
"\n"
"他只可能去机场，不会去别的地方。我想他一定是管理员之一。我记得\"布拉格_鹰\"说在丹佛有一些经理，他们会在普通员工不能去的地方待着，而且我从没有看到*"
"任何*其他人进去那里。他穿得像个建筑工人之类的，这和我在机场看到的情况不一样。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&To: Ryan\n"
"Subject: RE: RE: RE: Airport Facility\n"
"\n"
"Yeah I deleted it, don't worry.  Look, this is what he looks like.\n"
"\n"
"ATTACHMENTS: MVI 0022.mov"
msgstr ""
"&发往：瑞安\n"
"主题：回复：回复：回复：机场设施\n"
"\n"
"没错，我已经把它删了，不过别担心。看，这是它的长相。\n"
"\n"
"附件：MVI 0022.mov"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"WARNING!  ERROR B231; UNABLE TO CONNECT TO MESSAGING SERVER.\n"
" CONTACT INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY DEPARTMENT IMMEDIATELY!"
msgstr ""
"&警告！错误 B231；无法连接到消息服务器。\n"
"请立即联系信息技术部门！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Select the document you would like to view."
msgstr "选择你想要查看的文档。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "everything.txt"
msgstr "所有事情.txt"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "robert williamson.txt"
msgstr "罗伯特•威廉姆森.txt"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "shopping list.txt"
msgstr "购物清单.txt"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "MVI 0022.mov"
msgstr "MVI 0022.mov"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Enigma code cracked by Turing -> modern encryption technology -> internet "
"sentience arises and gives birth to AI in Chinese lab using new forms of "
"computation, aka: BIO-TECHNOLOGY, human AND robotic components TOGETHER.  "
"State media announces as 'fusion technology'.  Bio-weapon escapes lab, OF "
"COURSE.  Self-replicating bio-technology = imminent replacement of humanity.  "
"US gov now ACTIVELY manufacturing cover-ups for escaped bio-weapon to "
"maintain peace.  Follows same pattern as Roswell, Trinity (what they told the "
"public), oil pollution coverup (in my opinion).  Recent New York 'mass "
"psychosis events' instigated by them as cover.  PAID ACTORS on speed dial but "
"the THREAT IS REAL.  They are buying time, but what is the play?"
msgstr ""
"图灵破解恩尼格玛密码机 -> 现代加密技术 -> "
"互联网感知产生，并在中国实验室使用新的计算形式诞生了人工智能，也就是：生物技术，人类和机器人的成分结合在一起。国内媒体将其称为为\"融合技术\""
"。然后生物武器逃脱了实验室，意料之中。自我复制的生物技术=即将取代人类。美国政府现在正*积极*"
"为逃脱的生物武器制造伪装以维持和平。与罗斯威尔飞碟坠毁事件、三位一体核试验（他们对公众是这么叫的）、石油污染的掩盖（在我看来）的模式相同。最近纽约的\""
"大规模精神病事件\"是由他们煽动的，作为掩护。*受雇者*在不停打电话，但*威胁依然在*。他们在争取时间，但是要唱什么戏？"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Gov assigns names based off numerological conversions of house numbers.  "
"Robert Williamson: 205 W Orchard Avenue.  Robert (78) + Williamson (127) = "
"205.  Despite the beautiful weather, he keeps the curtains closed and no one "
"has even visited yet.  And he's been here for more than two weeks!  I only "
"ever see him when he's coming or going from work.  I assume it's work, even "
"if the hours are strange sometimes.  Black car, out of state plates, looks "
"brand new.  Fed behavior, if you ask me… Is he actually going somewhere or "
"just trying to convince me he's legitimate?  Is he on the job when he leaves "
"or on the job when he's here?  Further investigation required."
msgstr ""
"政府根据门牌号的数字转换来分配名字。罗伯特•威廉姆森：205 W 果园大道。罗伯特(78) + 威廉姆森(127) = "
"205。尽管天气很好，他一直拉着窗帘，也从未有其他人来访。而他已经在这里待了两个多星期了！我只有在他上下班的时候才能看到他。我假设他是在这工作，虽然他的上下"
"班时间有时很异常。黑色的车，外州的车牌，看起来是全新的。如果你问我，我只能说看起来像美联储的员工……他是真的去什么地方工作？还是只是想让我相信他是合法的？他"
"是离开这里去工作，还是在这里工作？需要进一步调查。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Non-perishables, MREs, canned soup, dehydrated milk, oats/rice, lemon juice, "
"protein powder.  Ammo, in crates if possible - just ask Rachel at RFA?  Large "
"drums (HDPE), reusable containers, spare fuel can.  More novels and TV from "
"home.  Iodine, colloidal silver, gas mask and filters for fallout."
msgstr ""
"非易腐食物：MRE，罐头汤，脱水牛奶，燕麦/"
"大米，柠檬汁，蛋白粉。弹药，如果可能的话，装在板条箱里——去问问自由亚洲电台的的瑞秋？高密度聚乙烯大桶，可重复使用的容器，备用燃料罐。更多从家里搬来的的小说"
"和电视。碘酒、胶体银、防毒面具和滤芯，以备防放射性尘埃。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&A video file starts playing.  It's quite low resolution, very shaky, and the "
"sound is somewhat muffled as the cameraperson appears to be filming inside "
"from their car.  On screen a man is walking away from the camera towards a "
"nondescript white building with large windows.  The glare of the sunlight "
"makes it hard to tell but it looks like… an airport terminal!  The man is "
"very far away, wearing an orange safety vest and a hard hat, and he appears "
"to be carrying a laptop bag.  You hear the person behind the camera mutter, "
"\"I've only ever seen him come and go through that door.  No one else in the "
"entire time I've been watching…\"  The man walks straight into the building, "
"only looking back briefly as he swipes a keycard at the door and enters."
msgstr ""
"&一段视频文件开始播放。这段视频的分辨率很低，画面剧烈颤抖，而且声音有些低沉，因为摄影师似乎是在车内拍摄的。在屏幕上，一个男人正从镜头前走过，走向一栋有大窗"
"户的不知名白色建筑。强烈的阳光让人难以分辨，但它看起来像……机场航站楼！该男子离得很远，穿着一件橙色的安全背心，戴着一顶安全帽，似乎背着一个笔记本电脑包。你"
"听到摄像机后面的人嘀咕道：\"我只见过他从那扇门进来和出去。在我观察的这段时间里，没有其他人……\""
"该男子径直走进大楼，在门口刷了一张门卡后，只简短地回头看了一眼，就进去了。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Continue watching…"
msgstr "继续观看……"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The cameraperson sighs.  The view slowly zooms out for a few seconds, but "
"then suddenly jerks to the left.  \"Ay… hey, look at these motherfuckers!\"  "
"The camera zooms in on two teenagers next to a car in the parking lot.  "
"They're both laughing and shouting very loudly, almost seemingly intoxicated… "
" One kid takes a step back, then kicks in the taillight of the car.  The "
"other appears from around the other side of it, dragging their keys along it, "
"scratching up the paint.  The boy who was kicking begins violently punching "
"the window with his bare fist.  The cameraperson lets out an astonished gasp, "
"\"Like New York…\"  One punch, two punch, and with a third smash his arm goes "
"through the glass!  He stares at the other teenager and they both let out a "
"burst of laughter that lasts a little too long.  The cameraperson mutters a "
"concerned \"Uhhh…\" and sets the camera on the seat.  The recording abruptly "
"ends."
msgstr ""
"&摄像师叹了口气。视野慢慢放大了几秒钟，但随后突然向左抽动。\"哎……嘿，看看这些狗娘养的！\""
"镜头拉近到停车场一辆车旁的两个青少年身上。他们都在大笑，大声喊叫，似乎很陶醉……一个孩子退了一步，然后踢了一下汽车的尾灯。另一个人从车的另一侧出现，沿着车拖"
"着的钥匙，刮起了车漆。踢的那个男孩开始用他的赤裸的拳头猛烈地击打车窗。摄像师发出了惊讶的喘息声：\"就像纽约……\""
"一拳，两拳，随着第三拳的砸下，他的手臂打穿了玻璃！他盯着另一个少年，两人发出了一阵笑声，笑声持续的时间有点长。摄像师关切地嘀咕了一句\"呃……\""
"，然后把摄像机放在座位上。录像突然结束了。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_PREPPER_1_COMPUTER.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Error: 'open': command not found."
msgstr "错误：'查看'：命令未找到"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Shady Hills Corporation.\n"
" You are logged in as: Randolph VanBuren, Community Manager.\n"
"\n"
" WARNING!  ERROR A101; FAILURE DETECTED IN POWER SUPPLY.\n"
" RESERVE POWER ACTIVATED.  CONTACT INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY DEPARTMENT "
"IMMEDIATELY!"
msgstr ""
"&Shady Hills 疗养院。\n"
"当前登录身份：伦道夫·范布伦，社区管理员。\n"
"\n"
"警告！错误 A101；检测到电源故障。\n"
"备用电源已激活。请立即联系信息技术部！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Access Main Drives"
msgstr "访问主数据库"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RETURN TO DESKTOP"
msgstr "返回桌面"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Seriously!?"
msgstr "主题：认真的！？"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Noise complaint"
msgstr "主题：噪音投诉"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Horrible smell"
msgstr "主题：难闻的气味"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: Jamie Forest, Community Resident, Unit A02\n"
"  TO: Shady Hills Corporation, Service Portal\n"
"  RE: Seriously!?\n"
"\n"
" My son just told me he keeps receiving advertisements in the mail for a "
"nursing home.  He told me that your company runs it!  Are you trying to get "
"rid of me!?  You're sick!  I demand you have your CEO call me!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：杰米·福瑞斯特，社区居民，A02 单元\n"
"发往：Shady Hills 企业，服务部\n"
"主题：认真的！？\n"
"\n"
"我儿子刚刚告诉我，他的邮箱不断收到疗养院的广告。他告诉我这家疗养院就是你们公司经营的！你们是想摆脱我吗！？一群恶心的家伙！让你们的CEO打电话给我！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: Larry Landborn, Unit B11\n"
"  TO: Shady Hills Corporation, Service Portal\n"
"  RE: Noise complaint\n"
"\n"
"  Hello.  I am once again requesting your help with my neighbor in B10.  "
"There are loud sounds from all times of day.  She claims her grandkids are "
"visiting but the noises have been non-stop for weeks!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：拉里·兰德伯恩，B11 单元\n"
"发往：Shady Hills 企业，服务部\n"
"主题：噪音投诉\n"
"\n"
"你好，我再次请求你们的帮助。住在 B10 里的邻居整天都很吵。她声称她的孙子们在拜访，但是噪声已经几周没停过了！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: Sandra Shells, Unit B06\n"
"  TO: Shady Hills Corporation, Service Portal\n"
"  RE: Horrible smell\n"
"\n"
"  There's a bad smell coming from unit B07.  Please look into it.  Thanks."
msgstr ""
"&来自：桑德拉·肖斯，B06 单元\n"
"发往：Shady Hills 企业，服务部\n"
"主题：难闻的气味\n"
"\n"
"B07 单元里有股难闻的气味散发出来。麻烦派个人看下。谢谢。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"MY PC.\n"
" You are logged in as: ADMINISTRATOR.\n"
"\n"
"  WARNING!  ERROR IN POWER SUPPLY DETECTED.  RESERVE POWER ACTIVATED.  SAVE "
"ALL WORK AND SAFELY SHUT DOWN THIS DEVICE IMMEDIATELY!"
msgstr ""
"&我的电脑\n"
"当前登录身份：管理员。\n"
"\n"
"警告！检测到电源错误。备用电源已激活。保存所有工作内容并立即安全关闭此设备！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Connect to BINGO CHAMPIONSHIPS ONLINE"
msgstr "连接到 BINGO锦标赛OL"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The webpage cannot be found :( Check your connection and try again, or "
"contact your Internet Service Provider."
msgstr "找不到网页 :( 请检查你的连接并重试，或联系你的网络服务提供商。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Error connecting to server.  You will be unable to send or receive new "
"messages.  Check your connection and try again, or contact your Internet "
"Service Provider."
msgstr "连接服务器时出错。你将无法发送或接收新消息。请检查你的连接并重试，或联系你的网络服务提供商。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Security Gate"
msgstr "主题：安全门"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Survivor's Club"
msgstr "主题：幸存者俱乐部！？"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "RE: Your Daily BINGO News!"
msgstr "主题：你的每日BINGO新闻"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: Randolph VanBuren, Shady Hills Community Manager\n"
"\n"
"  RE: Security Gate\n"
"\n"
"  Greetings everyone in our fine community.  I wanted to give you an update "
"on Shady Hills' official stance on the security and safety of our esteemed "
"residents.  We are doing everything in our power to keep you safe from harm.  "
"We understand the news has been frightening lately with talk of violence in "
"the streets.  Rest assured you are safe inside of our neighborhood.  Out of "
"an abundance of caution we are installing a new front gate to the entrance of "
"the neighborhood.  This gate will keep back even the most violent of "
"criminals.  Should you have any questions or concerns, please contact our "
"service portal.\n"
"\n"
"  Thank you for your trust in Shady Hills,\n"
" Randolph VanBuren"
msgstr ""
"&来自：伦道夫·范布伦，Shady Hills 社区经理\n"
"\n"
"主题：安全门\n"
"\n"
"美好社区中的各位，大家好。我想向你们介绍 Shady Hills "
"对我们尊敬居民的安全问题的官方立场。我们正在竭尽全力保护你免受伤害。我们知道最近有关街头暴力的消息令人恐惧，但请放心，你在我们的社区内是安全的。出于谨慎考虑"
"，我们正在社区入口处安装一个新的前门。即使是最凶恶的罪犯，这扇门也能挡住。如果你有任何问题或疑虑，请联系我们的服务部。\n"
"\n"
"感谢你对 Shady Hills 的信任，\n"
"伦道夫·范布伦"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: Jamie Forest, Community Resident, Unit A02\n"
"\n"
"  RE: Survivor's Club!?\n"
"\n"
"  Hey there!  Thanks for your interest in our club.  We are really excited to "
"have you!  I'll have to come check out your panic room sometime!  A few of us "
"are going to check out the cave in the park if you want to join us.  "
"Officially, it's supposed to be off limits, but what are they going to do "
"about it?  I heard it even connects to the sewers, maybe if the world really "
"goes to hell like they're all thinking, we can make use of it!  I'm kidding, "
"I don't believe that crap."
msgstr ""
"&来自：杰米·福瑞斯特，社区居民，A02 单元\n"
"\n"
"主题：幸存者俱乐部！？\n"
"\n"
"嘿！感谢你对我们俱乐部感兴趣，我们真的很高兴有你！有时间我得去看看你的安全屋！如果你想加入我们，我们中的一些人会去公园里的洞穴看看。按照官方的说法，那里应该"
"是禁区，但他们又能怎么做呢？听说那里甚至连通到了下水道，说不定世界真的像大家想的那样快要变成地狱了，我们可以利用一下！我在开玩笑，我不相信这种废话。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_RET_COMM.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"FROM: BINGO CHAMPIONSHIPS ONLINE\n"
"\n"
"  Your Daily BINGO News!\n"
"\n"
"  Thank you for being a member of BINGO CHAMPIONSHIPS ONLINE!  Today we have "
"an interview with our latest champion, WINIFRED SMITH!  Click the link below "
"to hear her incredible story!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：BINGO锦标赛OL\n"
"\n"
"主题：你的每日BINGO新闻！\n"
"\n"
"感谢你成为BINGO锦标赛OL的会员！今天我们采访了我们最新的冠军，温妮弗雷德·史密斯！点击下面的链接，听听她不可思议的故事！"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Request Monorail"
msgstr "请求单轨列车"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Download Train Data"
msgstr "下载列车数据"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Power off."
msgstr "关机。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"UNABLE TO CONTACT MONORAIL LINE.  PLEASE SEE YOUR ADMINISTRATOR FOR "
"ASSISTANCE."
msgstr "无法连接到单轨铁路网络。请向你的管理员寻求帮助。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#: data/mods/Perk_melee/menu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Go back."
msgstr "返回。"

#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "TRANSFER COMPLETE."
msgstr "转移完成。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me directions?"
msgstr "你能给我指明方向吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You listen to the directions, and jot them down in your map"
msgstr "&你听从了指示，然后把它记在地图上"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  Liam looks over your shoulder, and nods.  \"I've got a good feeling about "
"this one.\""
msgstr "。利亚姆回头看了看你，又点了点头：“我觉得这次一定能成功。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You listen to the directions, and jot them down in your map."
msgstr "&你听从了指示，然后把它记在地图上。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  The Merc looks at the map with an eyeroll.  \"This ain't it, chief.\""
msgstr "。 雇佣兵翻了个白眼，看着地图说道：“头儿，这不是正确的地方。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  Yusuke studies the drawing for a moment, then raises an eyebrow.  \"I've "
"been out that way scavenging before, and I don't remember seeing anything "
"like the warehouse we're looking for.\""
msgstr "。 雄介仔细端详了图画一会儿，然后挑了挑眉。“我以前去过那边搜寻物资，但我不记得我见过像我们现在要找的这种仓库。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  Chris watches over your shoulder, frowning slightly.  \"I think I know "
"that area, and I'm not quite sure that's what we're looking for.\""
msgstr "。 克里斯在你身后看着，微微皱眉。“我觉得我对那片地区有印象，但我不是很确定那是不是我们要找的地方。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Possible directions to Exodii warehouse"
msgstr "流亡族仓库的可能方向"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/common_talk.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Possible directions to Exodii warehouse"
msgid ""
"You've gotten directions to what might be the warehouse Rubik asked you to "
"find."
msgstr "你已经得到了鲁比克要求你寻找的仓库的方向。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ Materials manager and music fan from another Ethiopia.
msgid "Luliya"
msgstr "露莉亚"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Cyborg, type 2"
msgstr "改造人2型"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Job description of "Cyborg, type 2" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Cyborg, type 1" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Cyborg, type 9" NPC class
msgid "I'm a cyborg."
msgstr "我是个改造人。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Inikwani dehina metahi tegwazhi."
msgstr "Inikwani dehina metahi tegwazhi."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You see a tall golden figure with female features.  Strapped to the back of "
"the head with copper wire is a glass cylinder containing long frizzy black "
"hair.  The body stands still and emits an unpleasant beeping sound.  On the "
"back there is a large red button with strange markings.  There is a golden "
"harp of some kind in their hand."
msgstr ""
"&你看到一个具有女性特征的高大金色身影。一个玻璃圆柱体，脑后绑着铜线，里面有长长的卷曲黑发。她的身体静止不动，发出难听的哔哔声。背面有一个红色的大按钮，上面"
"有奇怪的标记。 她的手里拿着一把类似金色竖琴的东西。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Push the big red button.]"
msgstr "[按下巨大的红色按钮。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Stethoscope] Is this alive?"
msgstr "[使用听诊器] 还活着吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Do nothing.]"
msgstr "[什么都不做。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you speak English?  [slowly and loudly]  ENGLISH?"
msgstr "你听得懂我说的话吗？[缓慢而大声]英文能懂不？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[You point to your chest.]  <u_name>.  [You point at the golden figure.]  "
"What is your name?"
msgstr "[你指向自己]  <u_name>。[你指向黄金塑像]你名字叫啥？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I heard you playing that.  [You point at the golden harp she holds]  La la "
"la.  Do you like music, Luliya?"
msgstr "我听到你在弹奏。[你指向她手中的黄金竖琴]  La la la。  露莉亚，你喜欢音乐吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can't understand you."
msgstr "我无法理解。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You hear a loud static discharge, a rough mechanical chugging sound, and "
"then high-pitched shrieking with strange distortions and modulations in the "
"sound.  The golden figure shudders, arms flailing.  \"ቆዳዬ! ቆዳዬ በእሳት ላይ ነው! "
"እየሞትኩ ነው!\""
msgstr ""
"&你听见一阵巨大的放电声，一股粗糙的机械撞击声，然后是伴随着奇怪扭曲和调制的高音尖叫声。金色的身影颤抖着，手臂不断挥舞：“ቆዳዬ！ቆዳዬ በእሳት ላይ "
"ነው！እየሞትኩ ነው！”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello.  Are you all right?  I just hit the button on your back."
msgstr "哈喽。你没事吧？我刚刚按下了你背上的按钮。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not understanding that.  Can you try again?"
msgstr "我听不明白。你能再说一次吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Speak English ya <freaking> robot.  We don't take kindly to that kind of "
"thing here.  [You frown menacingly]"
msgstr "说英语，你这<freaking>机器人。我可对你们这类人不太好。[你威胁地皱起眉头]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "State your name and function machine."
msgstr "报上你的姓名和功能，机器。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 11]  Huh.  That sounds a little familiar, a little like Arabic.  "
"Earabiun?  [slowly and clearly]  EARABIUN?"
msgstr "[智力 11] 嗯。这听起来有点熟悉，有点像阿拉伯语。埃拉比恩？ [缓慢而清晰地] 埃拉比恩？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I'm done with this."
msgstr "算了，我不想再说了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You press your stethoscope to the chest of the figure and hear a clear, "
"strong heartbeat and a strange whirring sound that sounds like clockwork."
msgstr "你将听诊器按在人形的胸部，听到清晰强烈的心跳声和听起来像发条的奇怪嗡嗡声。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So she's alive then."
msgstr "所以她还活着。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Probably fine then.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Probably fine then.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&A long pause, then she shakes her head  \"Inigilizinya yelemi.  No.\""
msgstr "&长时间的停顿，然后她摇摇头：“Inigilizinya yelemi.不。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right then.  You seem to understand what I mean.  And the word no."
msgstr "那好吧。 你似乎明白我的意思。 还有“不”这个词。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "好吧，<end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&A long pause.  You can't see her eyes but it seems like she is studying your "
"face.  \"Sime Luliya ibalalehu.\"  She points to her own chest.  \"Luliya.\"  "
"She points to your chest.  \"<u_name>.  Siletewawekini desi bilonyali, "
"<u_name>.\"  She strums a pleasant melody on her krar."
msgstr ""
"&长时间的停顿。 你看不到她的眼睛，但她似乎正在研究你的脸。 “Sime Luliya（露莉亚） ibalalehu.” [她指着自己的胸口。] "
"“露莉亚。” [她指着你的胸口。]“<u_name>.Siletewwekini desi bilonyali,<u_name>.” "
"[她在卡拉琴上弹奏出一首愉快的旋律。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're getting somewhere.  Pleased to meet you Luliya."
msgstr "我们总算有些进展。 很高兴认识你，露莉亚。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&A long pause, then she shakes her head.  \"Ayi arebinya alinagerimi.\""
msgstr "&长时间的停顿，然后她摇摇头：“Ayi arebinya alinagerimi.”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right then.  It seems like you do kind of understand it though."
msgstr "那好吧。 看来你确实有点理解它。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&She nods enthusiastically and strums a few notes on her krar.  \"Awo muzika "
"iwedalehu.\""
msgstr "&她热情地点点头，并在她的卡拉琴上弹奏了几个音符：“Awo muzika iwedalehu.”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Guitar] I happen to have a nice guitar, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用吉他]我恰好有一把不错的吉他,想和我一起弹奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Trumpet] I happen to have a nice trumpet, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用小号]我恰好有一把不错的小号,想和我一起吹奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Saxophone] I happen to have a nice saxophone, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用萨克斯管]我恰好有一把不错的萨克斯管,想和我一起吹奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Violin] I happen to have a nice violin, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用小提琴]我恰好有一把不错的小提琴,想和我一起演奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Harmonica] I happen to have a nice harmonica, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用口琴]我恰好有一把不错的口琴,想和我一起吹奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Use Cowbell] I happen to have a nice cowbell, want to play with me?"
msgstr "[使用牛铃]我恰好有一个不错的牛铃,想和我一起敲奏吗?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Huh, you know music, good to know.  I'll try and find something to play and "
"come back."
msgstr "呵呵，你懂音乐，很好。我可以试着找些能够演奏的乐器再回来。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You perform on your musical instrument with everything you have, giving a "
"strong performance.  Luliya sways and begins to play her instrument and sing "
"along.  The music and her voice are beautiful, she sounds like she has had "
"some formal musical training."
msgstr "&你全身心地投入演奏你的乐器。露莉亚摇晃着身体，跟着节奏开始弹琴并唱了起来。音乐和她的声音都很美，听起来她受过某种正规的音乐训练。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fun, thank you for playing with me, Luliya."
msgstr "挺有趣的，露莉娅谢谢你和我一起玩。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_Luliya.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fun, thank you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "有趣，谢谢你。<end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "Rubik"
msgstr "鲁比克"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Cyborg, type 1"
msgstr "改造人1型"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Rubik's Exodii battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "鲁比克的流亡族战斗步枪"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle" of gun "Rubik's PA
#. md. 68 battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Rubik's PA md. 68 battle rifle" of item "Rubik's
#. Exodii battle rifle"
msgid ""
"The most popular gun to use the 12.3ln cartridge was, of course, the PA md. "
"71.  Its predecessor, the md. 68, was viewed by many as a sort of failure: "
"although it was reliable and powerful, it was too heavy to be used as a good "
"infantry weapon, and not really heavy enough to be a good support gun.  "
"Enough were made, though, that during the zombie apocalypse, it gained a "
"great deal of resurgent popularity as a light emplacement gun that used "
"readily available ammunition.  It perfectly served the purposes of the "
"Exodii, who had far less concern about its unwieldiness.\n"
"\n"
"This particular rifle has been painted a dusty pink color and has a picture "
"of a smiling eel twisting along the barrel."
msgstr ""
"在所有使用 12.3ln 弹的枪械中，最受欢迎的的枪当然是PA Md. 71 步枪。作为它的前身，PA Md. 68 "
"战斗步枪被许多人认为是某种程度上的失败品：虽然它非常可靠而且威力强大，但它太重了，不是一把好的步兵武器，但又不足以成为一把好的支援武器。尽管如此，它仍然被大"
"量制造，在随后到来的丧尸末日之中，作为一种弹药很容易获得的轻型炮塔枪，受到了人们的再次青睐。而且它完全符合流亡族的需求，它们对这把枪械不灵活的使用条件不太在"
"意。\n"
"\n"
"这把特殊的步枪被漆成暗粉色，枪管上画着一条盘在枪管上微笑的鳗鱼。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_definitions.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Rubik's Exodii battle rifle"
msgid "Rubik's PA md. 68 battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Rubik's PA md. 68 battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "鲁比克的 PA Md. 68 战斗步枪"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
msgstr "给鲁比克带来 1000 单位麻醉剂"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
msgid ""
"If'n us'll to add the metal an' plastic for ye, us'll need a thousand unit o' "
"them anus-feticks, half for your thinkin'-meat an' half for our stock."
msgstr "你的若想让我们的给你的加闪闪金属的，我们的需要一千的他们的\"马嘴鸡\"的，一半是给你的会思考的肉的，一半给我们的当储备的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "King's own luck!"
msgstr "愿王的赐你的幸运！"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "That be a choice an' you can tass.  Come back to this'n if you like."
msgstr "这个的抉择的，你的可以丢下。想清楚的，可以回到这里来的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
msgid "Check round the chirurgery an' such, I'd razz."
msgstr "可以检查的外科的地方的，我会去的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
msgid "Us'n waits patient-like for that anus-fetick."
msgstr "我们的病人一样的还在等那些坠机的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "Fine an' fine.  We can pass it in when you like."
msgstr "好的好的。你的准备好了的我们可以注射的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 1000 units of anesthetic to Rubik"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Investigate the Mysterious Bunker"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "Fine an' fine.  Come back to this'n if you like to try again."
msgstr "好的好的。你的准备好了的可以再试一次的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Investigate the Mysterious Bunker"
msgstr "调查神秘地堡"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Investigate the Mysterious Bunker"
msgid "What've ye scolted, then, o'the clunker?"
msgstr "你的好了没的，调查那个，吵吵的笛豹的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Investigate the Mysterious Bunker"
msgid ""
"Aye and fine!  One for the paper-claim an' so.  An I'm ken, these'n's could "
"be a right thorn.  For ol' Rubik's sake, let's hope they be'n't for to drive "
"us out o' your otherlands."
msgstr "好得很！一切都在计划之中。我知道，这些家伙可能会是个大麻烦。看在鲁比克的份上，希望他们不会把我们从你的领地赶出去。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Investigate the Mysterious Bunker"
msgid "Hm.  The escoltin' our way be less.  This'n'll yark at the Scythy mayhaps."
msgstr "嗯，我们路上的护卫减少了。这个可能会让瑟希警惕。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its locator antenna."
msgstr "找到丢失的流亡族仓库并重新启动其定位天线。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "What ye'r searching is safehouse-like, sand, stone, metal an' all."
msgstr "你们要找的东西就像安全屋一样，有沙子、石头、金属等等。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the lost Exodii warehouse and reboot its
#. locator antenna."
msgid "Us'n waits patient-like for that'."
msgstr "我们耐心地等待着。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Just because you asked, I think we can work something out.  Yes, the
#. Scythean has been bugging me about something.  It's not something a cyborg
#. like me can do, but a mercenary would probably fit the bill.
msgid ""
"Them as offer as can, an it be so.  Aye, there's summat the old Scythy been "
"larkin' up Rubik's tailpipe.  B'ain't tass right for a clanker like this'n, "
"but a pop-an-work like you'n, maybe well and suited."
msgstr ""
"它们会尽可能提供，被，如果可以。是的，某事现存于此，老瑟茜在捣腾鲁比克的排气管。不适合，叮叮当当的，像这样。但是流行的一个工作，像你这样的，或许是好的合适的"
"。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's \"the ol' Scythy\"?"
msgstr "“瑟希”是什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why can't one of you do this?"
msgstr "所以为什么不让你们的人去做呢？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about this job that you can't do."
msgstr "和我详细讲讲为什么没法干那个活。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  See you later, Rubik."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>。回头见，鲁比克。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Have you seen our big stompy quads?  There's a lot of things we're good
#. at, but sneaky and subtle we aren't.  If we want a meet cute, first we've
#. got to lay out the hempen mats.
msgid ""
"Hat ye kennt our great clanks an' stompers?  There be many a thing we can do "
"right good, but for the supple an' smooth, we b'ain't.  Wish'n we to make a "
"meet-cute, must we first lay out the hempen mats."
msgstr "你听说过我们伟大的巨型机器人和重型机甲吗?有很多事情我们都能做得很好,但我们在灵活和流畅方面就不行了。如果我们想要来一场浪漫邂逅,就必须先铺上大麻垫子。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold up, did you just say \"meet cute\"?"
msgstr "等一下，你刚才是说“邂逅”吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I am guessing it doesn't matter, but what do you mean about hempen mats?"
msgstr "我猜这不重要，但是你说的麻垫是什么意思？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, fine.  Tell me more about this job that you can't do."
msgstr "好吧,没关系。告诉我更多为什么你无法做这份工作的原因。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It's a bit hard to explain, but I'll do my best.  The forces we send far
#. out, what I'd call 'escolts'… explorers?  They've scouted a place with a
#. bit of promise, as far as I can tell.  A wall of concrete around a bunker.
#. That's not so odd in a place like this, but this one has people coming and
#. going.  There's something still in there, and I wonder who.  Are they
#. friendly or not?  What would you think about doing some scouting yourself?
msgid ""
"It be a right coddle to yark, but ol' Rubik'll do as can.  Them as we send "
"a'far, what I'd assert as 'escolts'… explorers?  They's escolted a place with "
"a mite o' promise, an I'm ken.  A wall o' crete-stone, abreast a rattlin' "
"clunker… a 'bunker'.  Not so odd in a deadlands alas, but this'n gots the "
"comin's and goin's.  Sommat's still in there, an' ol' Rubik wonders who.  Be "
"they friend or foe?  What say ye t'helpin' with a mite o' escoltin' y'self?"
msgstr ""
"这个的有点娇惯难说话的，但鲁比克会尽量将清楚的。我们的派出的部队很远，是你们叫做“趟先”……探险的？他们趟先到了一个有一点希望的地方，我记下的。一道全石灰石"
"的墙，就像是个吵吵的笛豹……是\"地堡\"的。 "
"唉，这个的在一个死地并不奇怪的，但有来来往往的人的。里面的还有谁的，鲁比克想知道的。他们友好的敌对的？你的会怎么考虑走一趟先的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, today's your lucky day, my metal friend.  I already know the place "
"quite well."
msgstr "好吧，今天你可走运了，我的金属朋友。我早就知道那个地方了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What exactly do you want me to do?  Scout out this bunker and contact the "
"people in it?"
msgstr "你具体想要我做些什么？就去探查一下这个地堡然后联系上里面的人吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ No, my friend, no!  Don't make contact, understand?  This is a covert op.
#. If you see that it's safe you can go in closer and look around, but for
#. goodness' sake, don't talk to anyone and don't linger.
msgid ""
"No, me fruit gum, no!  Make no contact, y'ken?  This be covert.  If ye kennit "
"be safe, traipse along an' for a kennabout, but upon the chimes, speak none "
"and tarry little."
msgstr "不，我的水果口香糖，不！ 别再联系了好吗？ 这个要隐蔽啊。如果你懂了安全的，就沿着小路漫步，探查一下的，不要说话的，也不要久留的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I get the impression this is important, but I don't know what you mean."
msgstr "我大概了解这件事的重要性了，但我还是不太理解你的意思。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This sounds insanely dangerous.  They could just shoot me on sight."
msgstr "这听起来危险指数爆炸了。他们可能一照面就把我一枪撂倒了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So you want me to go there, see what's inside the walls, look around a "
"little, and then let you know if I see anything, but if someone tries to talk "
"to me, not mention you or your people?"
msgstr "所以你是想让我去到那里，看看墙里面的情况，收集信息，然后告诉你我的发现，但如果里面有人问起来，不要提及你和你的族人，对吧？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm gonna need to think on this one.  See you later, Rubik."
msgstr "你的需求我要好好考虑一下。下次见了，鲁比克。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*pauses for a moment, and lets out a slow sigh, speaking hesitantly as they "
"catch themselves in idioms.  \"Make no contact.  We ken… we think the abroad "
"o'… the outside o' the bunker be safe an'… be safe to explore, for one such "
"as ye, who harks as from this'n land.  A wander in and escolt… a look around "
"we ken as no… no risk.  If ye think ye been spotted, wave along and make no "
"mention of ol' Rubik and the Exodii.  Not afore we be razzed some more o' "
"this rattlin'… this bunker."
msgstr ""
"*停顿了一会儿，缓缓地叹了口气，字斟句酌地仿佛自己被那些俗语给噎住了：“不要接触的。我们知道了的……我们认为的……外面的……地堡外是安全的，而且……对于像你"
"们的这片土地的人来说，探索是安全的。小路漫步的……护送的……转一转的，我们的认为没有……没有风险的。如果发现了的，挥挥手的，不要提及老鲁比克和流亡族的。不太"
"安全的我们去到更了解的……这个碉堡的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How can you know that it's safe?  What if I'm shot on sight?"
msgstr "你怎么确定那边是安全的？要是我过去被一枪撂倒了怎么办？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Our scouts have seen people who look like you wandering in the area
#. safely.  If the scavengers can make it in and out, you should be fine.
msgid ""
"Them as we've escolted seems a fair kin, an' we've eyed a scav or two "
"wanderin' the premise unscathed.  If'n the scavs o' the dust can make it in "
"an' out, so should ye be."
msgstr "我们护送的他们看起来都是好亲戚的，而且我们的还看到一两个拾荒的在屋子里毫发无伤地闲逛的。如果拾荒的可以进出，你的也应该一样的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aye, ye kennit well."
msgstr "当然的，你的很懂的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"This is insane.  I can't tell if you're leading me into a trap or not.  "
"What's in it for me?"
msgstr "这太疯狂了。我不知道你是不是在把我引入陷阱。这对我有什么好处?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Sure.  Don't know what good it'll do you, but I might be willing.  What are "
"you paying?"
msgstr "好吧。不知道这对你有啥帮助，但我愿意走一趟。你准备了什么报酬？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I didn't know you'd be such a hard bargain!  Tell ya what, when you come
#. back, I'll let you in on some of these fancy knick-kacks.
msgid ""
"Rightly a trig barter, an I'm ken.  By ol' Rubik's word, on your saintly "
"march home, for you'll have the pick of the bright and steelies roun' ol' "
"Rubik's shop, choice o' your own finely.  What say?"
msgstr "正确的是易货贸易的，我懂了的。用老鲁比克的话说的，在你神圣回家途中的，你的可以在老鲁比克的商店里挑选明亮而钢铁般的，精心选择你自己的。怎么样的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll go check it out."
msgstr "我会过去看一看的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's quite the spirit!  For an exchange, I'll give you some of these
#. shiny tools, whatever you want.  How's that sound?
msgid ""
"Ah, 'tis a fine spark.  F'r a switch an' clock, ol' Rubik can share y'like o' "
"these bright and steelies roun' the shop, choice o' your finely.  What say?"
msgstr "啊，这是一个很好的火花的。 对于开关和时钟，老鲁比克可以分享商店里这些明亮而钢铁般的，给你的精心选择的。怎么样的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll go check it out.  Thanks, Rubik."
msgstr "我会过去看一看的。谢啦，鲁比克。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm gonna need to think on this one.  I'll see you later, Rubik."
msgstr "你的需求我要好好考虑一下。下次见了，鲁比克。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, would you be willing to tell me about it?
msgid "Ah, would ye be willin' ta yark with me about it?"
msgstr "啊，你的愿意跟我的说一说的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "*Tell him."
msgstr "*告诉他。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe later, can we talk about something else?"
msgstr "下次再说这个。我们换个话题吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not right now.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "不是现在。<end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's great!  What would you like as payment?
msgid "'Tis a fine an' dandy!  What can ol' Rubik stand ye for, then?"
msgstr "这是一个很好的花花的！那么，老鲁比克还能给点什么的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's see what you have in stock."
msgstr "让我看看你还有什么存货。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I become a cyborg, like yourself?"
msgstr "我能成为一个改造人吗，像你一样？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just glad to help, I don't need any payment."
msgstr "我不需要报酬，帮到你就很好了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We are unable to locate one of our warehouses since the last jump.  We
#. would need you to go find it and reactivate its locator
msgid ""
"Well an surely, fruit gum!  Aye, ye kennit well.  'Tis a store-cabin, mayhap "
"the likes you've seen.  This'n be older'n most, clade o' iron and "
"crete-stone.  Abreast the ceil, high atop, there be a steely jut, piercin' "
"the heavens.  In times ordinary, Great Grey could call out and screed the "
"jut, kennit, and send aloft an escolt to razz 'er.  Oft times, the jut is "
"wibbled on the wobble, an' it be coals'n coke.  Ol' Rubik can give you'n a "
"dandy to pop 'er back aloft, and that's a fig and a fiddle."
msgstr ""
"当然的，水果口香糖！是的，你的懂得的。这是个储藏室的，也许就是你见过的。这是最古老的，铁和混凝土石碰撞的。与天花板并排，在高高的顶部，有个钢铁的突出物，刺穿"
"天空的。在平常的时候，大灰可以召唤并平整突出物，懂了没的，并派出一支护卫队到高处去的。很多时候，突出物会在摇摆器上摇摆，而且是煤和焦炭的。老鲁比克可以给你一"
"个花花的，你的在高处弹回来的，那就是无花果和小提琴的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We are unable to locate one of our warehouses since the last jump.  We
#. would need you to go find it and reactivate its locator
msgid ""
"Well an surely, fruit gum!  Mayhap this be a chance to show y'self a true, "
"for Rubik's got sommat to ask yet again.  The way o' the Exode is t'shimmy "
"an' wobble, an' on thislike wobble, a few bits wobbled off, kennit?  'Tis "
"rightful common, alack.  One such is hidden for our escolts an' our screeds.  "
"Mayhap as y'know the lands, ye'd have a see of it?  Aye, ye kennit well.  "
"'Tis a store-cabin, mayhap the likes you've seen.  This'n be older'n most, "
"clade o' iron and crete-stone.  Abreast the ceil, high atop, there be a "
"steely jut, piercin' the heavens.  In times ordinary, Great Grey could call "
"out and screed the jut, kennit, and send aloft an escolt to razz 'er.  Oft "
"times, the jut is wibbled on the wobble, an' it be coals'n coke.  Ol' Rubik "
"can give you'n a dandy to pop 'er back aloft, and that's a fig and a fiddle."
msgstr ""
"当然的，水果口香糖！也许这是一个你的展示真实的机会，因为鲁比克再次要求的。流亡的方式是摇摆再摇摆，就像摇摆一样，有一点摇摆不定，你懂了没的？这很正常的，唉。"
" 其中一个是为我们的护卫和我们的长篇大论所隐藏的。也许你的了解这片土地，你的会看过的吗？是的，你的懂得的。这是个储藏室的，也许就是你见过的。这是最古老的，铁"
"和混凝土石碰撞的。与天花板并排，在高高的顶部，有个钢铁的突出物，刺穿天空的。在平常的时候，大灰可以召唤并平整突出物，懂了没的，并派出一支护卫队到高处去的。很"
"多时候，突出物会在摇摆器上摇摆，而且是煤和焦炭的。老鲁比克可以给你一个花花的，你的在高处弹回来的，那就是无花果和小提琴的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We are unable to locate one of our warehouses since the last jump.  We
#. would need you to go find it and reactivate its locator
msgid ""
"Well an surely, fruit gum!  For an' such as ye've done us a good.  Aye, ye "
"kennit well.  'Tis a store-cabin, mayhap the likes you've seen.  This'n be "
"older'n most, clade o' iron and crete-stone.  Abreast the ceil, high atop, "
"there be a steely jut, piercin' the heavens.  In times ordinary, Great Grey "
"could call out and screed the jut, kennit, and send aloft an escolt to razz "
"'er.  Oft times, the jut is wibbled on the wobble, an' it be coals'n coke.  "
"Ol' Rubik can give you'n a dandy to pop 'er back aloft, and that's a fig and "
"a fiddle."
msgstr ""
"当然的，水果口香糖！对于你的这样的，已经为我们的做了大好事的。是的，你的懂得的。这是个储藏室的，也许就是你见过的。这是最古老的，铁和混凝土石碰撞的。与天花板"
"并排，在高高的顶部，有个钢铁的突出物，刺穿天空的。在平常的时候，大灰可以召唤并平整突出物，懂了没的，并派出一支护卫队到高处去的。很多时候，突出物会在摇摆器上"
"摇摆，而且是煤和焦炭的。老鲁比克可以给你一个花花的，你的在高处弹回来的，那就是无花果和小提琴的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think I got most of that.  A metal and concrete building with some kind of "
"metal pole on top that you want me to fix?"
msgstr "我想我听懂了一部分。一座金属和混凝土建筑，顶部有根金属杆，你想让我修一下？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What?  A jut?  Fig and a fiddle?"
msgstr "什么？ 突出物？ 无花果和小提琴？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ A jut is a long, thin pole.  The warehouse is made of concrete and rusty
#. iron, and atop it there's a glistening pole.  The pole is broken, turned
#. off.  I got a tool for you to turn it back on.
msgid ""
"A jut be a long, thin post, kennit.  The store-cabin be made o' con-crete an' "
"rusty iron, and atop it be a glintin' post.  The post be broken, I'd razz.  "
"Turnt off.  Rubik's got a tool for you to pop, make it turnt on."
msgstr ""
"只是一个又长又细的柱子，懂了没的。储藏室是用混凝土和生锈的铁制成的，上面有一根闪闪发光的柱子。柱子被破坏了，我的感到愤怒的。关掉。鲁比克有个工具可以让你弹出"
"并打开它。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"OK, got it.  A metal and concrete building with some kind of metal pole on "
"top that you want me to fix"
msgstr "好吧，我知道了。一座金属和混凝土建筑，顶部有根金属杆，你想让我修一下？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Exactly.  This is some talking fit for my beloved jaryi.  What do you
#. think?
msgid ""
"Just so.  'Tis like yarkin' fit f'r me beloved jaryi, y'kennit so fine.  What "
"say you?"
msgstr "就是这样的。这就像大喊大叫，很适合我亲爱的贾伊，你的真好的。你的怎么说的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What, now that I think on it, I am not sure what you meant about juts and "
"figs."
msgstr "好吧，现在我回想下，我还是不懂你所说的无花果和小提琴是什么意思。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Shouldn't your quads be able to do that?"
msgstr "你的四轮同伴们不是应该能够完成吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any clues on how to find it?"
msgstr "有如何找到它的线索吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's in this for me?"
msgstr "这对我来说有什么好处？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Then I'll find it."
msgstr "那我就去找它吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Beloved jaryi?  What did you just call me?"
msgstr "亲爱的贾伊？你刚才叫我什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ No, I'm not calling you jaryi.  Jaryi is my mother's mother.  It's a
#. King's Landing word for a grandmother, I'm making a little joke at you.
msgid ""
"Ha, not callin' y'me jaryi.  Jaryi be the mother-twice.  'Tis but a King's "
"Landing assert f'r a grandmother, Rubik's makin' a chestnut at ye."
msgstr "哈，不叫我贾伊。贾伊就是母亲的两倍的。这不过是祖母的君临断言，鲁比克在向你举个栗子。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That word doesn't sound like any of the other Anglic words you've used, "
"though.  What's it from?"
msgstr "不过，那个词听着不像你说过的其它英吉利语单词。它是从哪来的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you talking about before?"
msgstr "你刚刚还说了什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's right, I did.  My mother's mother was a woman of the old kind, and
#. so was my father's father.  My father's mother, she was a grandma, a little
#. piece of old London-Town, but I had a jaryi and a taita and a tamoi (these
#. are words for grandparents in a guarani dialect).  They were all there,
#. right to the end.  Standing by, we were, one and all.  No time for stories,
#. though.  Back to the here and now.
msgid ""
"Right so, a fine notice.  Rubik's mother-twice, she were a woman o'th'old "
"kind.  And were her mate, and Rubik's father-twice.  Rubik's father-mother, "
"she were a gran, a fitty bit of ol' London-Town, right so, but Rubik had a "
"jaryi and a taita and a tamoi.\" Rubik's voice goes distant for a moment.  "
"\"An' they was all there, right to the end.  Standin' by, we were, one and "
"all.\" They pause, then seem to snap back.  \"No time for stories, kennit?  "
"Back to the here an' now."
msgstr ""
"是的，很好的通知。鲁比克的母亲——两倍的，她的是位非常古老的女人。是她的伴侣，也是鲁比克的父亲——两倍的。鲁比克的父亲的母亲，她是一位祖母，是一位伦敦镇的人"
"，没错，但鲁比克的一个贾伊、一个泰塔和一个塔莫。”鲁比克的声音暂时变得遥远：“他们都是在那里的，一直到最后。我们都站在一旁。”他停顿了一下，然后似乎又回过神"
"来：“没时间讲故事，懂了没的？现在回到这里的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, let's talk about business again."
msgstr "是啊，我们再谈谈生意吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Without any indication of its location, there's too much ground to cover,
#. and we have many other things to look for.  This one is pretty easy to see,
#. so maybe some of the locals can help find it.
msgid ""
"'Tis a gull's errand, with narry a sign.  Our stompers cannot cover each "
"squarrel, and they've many a dropsy to search.  This'n be a right easy spot "
"for keen eyes, so mayhap your sameworlds can be of a snap."
msgstr ""
"这是海鸥的差事，没有任何标志的。我们的践踏者无法涵盖每一处争吵，而且他们还有很多水肿要搜索的。对于敏锐的眼睛来说，这将是一个非常容易的地方的，所以也许你的同"
"世界的会很快看到的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need a moment.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "I need a moment.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ that's up to you, I think.  If I could find it myself, I'd send quads out
#. there.  Maybe it would be worth asking around to other survivors?  Seems
#. like a good job for a local guide.
msgid ""
"That's be for your assert, an I'm ken.  If ol' Rubik could find 'er, us'n'd "
"send out the stompers.  For a yark an' a lark, though, couldst ask another of "
"your sameworld?  Mercants or traveler-such?  It be a fine slick to a local "
"guide."
msgstr ""
"这是为了你的断言，我记下的。如果老鲁比克能找到她，我们会派出踩踏者的。不过，对于说话的百灵鸟来说，还找不到你的同世界的吗？商人还是旅者？但对于本地向导来说，"
"这是十分细滑的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You'll win my endless happiness?  Of course not.  I can find you
#. something special from the CBM vaults.  Maybe I can give you a choice?
#. Three different ones.  Think on it and decide when it's done.
msgid ""
"Ye'll win the endless delight of ol' Rubik?\"  You hear a tinny chuckle from "
"behind Rubik's faceplate.  \"O'course.  Ol' Rubik can find f'r ye something a "
"mite special, from the ol' CBM vaults.  Mayahp a choice?  We're kickin' a "
"thriceways.\"  Rubik reaches into the desk in front of them and pulls out a "
"tiny, green-glowing CRT that, amid all the strange alien technology, looks "
"bizarrely familiar, like something from a 1970's sci-fi movie.  They scroll "
"rapidly down a list to find three items, which they tap to emphasize.  'air "
"filtration CBM', 'blood analysis CBM', and 'radiation scrubber system CBM'.\n"
"\n"
"\"Think on it, decide on a last."
msgstr ""
"你的真能让老鲁比克永远快乐的吗？” "
"你听见鲁比克面罩后传来微弱的笑声：“当然。老鲁比克可以从老CBM库里找些特别的东西。可以选择的？就像三次跳跃的。”鲁比克把手伸进他面前的桌子，拿出一个发出绿"
"光的微型CRT显示器，相比各种奇怪的外星科技，它看起来非常熟悉，就像20世纪70"
"年代的科幻电影中的东西。他快速向下滚动列表，找到三个物品，并点击放大。分别是‘空气过滤系统CBM’、‘血液分析CBM’和‘辐射清洗系统CBM’。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"An' a fine farthing ye did, on that.  Thankee sai.  We've a crib on the "
"walkway already."
msgstr "你的在那上面做了一个漂亮的法寻。谢谢的说。行道上的坐标已经回来了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gives you a long look, and somehow you know they're doing a slow blink "
"inside their metal shell.  \"An' did ye forget sommat?  The booter?  Me heart "
"and skelpy, 'tis not so hard a job.  Alas and alack, give us some directions "
"then.\"  They pull out a notepad and pass a pencil your way."
msgstr ""
"*意味深长地看了你一眼，不知怎么的你知道他正在金属壳里慢慢眨眼：“你的忘了的？启动的？我的心和骨头，这个的不是那么难的工作。唉，天哪，那就给我们指路的吧。”"
"他拿出一个记事本，递给你一支铅笔。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Long days and pleasant nights, Rubik.  Let's talk payment."
msgstr "漫长的白天和愉快的夜晚，鲁比克。我们得谈谈报酬。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Detail the road to the warehouse.  This will advance time by ten minutes.]"
msgstr "[详细说明通往仓库的道路。一直讲了快十分钟。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ol' Rubik's gone down into the stores an' slicked up a handful o' some "
"dandies for ye.\"  They reach below the counter and take out three clear "
"plastic bags, each containing a different cybernetic module.  \"Us'n can only "
"spare one o', though.  Which'll it be?  We can slip an' crank 'em in as "
"y'like.\""
msgstr ""
"老鲁比克这就去仓库里的，给你一个新花花的。“他把手伸到柜台下面，拿出三个透明的塑料袋，每个塑料袋里都有一个不同的控制模块。“不过，我们只能抽出一个的。会是哪"
"个的？我们可以随心所欲地把它们塞进你的曲柄里的。\""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Install Air Filtration CBM] I like the look of that air filtration thingy.  "
"Does it come with pine-fresh scent?"
msgstr "[安装空气过滤CBM]我喜欢那个空气过滤装置的外观。它有松枝的清新香味吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Install Blood Analysis CBM] I've always wondered what's in my veins.  Let's "
"try that blood analysis module."
msgstr "[安装血液分析CBM] 我一直想知道血管里流着些什么。让我们试试血液分析模块。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Install Radiation Scrubber CBM] I have nightmares about ending up like Marie "
"Curie.  Radiation scrubber it has to be."
msgstr "[安装辐射清洗系统CBM] 我经常会做噩梦，梦见自己变成玛丽·居里。辐射清洗系统就决定是它了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about store credit instead?  [adds $1500 in store credit]."
msgstr "帮我直接记在账上好吧？[获得等价1500美元的信用]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"How about instead, we turn this into a mutually beneficial relationship in "
"the future.  I don't need anything from you at the moment, but now you know I "
"get the job done."
msgstr "不如这样，我们把这件事当做我们今后互利互惠的起始点。我现在什么都不需要，但你需要记着我帮了你的大忙。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pay Back The Riot Gear to Rubik"
msgstr "Pay Back The Riot Gear to Rubik"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "shiny farthing"
msgid_plural "shiny farthings"
msgstr[0] "閃亮硬幣"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Description of "shiny farthing"
msgid ""
"A small, shiny brass coin with a picture of a stern-looking older man on one "
"side and the words 'For all of Angland and her children' in an arc beneath "
"him.  On the other side is a large number '1' wreathed in what appear to be "
"nettle leaves."
msgstr ""
"一枚闪闪发光的小铜币，一面是面容严肃的老人头像，他的下方围了一圈弧形铭文：\"献给全安格兰王国及其子民\"。而另一面印着一个巨大的数字\"1\""
"，数字上缠绕着的似乎是荨麻叶。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[PLAYTEST] Send me to the Labyrinthine Structure alpha test 0.1, I know it's "
"low on content and lacking combat balance, but I still want to check it out!"
msgstr ""
"[PLAYTEST] Send me to the Labyrinthine Structure alpha test 0.1, I know it's "
"low on content and lacking combat balance, but I still want to check it out!"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PLAYTEST] Tell me more about the Labyrinthine Structure alpha test."
msgstr "[PLAYTEST] Tell me more about the Labyrinthine Structure alpha test."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What've you got for trade?"
msgstr "你有什麼要交易的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you do something for me?"
msgstr "你能为我做点什么吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here to talk about a job."
msgstr "我是来谈工作的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't understand a word you're saying."
msgstr "你說的話我一個字都沒有聽懂。（譯註: NPC在用澳洲方言說話）"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you some kind of robot?"
msgstr "你是某種機器人嗎？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 9] You're called Exodii?  Does that mean you were driven out of your "
"home?"
msgstr "[智力 9] 你稱呼自己是Exodii？這表示你們是被趕出了家鄉？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of place is this?"
msgstr "這裡是什麼地方？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PER 6] Some of this tech looks… weird."
msgstr "[感知 6] 這裡的某些科技看起來……很奇怪。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What's with those weird metal zombies I've been seeing?  They resemble some "
"of the robots around here."
msgstr "我看到的那些奇怪的金属丧尸是怎么回事？它们和这里的一些机器人很相似。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You wanted to ask me some questions earlier, and I think I was rude about it. "
" What did you want to ask?"
msgstr "你之前想我一些问题，我想当时我太粗鲁了。你那时候想问什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can we continue our conversation about your arrival in this world?"
msgstr "我们能接着谈谈你怎么来到这个世界吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any chance I can buy some riot armor?  I need five complete sets."
msgstr "Any chance I can buy some riot armor?  I need five complete sets."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Remember that riot gear you gave me?"
msgstr "Remember that riot gear you gave me?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Back in a blink and a whiff, eh?"
msgstr "轉眼間就回來啦？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ah, a returnin', an I'm ken."
msgstr "啊，就回来了的，我记下的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"And a fine return, matey.\"  Rubik puts a hand on the countertop, and "
"gestures you closer with the other."
msgstr "还不错的回来的，你的。”鲁比克把一只手放在台面上，另一只手示意你靠过去。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fine and you still ain't dead.\"  Their gravelly voice is cheerful.  \"What "
"brings ye roun' Rubik's neckawoods?"
msgstr "还不错的，你的还没死的。”他略显沙哑的声音听上去很愉快：“什么的带来你的到鲁比克地盘的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Bright and sunny, you're back!\"  There's a bit of a friendly chuckle in "
"Rubik's gravelly voice.  \"Rubik's got goods for ye, if you got goods for "
"Rubik."
msgstr "阳光明媚的，你的回来了的！”鲁比克沙哑的声音中带着一丝友好的笑声：“如果你的有东西给鲁比克的，鲁比克有东西给你的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Before you stands a towering mass of metal, at least seven feet high, with a "
"large reflective glass plate in the center of its torso.  It turns as you "
"enter the room, and raises its hand in a surprisingly natural motion of "
"greeting.  A gravelly voice resonates from unseen speakers in the steel "
"frame.  Its tone is bizarrely normal, in complete contrast with everything "
"else around you.  \"Oy, you ain't dead.  Lookin' t'trade?\"  The accent "
"sounds vaguely British, but not familiar; like a terrible imitation of "
"Cockney."
msgstr ""
"&在你面前站着一块高耸的金属，至少有七英尺高，躯干中央有一块大的反光玻璃板。当你进入房间时，它转过身，并举起手来，以令人惊讶的自然动作向你打招呼。钢铁框架上"
"看不见的扬声器发出沙哑的声音。它的音调异常地正常，与你四周的一切形成了鲜明对比：“哦，你的没死的。来交易的？”口音听起来有点像英国口音，但并不熟悉；就像是对"
"伦敦腔的糟糕模仿。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you?  What is this place?"
msgstr "你是誰？這裡是哪裡？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I wanted to talk."
msgstr "其实，我只想随便聊聊。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hell no, I'm out of here."
msgstr "鬼才要。我要走了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just popping in to say hi.  See you later, alligator."
msgstr "只是过来打个招呼。再见了，拜拜。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my buddy doing?"
msgstr "How is my buddy doing?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fast, can you help this lad?"
msgstr "Fast, can you help this lad?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We call ourselves the Exodii, eh?  And other things, but that's good.
#. This is our home, such as it is.  I'm called Rubik, and I've been assigned
#. to trade with you.  Are you looking to trade?  We're always looking for
#. scrap, metal and more.
msgid ""
"Us call us the Exodii, eh?  An' other things, but that'n's good.  This're our "
"home, such as it.  This'n's monicked as Rubik, and tassed with a trade an'.  "
"You lookin' to trade?  Us'n's alay for the scrap, metal an' more as it be."
msgstr ""
"我們稱呼我們自己為 Exodii。還有其他的叫法，不過叫這個就行。這是我們的家，儘管不多。我叫 Rubik "
"，我被派來和你交易。你想要交易嗎？我們一直都缺廢料、金屬和其他東西。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good an' fine, then."
msgstr "好的好的，就这样的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Have it as ye'll see."
msgstr "拿好了的，随你便的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That was a good exchange.
msgid "For a card an' a wink, eh?"
msgstr "为了卡片的和闪闪金属的，对吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How come that dude is selling medieval gear in addition to all those guns?"
msgstr "How come that dude is selling medieval gear in addition to all those guns?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem to have a bunch of blueprints.  Can you tell me more about those?"
msgstr "你这里好像有不少蓝图。你能和我谈谈它们吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you anything more back there?"
msgstr "你们后面还有些什么吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It's a bit of a surprise, isn't it?  Before we came here, we were in a
#. place about 600 years earlier in time, or so.  We landed in the middle of a
#. war that turned wrong when the dead started joining back in.  Truth be
#. told, not a very unusual situation.  The Enemy makes us fight.  By and by,
#. we came in, and by then the killing fields were ready for us to harvest
#. their bronze.  It's not Avalonian steel, but it's a good strong metal for
#. stopping a nibbling mouth, so we kept some of their armor and weapons to
#. trade.
msgid ""
"That be a right welcher, eh?  Afore us'n were to this land, the preface were "
"on a half-score century by the reckonin'.  Landed us in amidst of a war'd "
"turned wrong, for an' as the dead had come back in.  By the butcher's block, "
"not much an unusual case, really.  The Enemy makes us fight.  By an' by, we "
"came in, an' by then the killin' fields were plump and ready to harvest the "
"bronze.  'Tain't no steel-of-the-lake, but 'tis a good dross metal for "
"holdin' off a nibblin' mouth, so we kept a few o' their vestments an' "
"stickers for to trade."
msgstr ""
"这有点令人吃惊，不是吗？在我们来到这里之前，我们在时间点往前600 "
"年的地方大概。我们直接出现在了一场因为死者重新加入而陷入失控的战争中。说真的，这不是什么很不寻常的情况。敌人迫使我们战斗。渐渐的，我们掌控了局势，而那时杀戮"
"场已经准备好让我们缴获了它们的青铜资源。这些武器不是什么湖中玄铁，但也是一种能够阻挡啃咬嘴巴的坚固​​金属，所以我们留下一些盔甲和武器来做交易。（注：特殊语"
"言，不作翻译。）"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, you've got a discerning eye.  They're the result of many years of
#. work.  We've been fighting the Enemy for a long time, and over the years
#. we've worked out some armor for the job.  Keeps you going a bit longer in
#. the field, if you ask me.  I keep some of the parts in stock, but you'll
#. have to put it together yourself.
msgid ""
"Ah, a real monger's eye, ye be.  Them's the mettle o' many a year of trials.  "
"Us'n've been clashin wi' the Enemy for a long an' then, an' o'er the turns "
"us've worked out some vestments for the job.  Keep's a walker walkin' longer, "
"an I'm ken.  This'n keeps some o' the parst in an' around, but ye'd be tassed "
"to make the vestment with the grease o' your own brow."
msgstr ""
"啊，你的眼睛敏锐的。它们的多年试验结果的。我们与敌人战斗了很长一段时间，多年来我们为此研制盔甲的。它会让走路人走更久的，我记下的。一些零件我这里有的，但你得"
"自己组装的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What makes your specific armor so great?"
msgstr "你的这套盔甲为什么这么棒？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why do I have to make it myself?"
msgstr "为什么我要自己组装？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are your lockers full of medieval gear?"
msgstr "为什么你的储物柜里塞满了中世纪的装备？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This and that, you know.  It's made for a traveling scavenger, you see.
#. What I mean is, it's well suited to carry around whatever you pick up in
#. the wastelands, without making it too hard to get around nor giving any
#. easy handholds for scrambling arms.  That, and I'd say it's as tough as
#. nails.
msgid ""
"This 'n that, an I'm ken.  It be made for a fine wander, beladen with the "
"goods o' the hunt, y'see.  By which I'm to say, 'tis well suited to carry all "
"ye can wrest from the cold arms o' the deadlands, without troublin' your gait "
"nor makin' it easy for the cold clutch o' the scrabblin' arm.  Be an' it is "
"tough as a tarket's nut, I'd razz."
msgstr ""
"这个那个的，你知道的。你看，它是为旅行的拾荒者设计的。我想说的，它非常适合携带你在冰冷死地里捡到的东西的，而不会让你太难四处走动的，也不会让手臂容易抓住的。"
"这就像钉子一样坚硬的，我理解了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It's a simple matter of how we teleport.  Our clothes are often made from
#. cloth and hides from wherever we visit, and our teleporter tears living
#. stuff apart here and there when we travel.  Some can be saved if we take
#. care, but there's no room to store nearly enough extra.  That, and our
#. fabricators are always busy, no time to waste on stuff we don't need for
#. ourselves.
msgid ""
"'Tis as simple as comes to a wobble.  Our vestment be oft made from the fine "
"clothes and hides of the land, and our jibber tears the stuff o' life apart "
"here and there when us'n travel.  For as some can be saved if care be taken, "
"there be no case to store nigh enough o' this.  That, an' our manuc-makers "
"run as hot as a sunstone, no spit'n taste for that which we don't use "
"usselves."
msgstr ""
"这是和摇摇门一样简单问题的。我们衣物都是用我们所到之处的布料和毛皮做成的，穿越世界时，摇摇门会把活的东西撕碎得到处都是的。如果我们小心的话，有些可以剩下来的"
"，但是没有足够空间储存多余东西的。我们的制造商总是很忙的，没法浪费在自己不需要的东西上的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ HEH, you can't get enough of old Rubik's merchandise, eh?  Sure as hell,
#. come back in <interval>.
msgid ""
"HEH, ye c'nnae get enough o' ol' Rubik's merchandise, eh?  Sure as 'ell, come "
"back in <interval>."
msgstr "嘿，你的对老鲁比克的商品怎么看都不够的，嗯？当然可以的，在过<interval>后回来的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You can surely try.  I'm not the greatest speaker, and I won't just chat
#. forever for free, you know.
msgid ""
"Sure as you c'n try.  Us're not the greatest yarker, nor do it all for "
"gratis, kennit."
msgstr "你當然可以試著聽懂。我不是最會說話的，而且我也不會沒事跟你聊一整天，懂嗎。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Hey, can I ask you something first?
msgid "Oy, c'n I bark you summat first?"
msgstr "嗨，我的先能问你的问题的么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Like, ask me a question?  Sure, I guess."
msgstr "呃，问我一个问题？当然可以，我想。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Know where I can find any work?"
msgstr "你知道我在哪能找到活干吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No.  I'm too busy to answer your questions, you're supposed to answer mine.  "
"<end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""
"No.  I'm too busy to answer your questions, you're supposed to answer mine.  "
"<end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Of course, what can I do for you?
msgid ""
"Sure as can,\" the gravelly voice takes on an unmistakeable 'customer "
"service' tone.  \"What'll ye tass this'n for?"
msgstr "当然可以的，”沙哑的声音中带着明显的“客服”语气：“能为你做的什么的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'm ready to try becoming a cyborg now."
msgstr "我想我已经准备好尝试变成改造人了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any chance you could help me get some of those sweet bionic upgrades?"
msgstr "你能不能帮我做一些可爱的生化插件升级？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be willing to sell some of your robots?"
msgstr "你愿意卖掉你的一些机器人吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you help me with CBM surgery?"
msgstr "你能帮我做CBM手术吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Can you turn me into a cyborg RIGHT NOW?  I'm a developer for this game, you "
"know."
msgstr "你能*现在*就把我变成一个机器人吗？你知道，我是这个游戏的开发者。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Actually, I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Business before pleasure.  What do you need?
msgid "Aye, business afore, 'tis said.  What'll ye tass to ol' Rubik?"
msgstr "是的，先做生意的，说过了的。你的要老鲁比克做什么的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do the Exodii have any work I could do?"
msgstr "流亡族这里有我能做的工作吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've brought the anesthetic for you.  Can you help me out?"
msgstr "我给你带来了那些麻醉剂。现在你能帮我吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I paid a visit to the bunker."
msgstr "我去过那个地堡了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I found the warehouse."
msgstr "我找到那间仓库了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nah, mate, still operatin'."
msgstr "Nah, mate, still operatin'."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Ok.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Give me a second, and I'll bring them here.
msgid "Gimme spek, 'n  fetch 'em 'ere."
msgstr "Gimme spek, 'n  fetch 'em 'ere."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Of course, it is time for us to talk."
msgstr "Of course, it is time for us to talk."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Player sees NPC spawns in an effect
msgid "Rubic leads a person to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's see what I get."
msgstr "Let's see what I get."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It is time to put this body to rest."
msgstr "It is time to put this body to rest."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Let me see.  Will do what I can for a coin.
msgid "Lemme poke.  Will tass what ye can for a shiny."
msgstr "Lemme poke.  Will tass what ye can for a shiny."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Prototype Cyborg] Can you help this guy it seems like they have lost their "
"mind?"
msgstr ""
"[Prototype Cyborg] Can you help this guy it seems like they have lost their "
"mind?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Broken Cyborg] Can you save my buddy who looks a bit rough around the edges, "
"but they still haven't flatlined?"
msgstr ""
"[Broken Cyborg] Can you save my buddy who looks a bit rough around the edges, "
"but they still haven't flatlined?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, forget it's not my problem."
msgstr "Actually, forget it's not my problem."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ For this one, I can pull out their CBM and give any working to you, or I
#. can just take out broken bits so that they will still be able to use the
#. rest of stuff in them.  Alternatively, why don't you just give them to me?
#. I surely can help them adjust to life as a cyborg.
msgid ""
"Fer this 'un, I can yank out their bits 'n give 'em to ya, or I can jus' take "
"out the busted pieces so they can still use th' rest o' stuff in 'em. "
"Elsewise, why don't ya jest give 'im to me?  I reckon I can turn 'im into a "
"right useful worker."
msgstr ""
"Fer this 'un, I can yank out their bits 'n give 'em to ya, or I can jus' take "
"out the busted pieces so they can still use th' rest o' stuff in 'em. "
"Elsewise, why don't ya jest give 'im to me?  I reckon I can turn 'im into a "
"right useful worker."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[$300] Take everything from him and if there is something useful, put it "
"aside for me."
msgstr ""
"[$300] Take everything from him and if there is something useful, put it "
"aside for me."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200$] Just remove broken bits so they can control themselves."
msgstr "[200$] Just remove broken bits so they can control themselves."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[95$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  Just bring my buddy back."
msgstr "[95$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  Just bring my buddy back."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They are all yours.  [Adds 200$]"
msgstr "They are all yours.  [Adds 200$]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This one can't be saved, too much brain rotted.  But I can salvage bits
#. from them or repurpose them for walker, or just cut out rot and neural
#. interface so you can bury them proper.
msgid ""
"This 'unwon't be twitching', too much grey lost to dead.  But ye can salvage "
"bits from 'em or born 'em for a walker, or just cut out the rot 'n grey link "
"so ya can miss 'em proper."
msgstr ""
"This 'unwon't be twitching', too much grey lost to dead.  But ye can salvage "
"bits from 'em or born 'em for a walker, or just cut out the rot 'n grey link "
"so ya can miss 'em proper."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200$] Pull out CBM if he can't use it, I can."
msgstr "[200$] Pull out CBM if he can't use it, I can."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[25$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  He deserves a burial."
msgstr "[25$] Pull everything out, you can keep what works.  He deserves a burial."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They are all yours.  [Adds 150$]"
msgstr "They are all yours.  [Adds 150$]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "'Ow long's it been since the mess happened?"
msgstr "这里的混乱的开始多久了的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Tell them.]"
msgstr "[告诉他们。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank ye.  When you an' Rubik first met, how long'd it been since the mess "
"begun?"
msgstr "谢谢你的。第一次鲁比克见到你的，混乱的开始有多久了的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Lovely!  Benzete (this is a name) is going to be beside themselves,
#. that's for sure.  I mean, they'll be really happy.  This is their first
#. jump, and it's a lucky one.
msgid ""
"Lovely!  Benzete's gonna be a pair, that's a track!  I mean, they'll be right "
"happy.  This is their first jump, and it's a flappin' duck."
msgstr "太棒了的！本泽特可以和它成对的，那是新路的！我意思的，他们的会很高兴的。这将是他们的第一次跳跃的，像会飞鸭子一样的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What makes it such a good jump?"
msgstr "什么样的跳跃才算的上是好的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who is Benzete?"
msgstr "本泽特是谁？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ As I recall, we were talking about Benzete and how this is a great jump
#. for their first time.
msgid "So 'twere an I recalt, us're yarkin' of Benzete an' their great first jump."
msgstr "我的想起来的，我们的再谈本泽特的第一次跳跃的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We've got to leave the old world before it gets too worn out, you see,
#. and find a nice fresh one on the other side.  Your deadland is as fresh as
#. it gets.
msgid ""
"Us gotta leave the old world afore it's worn right to the gums, an y'ken, and "
"find a nice twitchy one on t'other side.  Your deadland be a brand shiny"
msgstr "我们的离开旧世界的在被侵蚀穿前的，唰一下的，找到一个新的活生生的另一边的。你的死乡是闪亮新的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not following that at all."
msgstr "我一点也听不明白。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 9] So you mean, we have a nice, freshly dead world for you to visit?"
msgstr "[智力 9] 所以你是說，我們有個很棒的，全新的死人世界供你們拜訪？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ No worries.  I mean, the Enemy is new here, and we have a bit of safe
#. time ahead of us before we have to jump away again.
msgid ""
"Neverken.  Right and so, the Enemy is new here, and us'n have a few good "
"hours in the sun beforenext the jump."
msgstr "没关系的。正常的，敌人的是新来的，我们的还有阳光下的好几个小时才能下一次跳跃的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, you mean you got here early in the Cataclysm.  Why is that so good?"
msgstr "哦，你是说你们在大灾变中很早就到了这里。这有什么好的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's a part of it, sure, but this is nice for other reasons, and much
#. better than our last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are
#. really useful to us.
msgid ""
"That be a part an' switch, but this be'n nice for all, overtop the last jump "
"by heads.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings, us'n gets a fine change on "
"that."
msgstr "这是一个部分，一种转变，但这是不好的所有，超过了我们的最后一跳的。在有喷喷的轰轰的他乡的，我们的很好改变了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know what fusillies and mobbings are."
msgstr "我完全听不懂什么喷喷的轰轰的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's exactly it!  This is nice for many reasons, and much better than
#. our last jump.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings are really useful to
#. us.
msgid ""
"You kennit rightly!  That and this be'n nice for all, overtop the last jump "
"by heads.  Otherlands with fusillies and mobbings, us'n gets a fine change on "
"that."
msgstr "你的很懂的。这是一个部分，一种转变，但这是不好的所有，超过了我们的最后一跳的。在有喷喷的轰轰的他乡的，我们的很好改变了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Wait, am I following this right?  You're from a place where this happened "
"before, and you escaped to our world?"
msgstr "等等，我理理思路好吗？你说来自一个以前发生过这种事的世界，然后你逃到了我们的世界？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, yeah.  Lots of places have different words for those.  A fusilly is a
#. weapon that fires a bullet at high speeds using propellant.  A mobbing is a
#. big metal box that's moved around by an internal explosion.  Do you get it?
msgid ""
"Oh, rights.  Many lands be'd assert on thosun's.  A fusilly, she's a weapon, "
"shoots a shot at high speeds usin' bang.  A mobbing, he's a grand box o' "
"metal, pushed by burnin' and boomin' from wit'in, kennit?"
msgstr "哦，是的。许多世界都有这些东西的。喷喷的，她是一种武器，用砰的一声高速射击。轰轰的，他是一个巨大的金属盒子，由燃烧推动，里面轰轰的，懂了没有的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 7] Sounds like you mean a fusilly is a gun, and a mobbing is a car?"
msgstr "[智力 7]听上去喷喷的是把枪，而轰轰的是一辆车？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, I'll put that in the dictionary.  Here's a token of my gratitude
#. for your explanation.
msgid ""
"Right so, us'n'll write it in the dicky.  Here, a shiny brass farthing for "
"crossin' the nation."
msgstr "对的对的，那么我们的就记下来了的。在这里，一个闪亮的铜币，用来横穿这个国度的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Now that we've sorted that out, I have to ask.  You're from a place where "
"this happened before, and you escaped to our world?"
msgstr "既然我们已经解决了这个问题，我必须问一下。你说来自一个以前发生过这种事的世界，然后你逃到了我们的世界？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ They're an otherlander from around three jumps ago, a real optimistic
#. greenhorn.  They're really interested in how we do tracking, you see?
msgid ""
"Them's an otherlander from thrice jumps an' change, wide as the sky.  They's "
"got happily on sommat for the tracking, you ken?"
msgstr "他们的是来自三次跳跃外的他乡人的，像天空一样宽的。他们的很高兴能用上了新东西，懂了没有的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I… didn't really follow that."
msgstr "我……真的听不懂。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Like an apprentice to the old tracker.
msgid ""
"Hmm.  They… planned out the last jump?  Like as an apprentice to the ol' "
"sexten."
msgstr "嗯，他乡人的……计划了上一次跳跃的？就像一个六十多岁的老学徒的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, like a navigator?"
msgstr "哦，像个领航员一样？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Sure, that word is fine, I think.
msgid "Sure an' that's a fine enough word, an I'm ken."
msgstr "当然，这个词很好的，我记下的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You said this was an especially good jump?"
msgstr "你之前说这次跳跃得特别好？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, you could say that.  We're from otherlands, most of the time.  Not
#. otherworlds though.  Too risky bringing those monsters into our safe haven.
msgid ""
"Yeah, you could call us as it.  Us're from otherlands mostlike.  Not "
"otherworlds though.  Too risky bringin' them squelchies into the fold."
msgstr "是的，你的可以这样称呼我们的。我们像是来自他乡的。但不是他界的。太冒险了，像把他们带进羊圈的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know the difference between otherlands and otherworlds."
msgstr "我不知道他乡和他界有啥区别。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, that's a big question.  Otherworlds are how you got those ugly bug-
#. creatures around here, you know?  Walking plants, talking mushroom, stuff
#. like that.  Otherlands are closer related.  I'm from Earth, just a
#. different Earth.  You shouldn't be asking what the Exodii are doing in
#. Earth, because some of us are feeling pretty at home here, I think.  You
#. should be asking what we're doing hanging out in your part of town.
msgid ""
"Sure an that's a biggun'.  Otherworlds be the wherefore o' them uggo buggers "
"you got round and here, eh?  Walkin' plants and talkin' mushrooms and "
"whatlike.  Otherlands be tassed more of a kinship.  I be from Earth, but my "
"Earth be differed.  So you's shouldno be asked what the Exodii is doin' on "
"Earth, because some is feelin' of us fine an' fine at home, an I'm ken.  "
"You's should be askin' what the Exodii is doin' razzin up your green and "
"brown."
msgstr ""
"当然，区别大了的。他界就是你这里的那些可恶家伙来的，嗯？行走植物的，说话蘑菇之类的。他乡更像是亲属关系。我来自地球的，但我的地球是不同的。所以你的不应该被问"
"到流亡族来地球上做什么，因为有些人觉得我们在家里很好的，我记下的。你的应该问问流亡族为清除绿色和棕色做了什么。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK then, what are you meaning with 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "好吧，那么，你说\"清除绿色和棕色\"是什么意思？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your own world."
msgstr "和我说说你们来的世界。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah.  Home.  That's a long time gone, you know?  Yours isn't too
#. different.  I… don't think I want to talk about it.  I've changed too much
#. between then and now."
msgid ""
"*becomes distant for a moment.  \"Ah.  Home.  It were a long time gone, "
"kennit.  Your'n be not too far.  This'n… I don't think I want to talk 'bout "
"it.  Too much metal atwixt now an' then.\""
msgstr "*走神了一瞬间。\"啊，家乡。已经离开很久了的，你懂了没的。和你的差不太远的。这……我想我不想谈论它。现在和那时有太多的金属打卷了。\""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's rough, maybe we should talk about something else."
msgstr "听上去很糟糕，也许我们该换个话题。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you meaning with 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "你说\"清除绿色和棕色\"是什么意思？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you come to be made of metal like this?"
msgstr "你是怎么变成全金属做的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I realized that it was a no-brainer question.  There was only one other
#. option, you see, if I didn't join the Exodii.
msgid ""
"Us'n saw this were a pidgeon's road, I'd razz.  Only one way, I'm ken, if I'm "
"not to join the rank an' file."
msgstr "我的看到这问题是个没脑袋的，我理解了的。只有一条路的，我记下的，如果我没早就加入他们的行列的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think I know what you mean.  The only way to survive is to… \"upgrade\".  "
"Can you help me with that?"
msgstr "我想我知道你的意思。活下去的唯一方法是……\"升级\"。你能帮我吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Robot?  What does that word mean?  Hang on.  …Ah, an automate?  No, I'm
#. as flesh and blood as you are, encased in a shell of metal and wire.  Not
#. as much flesh as there used to be.  The wire is mixed and woven into the
#. flesh, all as one, you see.
msgid ""
"Robot?  What assert is f'r it?  Ahold…\"  Rubik stops for a moment, as if "
"thinking.  \"Ah, an automate?  No, this'n be flesh 'n blood as ye be, encased "
"in a shell o' metal an' wire.  Not so much flesh as there were.  The wire is "
"amixed an' afloat with the flesh, all as one, kennit.\""
msgstr ""
"\"机器人？那又是什么？等等……\"鲁比克停了一会儿，好像在思考。\""
"啊，一台自动机器？不，这是你的血肉之躯，被包裹在金属和电线的外壳里。没有那么多肉的。电线和肉混在一起，就像一个整体，你懂了没的。\""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 9] So you're a cyborg of some kind?  That's awesome.  How do I become a "
"cyborg?"
msgstr "[智力 9] 所以你是某種生化人囉？太棒了。我要怎麼成為一個生化人？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I don't have any idea what you mean.  You're kind of a robot, but you're also "
"flesh and blood?"
msgstr "我完全聽不懂你的意思。你是某種機器人，但是也是由血肉組成的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you meaning 'razzing up our green and brown'?"
msgstr "你说\"清除绿色和棕色\"是什么意思？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, that's the basic explanation.  A bit of both now, but I used to be
#. just like you.
msgid ""
"Yeah, that be the soggy leaves, an I'm ken.  A bit o' both, but Rubik were "
"once as a kin, to you be."
msgstr "是的，那是湿漉漉的树叶，我记下的。两者都有一点，但对你来说，鲁比克曾经是亲戚的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This is confusing.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "This is confusing.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ A junker base, obviously.  A jury-rigged mess.  We'll pack it up and
#. leave eventually.
msgid ""
"A junker base, innit?  Pile o' gamp.  Us'll pack it up and sing along soon "
"enough."
msgstr "一个垃圾基地，不是吗？成堆成堆的杂物。我们的很快就会收拾好，然后一起吟唱。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pack it up?  How can you pack up something like this?"
msgstr "收拾？你怎么能把这样么大的东西打包收拾起来？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Soon?  How long will you still be here?"
msgstr "马上？你们还会在这里呆多久？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ The otherlands we were in before had only little time left, so we can't
#. say for sure.  But this land is as fresh as it can be.
msgid ""
"Yon aforetime otherland, 'twere a right soggy biscuit.  This'n be crisp an' "
"fresh yet.  Us'n'll try as might stay a fair tick."
msgstr "在以前的他乡里，只剩下湿漉漉的饼干的。既不脆也不新鲜的。我们会试着保持相当长滴答响的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to know you will be here for a while."
msgstr "很高兴知道你会在这里待一段时间。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ To understand how, you've gotta think eleven-dimensionally.  We'll open
#. up a gate and teleport out, the same as we came.
msgid ""
"For an' how, ye be needin' to think wi' them elevens o' directions, kennit?  "
"Us'll open a gate an' wibble-an-wobble.  Same as us came."
msgstr "怎么你的需要如何思考他们的十一个方向，懂了没有的？我们会打开一扇门，摇摇晃晃的。和我们来时一样的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, good question.  Enough cybernetic implants can keep someone from
#. coming back as a zombie, but it's not a sure thing.  Some come back anyway,
#. and some just don't have enough cybernetics.  Most of them aren't full
#. Exodii like old Rubik, they're more our friends - like you.  Sooner or
#. later we'll get out there, put them down, and bring their parts back for
#. cleaning.
msgid ""
"'Tis a good an' yark, sooth.  Them as can have the metal deep in, can be "
"saved for the risen, but it b'ain't a sure course.  Some as comes back "
"anyway, an' some be too much flesh.  The grander lot are no Exodii like ol' "
"Rubik, most be friends more kin to thyself.  Us'll hearken out and trundle "
"home the pieces for a scrub-and-bucket."
msgstr ""
"'Tis a good an' yark, sooth.  Them as can have the metal deep in, can be "
"saved for the risen, but it b'ain't a sure course.  Some as comes back "
"anyway, an' some be too much flesh.  The grander lot are no Exodii like ol' "
"Rubik, most be friends more kin to thyself.  Us'll hearken out and trundle "
"home the pieces for a scrub-and-bucket."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So you use these cybernetics to prevent zombification, but they don't work "
"perfectly?  Why not?"
msgstr "所以你们所用这些CBM可以防止丧尸化，但它们并不完美？为什么不呢？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I don't think I'm the best to explain that, but I'll do my best.  Our
#. technology might seem pretty high-tech and well made to you, but on the
#. inside I'm still mostly human meat bound up in wires and steel.  Nobody's
#. left that remembers exactly how it all goes, and much of it is cobbled
#. together from a few different dimensions.  It's a miracle they work as well
#. as they do, but somehow it's actually pretty functional.  Still, it can be
#. hard to know exactly what could go wrong.  The ones who come back as
#. zombies, they're generally less well made than me.  Some even did their own
#. cybernetic conversions, and didn't exactly follow best practices.
msgid ""
"Rubik's not the finest dandy to yark it, an I'm ken, but this'n'll do best as "
"can.  Ol' Rubik an' the stompy-clanker gang be shiny an' fine as can be, for "
"y'see so well, but on the wind-up, the guts be nigh so fleshy as they were "
"afore, twixt as they be with wire and steel.  Ain't none so left as remembers "
"precise how it all goes, and much is boggled from bits and drabs o' a dozen "
"elsewheres.  'Tis a marked fine they work at all, though work they do, and "
"nicely.  Still, 'tis hard to know what'll crumple out from the can.  Those as "
"return, they be… less well made as ol' Rubik.  Some as did work themselves, "
"even, and mayhap against the good old ways."
msgstr ""
"鲁比克并不是最好的球员的，我知道的，但他会尽力做到最好。老鲁比克和跺脚叮当的则尽可能地闪闪发光的，因为你看得很好的，但最终，内脏几乎和以前一样肉质的，就像它"
"们用电线和钢铁一样柔软的。没有人能准确地记得这一切是如何进行的，还有很多事情都是从其他十几个他乡的点点滴滴中拼凑出来的，但它们能工作的，还有做得很好的。尽管"
"如此，很难知道会从罐子里挤出来什么的。那些回来了的，它们……不如老鲁比克做得好的。有些甚至自己也在工作的，可能会不是旧的好方法的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You seem to have a lot of standardized robotic helpers, like those quads.  Is "
"that a different thing?"
msgstr "你似乎有很多标准化的机器人助手，比如那些四足机器人。它们属于另外一类吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*'s tone changes slightly, sounding a bit pained.  \"Ah, them be an "
"in-between, more machiner.  Us'n use the softer bits o' other critters for "
"them, an' there be a manufactory for the walker.  A hard but needed choice.\""
msgstr ""
"*的语气略有变化，听起来有点痛苦：“啊，它们是介于两者之间的，更机械性的。我们用其他的柔软部分来代替它们，还有一个制造两脚的工厂的。它们是艰难但必要的选择的"
"。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How long does it take you to make one of these walkers?"
msgstr "你们造一台这样的机器人需要多长时间？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I buy one of your machines?"
msgstr "我能买一台你们的机器人吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Faster than you might guess, but it can still take a while, the hardest
#. part is sourcing the materials for one.  We've got printers that make the
#. body, and others that make the tools and equipment the walker will use.
#. Some of the special parts have to be manufactured by hand, so we have a
#. small team that does that.  Right now, it's very slow, we're still setting
#. up our operations.
msgid ""
"Blinker than a bat, but downer than a cat.  Razzin' up the bits be a trick "
"and some.  The draw-make automates can manufactorize the outer shell, and "
"there be automates for the most o' the tools.  Some bits be more a breakfast "
"o' rats, an' for them, us'n has some artisanals.  Us'n b'ain't on the solid "
"now, so 'tis a longer down."
msgstr ""
"比蝙蝠更闪亮，但比猫更令人沮丧。拼凑起这些碎片是需要技巧的。绘图可以自动制造外壳的，而且大多数工具都是自动化的。有些东西更像是老鼠的早餐，对它们来说，我们也"
"有手工匠的。我们现在不是实心了的，所以下降的时间更长。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I don't know about that.  Each one we make is very important to our
#. operations here, and they're extremely expensive.  I might be able to sell
#. you one later, but not right now."
msgid ""
"*sounds thoughtful.  \"This'n can't make a call o' the quarter.  The stompers "
"be a king's necklace, and the manufactory don't run on dreams.  Mayhap when "
"us'n be more on the solid, but for the tick and tumble, no.\""
msgstr ""
"*sounds thoughtful.  \"This'n can't make a call o' the quarter.  The stompers "
"be a king's necklace, and the manufactory don't run on dreams.  Mayhap when "
"us'n be more on the solid, but for the tick and tumble, no.\""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Yeah, we're always in need of some help around here.  Here's the list
#. I've got for stuff like this.
msgid ""
"*pulls out a sheaf of mismatched papers, and leafs through the pages for a "
"second.  Their broad metallic fingers look surprisingly deft and delicate, "
"and incongruous on the otherwise unremarkable looseleaf.  \"Aye, an' there's "
"room for a pop-an-work roun' here.  Rubik's got tassed a lissy, right and "
"clean"
msgstr ""
"*拿出一捆大大小小的纸片，翻阅了几张。他的那些金属手指虽粗壮却异常灵巧，在那堆不起眼的合页纸片里显得极不协调。“是的，这里有帮工的空缺的，鲁比克有个列表的，"
"清晰明了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  Right and so, mayhap ye should first see about that escoltin'.\""
msgstr "。是的，也许你的应该先看看那个护卫的。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but for the right-an-quick, this'n has nothin' t'be tassed for ye.\""
msgstr "，但为了正确且快速的，这个现在没有什么可以为你做的。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  How'd ye be twigged by a pop-an-squeak?  Or as y'r tassed, a treasure "
"hunt?\""
msgstr "。你觉得被砰的一声吱吱叫弄到怎么样的？还是像你说的那样，寻宝的？”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  How'd ye be twigged by a quick an' round, a nice escoltin' out to a place "
"sommat of curiosity?\""
msgstr "。你觉得来一次快速的轮次怎么样，一次漂亮的护卫的去个充满有趣地方的？”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like you're saying a job?  That's what I'm looking for.  Tell me more."
msgstr "听起来，你是说有个活儿给我？这正是我要找的。具体是？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not interested in anything right now.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "I'm not interested in anything right now.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Sure you can, at least a bit.  I'll do my best to speak your Anglic, but
#. seeing as we're from otherlands and all, it's not that simple.
msgid ""
"Sure as ye can, at least sommat.  Us'n'll try as we might to parley your "
"Anglic, but so ye kennit as us be from otherlands and all, it ain't that "
"simple."
msgstr "你當然能，至少能聽懂一點。我會盡我所能的說好你們的語言的，但你要知道我們是從異地來的，這沒有你想的那麼簡單。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT or PER 7] How come you speak English, or uh, 'Anglic' like that?"
msgstr "[智力/感知 7] 你说的英语，呃，\"英吉利语\"，怎么是这个腔调？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, right and so.  Each and every.  We wander, we make do.  It's a "
"livin'."
msgstr "哦，是的，没错的。每一个的。我们流浪的，我们将就的。一种生活方式的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What drove you out?"
msgstr "是什么把你们赶出来了？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Same as you, I'd guess.  The Enemy.  The dead.
msgid "Same as you will be, an I'm ken.  The Enemy.  The dead."
msgstr "和你的一样，我记下的。敌人的。死人的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just so, aye.  Again an' again, this'n has seen it.  Too many times."
msgstr "就是这样的，是的。一次又一次的，这个看到了的。太多次了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know what's going on?  What caused all this?"
msgstr "你知道发生了什么事吗？是什么导致了这一切？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is it always like this?  What's going to happen to us?"
msgstr "总是这样吗？我们会怎么样？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You want to get religious, eh?  I can't tell you for sure, but the people
#. who claim to know, they talk about the Enemy.  Most folks have a fairy tale
#. like that, I think.  A monster from ancient memory, returned.  I don't know
#. much about that, but something makes those bodies walk and moan, and it
#. doesn't seem to be anything human.  How it gets in, well, that's anyone's
#. guess.  It can come the way we came, through a portal, but it doesn't
#. always.  How it was for your world, I can't tell you.
msgid ""
"F'r to wax religious, eh?\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik pauses for a while.  When they start talking again, their voice is "
"slow and more serious than usual.*\n"
"\n"
"This'n can't tell ye, rightly, but those what have a bottle an' a cork what "
"fits it, they yark about the Enemy.  Most folks got a story like that in "
"their ol' hearth-tales, an I'm ken.  A bad way, from times old, come back.  "
"Ol' Rubik don't know much about that, but something makes them bodies walk "
"and moan, and it don't seem to be somethin' of the way o' our kin.  How it "
"gets in, well, that be anyone's for a guess.  It can come the way we came, "
"wibbling and wobbling, but it don't always.  How it be'd the end for your "
"deadland, Rubik can't say for ye."
msgstr ""
"你的想要信教的，是吗？\n"
"\n"
"*鲁比克停顿了一会儿。当他再次开始说话时，他的声音比平时缓慢而严肃。*\n"
"\n"
"没法肯定地告诉你的，但是那些声称知道的人，他们谈论的是敌人。很多人都听过这种故事的，我记下的。一个远古记忆中的怪物，回来了的。老鲁比克对此不太了解的，但有些"
"东西使这些尸体行走和呻吟，而与我们族类无关的。它是如何进入的，嗯，随大伙猜的。它和我们一样来的，摇摇门的，但并不总是的。你的世界是怎样的，我告诉不了你的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait, it can come like you did?  Did you bring this here?!"
msgstr "等等，它可以像你那样来？是你把它带来的吗？！"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No!  Bluster an' clouds, no!\"  Rubik's voice comes haltingly, as if they are "
"picking their words with unusual care for clarity.  \"We done a few things "
"what Rubik don't like to pickle an'… to think about, but never that!  We came "
"after the fall, long after.  Always.\""
msgstr ""
"不的！咆哮和乌云，不的！\""
"鲁比克的声音断断续续，仿佛他在小心翼翼地挑选自己的话语，以求清晰无误。“我们做过一些鲁比克不喜欢记和……想的事情的，但绝对不是那样的！我们是在陷落之后来的，"
"这一切之后的。总是这样的。”"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is a deadland, you see.  Take a moment and look around, know what I
#. mean?  What's left for you?  The dead will be in the fields, the forests,
#. all over the world.  Anything that walks, they'll make it so it doesn't,
#. and most will come back as undead.  Those that don't, the Enemy will change
#. them as well.  Every deadland is the same.  You've years and more to go,
#. but one way or another, this place is dead.  Though, as far as I can see,
#. you've got quite a few years to go yet.
msgid ""
"This be a deadland, kennit.  Spend a farthing at the pastor's house, d'ye "
"razz?  What be left for ye?  The dead'll be in the fields, the forests, all "
"around the green and brown.  Anything what walks, they'll salt 'n fallow, and "
"most'll rise up and rejoin.  Those what don't, the Enemy twists and turns as "
"well.  Every deadland be the same.  Ye've turns and twain, but come as it "
"may, this land be dead.  Though, an I'm ken, ye've quite a few turns and "
"twain to go yet."
msgstr ""
"这是一片死地的，懂了没的。花点时间四处看看，懂了没的？还剩下什么的？死者将在田野里的，森林里的，全绿色和棕色的。任何能行走的东西，它们都会让它不行走的，大多"
"数变成不死生物回来的。如果没有，敌人也会改变他们的。每个死地都是一样的。你还有很多年的路要走的，但不管怎样，这里死地了的。不过，你还有好几年的时间的，我记下"
"的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What then?  What happens after the whole planet dies?  Could it spread to "
"other worlds from here?"
msgstr "然后呢？整个星球死后会发生什么？它能从这里传播到其他世界吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's pretty hopeless talk.  I've killed a lot of zombies, I can beat this "
"'Enemy' too."
msgstr "这真是自暴自弃的说法。我杀了很多丧尸，我当然也能打败这个\"敌人\"。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Spread, yes, through the portals, but we don't know how.  After the world
#. is down to dust, I'm long gone.  Once or twice we've send back a probe to
#. the deadlands we left behind, but none have returned.  As far as I know,
#. there's only one way it goes from here.
msgid ""
"Spread, aye, through the wibbles, but we ain't ken on how.  After the green "
"an' brown be to grey and black, so t'speak, Rubik be long gone.  On a moment, "
"we folk've sent back a lover's robe or so t'the deadlands what left, but "
"narry have returned.  An I'm ken, there be only one course from here."
msgstr ""
"是的，通过摇摇门传播的，但我们不知道如何传播的。世界尘埃落定后，鲁比克早已离去的。有一两次，我们把探测器送回了我们离开死地的，但没有回来的。我记下的，今后单"
"行路的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So traveling off-world is definitely an option.  Or getting to the ISS, maybe "
"stepping off from there."
msgstr ""
"So traveling off-world is definitely an option.  Or getting to the ISS, maybe "
"stepping off from there."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It sounds like a secure base with a safe perimeter could last a long time.  "
"Maybe forever."
msgstr "听起来像是一处防护严密的安全基地可以持续很长时间。也许直到永远。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I haven't seen many zombies underground.  Seems like it might be possible to "
"make a safe base down there."
msgstr "我在地下没见过多少丧尸。似乎有可能在那里建立一个安全的基地。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So what do you do, then?  How do you get out, and how do I do that?"
msgstr "那你怎么办？你怎么出去，我怎么出去？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ If you want to try it, I won't stop you.  In fact, I'll sell you
#. equipment that might help.
msgid ""
"If ye be champed t'try, this'n won't stop ye.  Right so, Rubik'll sell ye the "
"pieces ye might use t'do."
msgstr "如果你想试试的，不会阻止你的。事实上，鲁比克会卖给你有用装备的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You do that then.  I'll cheer for you when you stand over the vanquished
#. corpse of the devil himself.
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine.  Rubik'll clarion for ye when ye stand o'er the garried trick "
"o' Anubine hisself."
msgstr "好的好的。当你站在被征服的魔鬼尸体前，鲁比克会为你欢呼的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ I'm a lowlife from old Upper Landing, this is my way of talking.
#. Everyone from where I come from talks like this.
msgid ""
"Be an' as us're a dock climber from ol' Upper Landin', this'll be our way o' "
"yarkin'.  All an' all from our green an' brown yark like this'n."
msgstr "我是在老集材廠的底層，這就是我說話的方式。我們那裡的人都是這樣講話的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about \"ol' Upper Landing\".  What was your home like?"
msgstr "告诉我关于\"上岸\"的事。你的家怎么样？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ha!  A new part of our crew.  Signed up early on in the world we were in
#. before.  He's a really tough guy, and the node appreciates his grit.
#. (Recites some poetry), as it were.  I think he's pretty good as a military
#. commander.
msgid ""
"Ha!  A new string and beans, an I'm ken.  Latched and keyed in the bright "
"shine o' the deadland afore this'n.  He be a thing o' fire and bronze, an' "
"the node appreciates his grit.  \"A cnight of old, clade in shining steel, "
"leading the hoste onward to glorie,\" as 'twere.  This'n finds him an apt one "
"to give rede.  To command in battle, that's t'yark."
msgstr ""
"哈！一根新的绳子和豆子，我知道了的。在这之前的荒原上，他被锁住并锁住了明亮的光芒。他是一个火和青铜的东西，节点欣赏他的勇气：“一个古老的骑士，披着闪闪发光的"
"钢铁，把族人带向辉煌”，他是这么说的。这个人认为他是一个合适的人。指挥着战斗的，那就是这么说的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know, every so often you talk normally and I realize you could probably "
"drop the whole accent if you wanted to."
msgstr "你知道，偶尔听你说话也挺正常的，我觉得只要你愿意，你就能够去掉这种口音。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think I've had about enough of trying to figure out what you're talking "
"about, see you later."
msgstr "我想我已经受够了不断尝试弄清楚你说的话了，回头见。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Maybe, but where's the fun in that?  Besides, quoting poetry is one
#. thing, but changing the way I speak all the time takes a lot of practice.
msgid ""
"Mayhap, but where'd be the fun in that?  Asides, quoth poetry is one thing, "
"but changin' this'n's whole yark for always takes a lot o' practice."
msgstr "也许吧的，但这其中的乐趣在哪里？离题的话，再说一遍诗歌是一回事，但要改变这整个总是需要大量练习的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was it you were saying before, about the mission you had for me?"
msgstr "你刚刚还说了些什么，你有个任务给我对吧？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, a person can get sick of trying to piece it together.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Well, a person can get sick of trying to piece it together.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Right.  You see, it's when two compatible people randomly happen into
#. each other and take a liking to one another.  It's a bit of Anglic slang.
msgid ""
"Aye.  Ye kennit, when two of a sort happen upon each other as per chance, an' "
"find a liking to another?  'Tis a bit o' Anglic yark."
msgstr "是的。你明白的，当两个一类人碰见彼此的，并发现互相欣赏的？是一点英吉利话的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's what I thought it meant, just… nevermind.  What were you saying "
"about the job?"
msgstr "是的，这就是我想的意思，只是……算了。你对这个任务有什么能说的吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know what kind of game you're playing, but I'm out for a bit."
msgstr "我不知道你在玩什么把戏，但我要出去一会儿。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That takes me way back.  That's a bit of the old King's Landing right
#. there, you know, calling back from when I was just little.  It… ah, it's
#. really hard for me to think about those old days.  Maybe another time."
msgid ""
"*seems to become wistful for a moment.  \"Harks this'n yonder, right so.  "
"'Tis a bit o' t'ol' King's Landing right there, kennit, yarkin' from back "
"when Rubik were nigh smaller than a kelpie.  It…\"  Rubik's gravelly voice "
"falters.  \"Ah, 'tis mightily tassed to hearken back yonder.  Mayhap another "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe later then.  What were you saying about the job?"
msgstr "也许下次吧。你刚刚还提到了工作，对吧？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know, I think it'd be best if I just got going."
msgstr "你知道吗，我想我最好还是走吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Making do, making do, same as you I'd imagine.  Our last home got too
#. dead and putrid around the edges, basically.  It happens to the best of
#. them.  We caught some news that brought us along to your place here, fired
#. up the engines, and boom!  Now, quick as can be, here we are.  We got a
#. good timing this time, seems to me you'd only been dead a few days when we
#. got here.  Freshest corpse I've seen in a while.
msgid ""
"Makin' do, makin' do, same as you, an I'm ken.  Last home got a bit too dead "
"'n putrid roun' the edges, like.  Happens to the best of 'em.  Caught a "
"jibber that made us ken 'bout your place here, fired up the ol' "
"wibble-wammles and boom!  Now it's all tick-tock on a zimmer, here we be.  "
"Got a good timing this time, I razz you only been dead a few days when we "
"wobbled in.  Freshest corpse this'n's seen in a kitchen sink."
msgstr ""
"凑合的，凑合的，和你一样的，我记得的。上个家太死气沉沉的，边缘都全腐烂了的。发生在他们中最好的人身上。听到些消息指向你们这里了的，点燃了摇摇晃晃的，然后唰的"
"一声！一切都在时间的滴答声中，我们到了的。这一次时机很好的，我知道的我们进来的时候你才死了几天的。这是厨房水槽里见过的最新鲜尸体的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…what?"
msgstr "……什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT or PER 9] Where did you come from then?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[智力/感知 9]那你是从哪里来的？你是外星人还是什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything else you want from this place?"
msgstr "你还想从这里得到什么吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ We're just here to survive, you understand?  Our last world got too
#. overrun with undead.  So, we came to a new world.  This one.  If I'm not
#. mistaken, it's not so long dead around here just yet.
msgid ""
"Us're here to live and breathe, kennit?  After our last otherland got a li'l "
"too dead an' all.  So, us'n came to a new place.  This'n.  An I'm ken, it's "
"not so long dead round here jus' yet."
msgstr "我们的是来这里生活和呼吸的，懂了没的？在我们上次去的他乡后，没多久也死了的。于是，我们来到了一个新地方的。这个的。我记下的，这里还没死多久的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT or PER 7] Otherland?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[智力/感知 7]他乡是什么？你是外星人还是什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Aside from just having a safe place to live?  We're here to mine, you
#. understand.  Picking the scraps, seeing if this world has any tech worth
#. reverse engineering.  No sense letting good scraps go to waste.  If we're
#. lucky, maybe we'll get some new Exodii before we teleport out.  Pickin' up
#. the pieces of our sweet, shattered dreams, such as they are.
msgid ""
"Aside from jus' livin' in such a cozy nook?  Us be minin', ye kennit.  "
"Pickin' the scraps, seein' if for your otherland has any tech worth an "
"upside-down.  No sense lettin' good scraps go to waste.  If we're lucky, "
"pickin' a few new Exodii afore we wobble out.  Pickin' up the pieces of our "
"sweet, shattered dreams, suchlike."
msgstr ""
"除了在这样的舒适角落里生活的？我们挖矿的，你懂了的。挑废品的，看看你们的他乡是否有值得一翻的技术的。让好东西浪费掉是没有意义的。如果幸运的话，在我们的离开之"
"前挑选一些新流亡族的。重拾我们的甜蜜破碎梦想的，诸如此类的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What do you mean 'go to waste'?  The zombies aren't using the scrap, and "
"there's plenty to go around."
msgstr "\"浪费\"是什么意思？丧尸们不会使用这些废料，而且还有很多东西可以使用。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is a deadland, don't you see?  You've already got an infestation and
#. it's not going away.  There's no cure for the zombies.
msgid ""
"This'n be a deadland, an I'm ken.  You gots you a case o' the willies ain't "
"gonna sing along.  No cure for these rats and fleas."
msgstr "这里是死地的，我记下的。你还带着外壳的，心惊肉跳的，没法跟着唱的。这些老鼠和跳蚤没有治愈方法的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What the hell does that mean?"
msgstr "这到底是什么意思？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 8] Are you saying you think we're doomed?  Why would you have come here "
"if there wasn't some way to survive?"
msgstr "[智力 8] 你是说你认为我们注定要失败？如果没法生存，你们为什么还要来这里？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ It means what it means.  Your land's dead already, it's just still
#. kicking is all.
msgid "Means what it means.  Your land's a deadun', still kickin' is all."
msgstr "意思就是意思的。你的土地已经是死去土地的，虽然还在挣扎的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Are you saying you think we're doomed?  Why would you have come here if there "
"wasn't some way to survive?"
msgstr "你是说你认为我们注定要失败？如果没有办法生存，你为什么会来这里？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, we can teleport along as we need to.  We send the scrap along, then
#. the food, and shake off some baddies, you understand.  It's no good for you
#. though, it won't take too much flesh and bone.
msgid ""
"Oh, us can wobble along as needs.  Sends the scrap back, brings in the foods, "
"and shakes off a willie or three, kennit.  No good for you, won't take too "
"much meat-an'-bone."
msgstr "哦，我们可以根据需要摇一摇的。把废料送回去的，把食物带进来的，甩掉一两个坏家伙的，懂了没的。这对你的没好处的，太多肉和骨头的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well… could you help me fix that?"
msgstr "嗯……那你能帮我修一下吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait.  I thought you were still flesh and bone, under that metal."
msgstr "等等。我还以为你在这堆金属底下还有骨有肉的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Haha, not mostly, mate.  It's not worth risking the side effects, you
#. see?  I keep the parts of me that make me Rubik, but the rest is all solid.
msgid ""
"Haha, not mostly, mate.  Not worth riskin' the willies, innit?  I keep what's "
"Rubik, but the rest is all solid."
msgstr "哈哈，不多的，伙计。不值得心惊肉跳的，不是吗？我保留下是鲁比克的，但其他的都是实心的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What?  I mean, really, it seems like you're being hard to understand on "
"purpose.  What are the 'willies'?"
msgstr "什么？要我说，真的，你好像故意讲得让人听不懂。什么\"心惊肉跳\"？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh, sure, that's a fair assessment.  I mean, I do get a bit of a laugh
#. out of the look on your face sometimes.  What I'm saying is, if my body
#. were flesh and bone, the device we use to travel around dimensions would
#. rip up the meat and leave me quite a mess.  We can take a bit, but too
#. much… one time, I felt a bit of that, and I'm not in any rush to try it
#. again.
msgid ""
"Oh, sure an it's bagged in a coffer an' all that.  That is t'say, this'n does "
"get a wipe o' a grinny t'see the perplexion upon a visage, an I'm ken.*  "
"You're pretty sure you hear a faint chuckle in the metallic voice.  *What I "
"be meanin' is at, for my body were t'be meat-an'-bone, the tool what we be "
"usin' for t'travel to an' fro, it rips up the meat an' leaves it a right "
"mess.  A bit can come along for a right fun, but too much… on a time, an "
"earlier Rubik felt a spot o' those willies, an' this'n be not in the "
"farrier's hut for t'try it again."
msgstr ""
"哦，当然，这个评价挺公平的。有时候我的确能从你脸上的表情中获得不少笑的，我记下的。\n"
"\n"
"*你敢肯定自己听见那金属般的声音中有丝轻笑。*\n"
"\n"
"我想说的，如果我的身体是骨肉，我们的摇摇晃晃的装置会撕碎肉的，把我弄得一团糟的。一点点还可以受的，但多了就……有次，曾经的鲁比克感受到一点心惊肉跳的，可不想"
"再试一次了的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What?  I mean, really, it seems like you're being hard to understand on "
"purpose."
msgstr "什么？要我说，真的，你好像故意讲得让人听不懂。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Not to me it doesn't.  We didn't get it from around here though.  I bet
#. it looks pretty nice to you.
msgid ""
"Not to me it don't.  We ain't tassed from around here though.  Looks fine an' "
"fine to you I'd razz."
msgstr "对我不是的。但我们的不会在这里久待的。你的很好的，我很高兴的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT or PER 7] Not from around here?  Are you aliens or something?"
msgstr "[智力/感知 7]不在这里久待？你是外星人还是什么？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ If you've got what I need, I'm happy to call ahead and make the
#. arrangements, for a fee.
msgid ""
"If'n you're full an' plenty, this'n's happy to make the call, for a shiny "
"farthing."
msgstr "如果你的有很多的，我的很高兴完成的，只要一个闪亮的硬币的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got some stuff I'd like to install."
msgstr "我有一些东西要安装。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be able to take out one of my implants?"
msgstr "你能取出我体内植入的东西吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Mayhaps this gear will do you better than it did the scuffers wot trained "
"with it. [$400]"
msgstr ""
"Mayhaps this gear will do you better than it did the scuffers wot trained "
"with it. [$400]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy it."
msgstr "I'll buy it."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any chance I can buy gear this on layaway?"
msgstr "Any chance I can buy gear this on layaway?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If'n you survive, we can give you a fortnight and six odd days to pay us'n "
"back."
msgstr ""
"If'n you survive, we can give you a fortnight and six odd days to pay us'n "
"back."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks Rubik, I'll be back with your payment soon."
msgstr "Thanks Rubik, I'll be back with your payment soon."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right and done, don't let whatever you are going after turn you into a pork "
"loin well done.  I's expectin' you back."
msgstr ""
"Right and done, don't let whatever you are going after turn you into a pork "
"loin well done.  I's expectin' you back."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Here's the money to pay off that debt."
msgstr "Here's the money to pay off that debt."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure an' I can make you a cyborg, here an' now, since you're a developer an' "
"all."
msgstr "当然，现在我可以让你成为一个改造人，因为你是一个开发者。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Install CBM Interface] Let's do it."
msgstr "[Install CBM Interface] Let's do it."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I changed my mind.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "I changed my mind.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "I changed my mind.  <end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Oh HO!  Well, now you're speaking my language.  We can fix you up good,
#. if you're willing to pay us back.  I'll say it as clearly as I can.  If you
#. help us kill the undead, we can help you get fixed up like us, yeah.  Stuck
#. right into your flesh and bone and wired into your brain.  You understand?
#. If not, we'll ask the Great Grey to help clear it up.
msgid ""
"Oh HO!  Well, well.  Now you're yarkin' the King's Anglic.  Aye, us'n can fix "
"ye good, if'n ye're tassed to repay it in kind.  Us'll speak it as clear-like "
"as this Rubik can.  If ye'n use it to put the dead back in the ground, us'n "
"can fix ye with some goods like this, aye.  Stuck in the flesh and to the "
"bone, wired into the brain.  Ye kennit?  If no, us'll speak to the Great Grey "
"for a pint o' the ol' clarity-draught."
msgstr ""
"哦，呵呵！好吧，好吧。现在你在说国王的英吉利语了。是的，如果你的能做出等价偿还的话，我们可以给你带来好处的。我们会尽可能像鲁比克一样清楚地说出来。如果你用它"
"把死人埋回地下，我们可以用这样的东西来修理你，是的。卡进肉和骨头里，连接到大脑的。你懂了没的？如果没有，我们的可以找大灰要一品脱清爽剂的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Ah, well.  I'll file that away, so to speak.  Maybe you could bring us a
#. little more trade, and we'll fix you up as soon as possible.  The Exodii
#. won't turn away a willing convert.
msgid ""
"Ah, well.  Us'll put that into the key and lock, if'n you're ken.  Mayhap you "
"could bring us a mite and trade, and we'll see if we can fix you good soon "
"and soon.  Let no Exodii turn away a willin' Benny, and so it is."
msgstr ""
"啊，好吧。如果你记下了的，我们会把钥匙放进锁里的。也许你能给我们带来一点东西做贸易的，我们会看看我们是否能很快解决你的问题。流亡族从不赶走一个自愿的本泽特，"
"就这样的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If I just keep on killing zombies, you'll help turn me into a cyborg?  Why "
"are we still yarkin', then?  Sign me the heck up."
msgstr "如果我继续杀丧尸，你能会帮我变成一个改造人吗？那么，我们还等什么呢？给我报名吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"On second thought, I'm not sure I want to let a bunch of unfamiliar alien "
"robots do brain surgery on me."
msgstr "再想一想，我不确定我是否想让一群陌生的外星机器人给我做脑部手术。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe try that clarity-draught?"
msgstr "也许我该试试那种清爽剂？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, well, I've got some stuff I could trade right now."
msgstr "好吧，我现在有一些东西可以交易。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, maybe I'll come back when I've traded a bit more."
msgstr "好吧，也许等再多交易一些东西后，我再回来找你们。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hmm.\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik's voice becomes mechanical and distant for a moment, as if a computer "
"takes over speaking.*\n"
"\n"
"In exchange for the guarantee that you will use these gifts to combat the "
"Great Enemy, this Exodii Node is willing to provide you with a bionic module "
"command plexus, a power supply, and all the necessary infrastructure to "
"obtain further upgrades with standardized CBMs - compact bionic modules.  We "
"will require only a token fee for this service.  We will provide further "
"upgrades as purchased.  Your personal improvement serves our mutual benefit.\n"
"\n"
"*Rubik's voice takes over again.*\n"
"\n"
"Clear as a draught?"
msgstr ""
"嗯。\n"
"\n"
"*鲁比克的声音在一瞬间变得既机械而遥远，好像是电脑接管了说话一般*\n"
"\n"
"为了保证你将使用这些天赋与大敌作战，流亡族节点愿意为你提供生化模块控制电极、供电系统和所有必要的基础装置，以获得标准化CBM（紧凑型生化插件）的进一步升级。"
"我们只需要支付此服务的象征性的费用。我们将提供购买后的进一步升级。你个人的进步对我们双方都有利。\n"
"\n"
"*鲁比克的声音再次出现*\n"
"\n"
"是不是很清爽的？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why can't you talk that clearly all the time?  You have no idea how hard it "
"is to understand your accent, let alone your words."
msgstr "你为什么不能一直说得那么清楚？你不知道要听懂你的口音有多难，更不用说你的话了。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ MY accent?  You've obviously never had to listen to yourself talk.  Great
#. Grey has more important work to do, get it?  I have to keep myself useful
#. and keep Great Grey doing what it's supposed to.  Besides, talking to the
#. locals keeps me young and shines my chrome, as I see it.
msgid ""
"THIS'n's accent?  Ye've never egged y'r own yark, an' that's a fine fiddle.  "
"Great Grey has a bit o' work on it, kennit?  This'n has to keep usselves "
"useful, an' keep Great Grey doin' what it's tassed.  Asides, yarkin' to the "
"local brights keeps us young an' shines our chrome, an I'm ken."
msgstr ""
"我的口音？明显的，你的从来没有听过自己说话的。大灰还有更重要的工作要做，你的明白的？必须让我自己有用的，让大灰做它应该做的事。另外的，与当地人交谈让我保持年"
"轻的，让我光彩照人的，我记下的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Fine, whatever.  It doesn't matter, if you're gonna turn me into a horrifying "
"fusion of machine and human, sign me the heck up."
msgstr "好吧，随便吧。没关系，如果你想把我变成一个可怕的机器和人的融合体，就给我报名吧。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The more I talk to you, the more I'm not sure I want to let a bunch of "
"unfamiliar alien robots do brain surgery on me."
msgstr "我跟你说的越多，我就越不确定我是否想让一群陌生的外星机器人给我做脑部手术。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, OK.  What was it you said?  I was distracted by the voice change."
msgstr "好，好。你刚刚说了什么？我被声音的变化分散了注意力。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  Your job
#. is to bring us a bit of good tea.  Not literally 'tea' of course.  That's
#. my Anglic street slang.  I mean the stuff that puts you to sleep for
#. surgery.  The Great Grey says your word for it is 'anesthetic'.  You bring
#. us a thousand units of anesthetic, we'll fix you up with a wire and
#. everything.
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine, an' fine an' fine!  Ha!  Us'll rubber up the ol' gristle mill. "
" Yer tassed wi' bringin' us a nip o' good tea.  Not 'tea', o'course.  I'm "
"yarkin dockside Anglic here.  Us means the stuff what puts y'to sleep f'r a "
"chirurgery.  The Great Grey says y'r assert for it is 'anus fetick'.  You "
"bring us a thousand unit of 'anus fetick', us'll fix'n ye up with a wire an' "
"a tiff."
msgstr ""
"好的好的，太好的太好的！哈！我们就要给软骨老磨上橡胶了。你的工作是给我们带点好茶。当然不是字面上的\"茶\""
"。那是我的码头英吉利语的。我说的那些能让你的手术前睡觉的。大灰说用你的话叫\"马嘴鸡\"。你的给我们的带一千来，我们的会用电线和其他东西把你修理好的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "One thousand units of, uh, anesthetic, coming up.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "One thousand units of, uh, anesthetic, coming up.  I'd better start looking."
msgstr "一千份，呃，麻醉剂是吧，马上好。我这就去找。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Something's weird, I shouldn't have ever reached this dialogue option.  I'd "
"better go file a bug report."
msgstr "奇怪的事情发生了，我不应该看见这个对话。我最好去官网提交一份错误报告。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Great, great, great!  Ha!  We'll fire up the old meat grinder.  You just
#. come along with old Rubik.
msgid ""
"Fine an' fine, an' fine an' fine!  Ha!  Now as us've got the good tea, us'll "
"rubber up the ol' gristle mill.  You jus' set along with ol' Rubik."
msgstr "好的好的，太好了太好了！哈！既然我们有了好茶，我们就要用橡胶把旧的磨坊磨平的。你马上就和鲁比克在一起的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Install CBM Interface] All right.  Let's do this."
msgstr "[Install CBM Interface] All right.  Let's do this."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold on.  I need to rethink it again."
msgstr "等等。我需要重新考虑一下。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ That's a fine choice, I understand.  If you change your mind, old Rubik's
#. going to be here for a while.  You'll get to know us better, we'll get to
#. know you better, and that's going to be good all around.
msgid ""
"An' that's a fine choice, I'd razz.  If'n ye change mind, ol' Rubik's here "
"for the long an' short.  You get to know us'n better, us'n get to know you "
"better, an' that's a good tassin'."
msgstr "一项很好的选择，我理解的。如果你的改变主意的，老鲁比克会一直在这里的。你的更了解我们的，我们的更了解你的，这个的很好的选择。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*makes a stiff, bowing gesture and leads you out of the shop and down a stone "
"pathway towards one of the larger buildings in the compound.  A thick steel "
"door slides aside to reveal a gloomy, rust-dusted corridor.  At the end of "
"the corridor is a clean appearing surgical suite, not too different from any "
"other surgical suite aside from the dim lighting and the surgeon itself.  At "
"the head of the surgical table is a contraption reminiscent of an upside-down "
"spider, its multiple glistening medical limbs curling gently in eager "
"anticipation of your approach.  You have little time to question your choices "
"before you feel a sharp pinch in your left shoulder, and the world drifts "
"away.\n"
"\n"
"You awaken on a comfortable bed, your chest and throat sore but otherwise "
"well.  As the haze of anesthesia fades, you notice several tiny, sore wounds "
"on your chest and arms.  A humanoid cyborg, not Rubik, notices that you are "
"awake and wordlessly gestures you to follow, leading you back to Rubik's "
"store.\n"
"\n"
"\"Ah, an' you're with the stars 'n lights again, an I'm ken.  'Tis grand.  "
"Those wee CBMs will do ye little an fine, but they are a start.  Now us'n can "
"sell you all you like, an' help with install, should ye wish.\""
msgstr ""
"*做出一个僵硬的鞠躬姿势，领着你走出商店，沿着一条石头小径走向院子里的一座更大的建筑。一扇厚厚的钢门滑到一边，露出一条阴暗、锈迹斑斑的走廊。走廊尽头是一间外"
"观整洁的手术室，除了昏暗的灯光和外科医生本身，与其他手术室没有太大区别。在手术台的顶部是一个让人联想到倒挂蜘蛛的装置，它的多个闪闪发光的医疗机械臂轻轻地卷曲"
"，热切地期待着你的到来。你几乎没有时间去质疑你的选择，直到你感觉到左肩上的剧痛，世界渐渐远去。\n"
"\n"
"你在舒适的床上醒来，你的胸部和喉咙有些痛，但在其他方面都很好。当麻醉剂的效果渐渐消失时，你注意到胸部和手臂上有几处细小的疼痛伤口。一个改造人，不是鲁比克，注"
"意到你醒来了，无言地示意你跟随，带你回到鲁比克的商店。\n"
"\n"
"\"啊，你终于和星星在一起了的，我记下的。太棒了的。那些小小的CBM会帮你一点忙的，但它们只是开始的。现在我们的可以出售你想要的一切的，如果你想要的，还可以"
"帮助安装的。\""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So I'm a cyborg now?  I don't really feel much different."
msgstr "那么我现在是一个改造人了？我觉得没什么不同。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Thanks for the brain implants.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  Thanks for the brain implants.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#: data/mods/translate-dialogue/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ This is what you'd call a 'starter package', if I understand it.
#. Suitable to get you started, but for the really sweet parts you're going to
#. want what I'm selling.  As we get to know each other better, I'll be able
#. to get access to even more stuff.
msgid ""
"This're what ye'd razz a 'starter package', an I'm ken.  Tassed to get ye "
"started, but for the real lemony tarts you'd be wantin' what this'n's got for "
"sale.  As us'n can come to see you clairly-like, this'n can be tassed to "
"offer more an' more."
msgstr "这是你想要的\"入门包\"，我记下的。给你让你开始的，但你真正想要的柠檬馅饼，是商品的。当我的可以更清楚见到你喜欢的，可以提供更多的。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_merchant_talk_exodization.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So you can sell me more bionics, and as I get to know you better you'll have "
"more?  Mind showing me what you've got right now?"
msgstr "所以你可以卖给我更多的生化插件，当我们关系更好的时候，你能出售有更多？介意给我看看你现在有什么吗？"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "Nine"
msgstr "九"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "Weaponmaster"
msgstr "Weaponmaster"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Cyborg, type 9"
msgstr "Cyborg, type 9"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Mutation name
msgid "Exodii cyborg framework - style 9"
msgstr "Exodii cyborg framework - style 9"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster.json
#. ~ Description of mutation "Exodii cyborg framework - style 9"
msgid ""
"Your entire body is covered by a rectangular frame, that has numerous "
"supporting arms and manipulators, with decent stability.  The price of this "
"is that the weight of the entire frame is enormous, which causes the user to "
"either use dedicated tracked treads to move around, or stay immobile for a "
"large amount of time."
msgstr ""
"Your entire body is covered by a rectangular frame, that has numerous "
"supporting arms and manipulators, with decent stability.  The price of this "
"is that the weight of the entire frame is enormous, which causes the user to "
"either use dedicated tracked treads to move around, or stay immobile for a "
"large amount of time."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&What you see looks like the back of a mechanical spider, with at least a "
"dozen crude but polished metal arms coming from the enormously wide spine and "
"shoulders.  The spine of the creature, meanwhile, sits in an awkward-looking "
"chair, manipulating tools and geegaws on a wide, brightly lit workbench.  The "
"creature seems to be busy with something."
msgstr ""
"&What you see looks like the back of a mechanical spider, with at least a "
"dozen crude but polished metal arms coming from the enormously wide spine and "
"shoulders.  The spine of the creature, meanwhile, sits in an awkward-looking "
"chair, manipulating tools and geegaws on a wide, brightly lit workbench.  The "
"creature seems to be busy with something."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Wait a bit.]"
msgstr "[Wait a bit.]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#: data/mods/CrazyCataclysm/crazy_speech.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Speech from speaker aperture_potato, mon_mi_go, mon_mi_go_slaver
msgid "Hello?"
msgstr "哈囉? "

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&It doesn't react to your presence at all."
msgstr "&It doesn't react to your presence at all."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Wait for longer.]"
msgstr "[Wait for longer.]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&It seems to not hear you at all."
msgstr "&It seems to not hear you at all."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Wait in silence.]"
msgstr "[Wait in silence.]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello!?"
msgstr "Hello!?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&A few seconds later, they seem to finish whatever they were busy with and "
"turn their chair towards you.  Their front looks no less exotic than their "
"back; the abundance of metal arms are even more extraordinary next to the "
"clear lack of any legs.  What you initially thought to be a chair is simply a "
"rotating platform, sturdy enough to support the weight of the entire body of "
"the creature.  A number of cameras, which seem to be a replacement for eyes, "
"look at you motionlessly, while the forehead of the creature has the "
"surprisingly familiar sign \"IX\" painted on."
msgstr ""
"&A few seconds later, they seem to finish whatever they were busy with and "
"turn their chair towards you.  Their front looks no less exotic than their "
"back; the abundance of metal arms are even more extraordinary next to the "
"clear lack of any legs.  What you initially thought to be a chair is simply a "
"rotating platform, sturdy enough to support the weight of the entire body of "
"the creature.  A number of cameras, which seem to be a replacement for eyes, "
"look at you motionlessly, while the forehead of the creature has the "
"surprisingly familiar sign \"IX\" painted on."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who-…  Wha-…  What are you?"
msgstr "Who-…  Wha-…  What are you?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Still completely mute, it shows you something you had initially missed.  The "
"entire wall behind the workbench is full of various weapons; some as big as "
"modern rifles, a few as large as the machine guns installed on aircraft, and "
"one that looks like a dismantled tank turret.  Melee weapons were not "
"forgotten, from moderately-sized swords and clubs to war hammers twice the "
"height of a human, and what you can describe only as \"boots for mecha\".  "
"Then it points to a sign near you that shows three things: the carved "
"pictograms of coins, some sign you are not familiar with, and a pictogram of "
"a bullet - all things considered, this creature is either a weaponmaster, or "
"a weapon merchant."
msgstr ""
"&Still completely mute, it shows you something you had initially missed.  The "
"entire wall behind the workbench is full of various weapons; some as big as "
"modern rifles, a few as large as the machine guns installed on aircraft, and "
"one that looks like a dismantled tank turret.  Melee weapons were not "
"forgotten, from moderately-sized swords and clubs to war hammers twice the "
"height of a human, and what you can describe only as \"boots for mecha\".  "
"Then it points to a sign near you that shows three things: the carved "
"pictograms of coins, some sign you are not familiar with, and a pictogram of "
"a bullet - all things considered, this creature is either a weaponmaster, or "
"a weapon merchant."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Woah.  Can I buy one?"
msgstr "Woah.  Can I buy one?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They do not move and do not say anything."
msgstr "&They do not move and do not say anything."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey?  Do you understand me?"
msgstr "Hey?  Do you understand me?"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They clearly do not understand you.  It seems they do not hear you either."
msgstr "&They clearly do not understand you.  It seems they do not hear you either."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[You pull off your backpack, and start to pull out items you deem worthy of "
"trading.  The weaponmaster finally looks interested.]"
msgstr ""
"[You pull off your backpack, and start to pull out items you deem worthy of "
"trading.  The weaponmaster finally looks interested.]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be tinkering on something, but turns their chair "
"to you as you approach."
msgstr ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be tinkering on something, but turns their chair "
"to you as you approach."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be cleaning some sort of weapon, but as you "
"approach them, they signal to a bystanding worker to take the weapon, and "
"turn to you."
msgstr ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be cleaning some sort of weapon, but as you "
"approach them, they signal to a bystanding worker to take the weapon, and "
"turn to you."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be polishing some armor, but they turn towards you "
"the second you enter the room."
msgstr ""
"&The Weaponmaster seems to be polishing some armor, but they turn towards you "
"the second you enter the room."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_weaponmaster_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[With a familiar movement, you place a variety of valuables onto the counter, "
"proposing a trade.]"
msgstr ""
"[With a familiar movement, you place a variety of valuables onto the counter, "
"proposing a trade.]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You see a human-like robot walking nearby."
msgstr "&你看到一个人形机器人在附近行走。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You see a mechanical humanoid moving somewhere in a hurry."
msgstr "&你看到一个机械人形匆匆忙忙地路过。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You see some sort of robot walking in a hurry."
msgstr "&你看到某种机器人匆匆忙忙地走着。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&This robot doesn't seem to be very busy."
msgstr "&这台机器人似乎不是很忙。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Move away.]"
msgstr "[走开。]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They seem to completely ignore you."
msgstr "&它们似乎完全无视你。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They ran past you, completely ignoring your presence."
msgstr "&它们从你身边跑过，完全无视你的存在。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They don't seem to want to talk to you."
msgstr "&它们似乎不想和你说话。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&They seem to greet you, but that's it."
msgstr "&它们似乎在点头问候，但仅此而已。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/exodii_workers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How rude."
msgstr "真没礼貌。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgstr "抵达象形路标上指引的地点"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgid ""
"I found a weird pictographic sign that seemed to point towards someone "
"willing to trade."
msgstr "我发现了一个奇怪的象形路标，似乎指向某个愿意做交易的人。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgid ""
"This is a sign with a series of simple line-art pictograms showing what "
"appears to be a basic trade transaction.  A pair of hands offers a piece of "
"some kind of junk, and another pair of hands offers a small pouch in return."
msgstr "这是一个带有一系列简单线条象形图案的路标，描绘的似乎是简单交易行为。一双手捧着某种废料，另一双手捧着一个小袋子作为回报。"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"[v0.1 info] Okay I'm just gonna drop my dialect for this, it's way too much "
"for Anglic.  The Labyrinthine Structure (LS) is planned to be a sprawling "
"procedurally generated dungeon where you can fight advanced monsters and loot "
"cybernetics, both regular and weird artifact versions.  It is currently far "
"from that state.  Playtest information on the general layout and the monster "
"balance would be helpful.\n"
"\n"
"In the long run, the goal is to have a number of 'biomes' that you can reach "
"as you travel further from the origin point.  When you leave and return, the "
"dungeon resets, although in the future the devs want to have a stable 'home "
"base' you can upgrade.\n"
"\n"
"In its final form, if it ever gets there, it would have enough content that "
"you could spend an entire playthrough just exploring the labyrinth and "
"getting weird unique items that only work down there, something like the "
"backrooms mod but for mainline."
msgstr ""
"[v0.1 info] Okay I'm just gonna drop my dialect for this, it's way too much "
"for Anglic.  The Labyrinthine Structure (LS) is planned to be a sprawling "
"procedurally generated dungeon where you can fight advanced monsters and loot "
"cybernetics, both regular and weird artifact versions.  It is currently far "
"from that state.  Playtest information on the general layout and the monster "
"balance would be helpful.\n"
"\n"
"In the long run, the goal is to have a number of 'biomes' that you can reach "
"as you travel further from the origin point.  When you leave and return, the "
"dungeon resets, although in the future the devs want to have a stable 'home "
"base' you can upgrade.\n"
"\n"
"In its final form, if it ever gets there, it would have enough content that "
"you could spend an entire playthrough just exploring the labyrinth and "
"getting weird unique items that only work down there, something like the "
"backrooms mod but for mainline."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's stop breaking the fourth wall and get back to the normal conversation."
msgstr "Let's stop breaking the fourth wall and get back to the normal conversation."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You see a strangely mundane black computer screen, with a blinking green "
"cursor awaiting input.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"
msgstr ""
"&You see a strangely mundane black computer screen, with a blinking green "
"cursor awaiting input.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _</color>"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Activate exit protocol"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > skill -EXIT -@User\n"
"<color_light_green>Really exit?  You will not be able to return to the same "
"place."
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > skill -EXIT -@User\n"
"<color_light_green>Really exit?  You will not be able to return to the same "
"place."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Unlock connected doors"
msgstr "Unlock connected doors"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Lock connected doors"
msgstr "Lock connected doors"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Now all the doors are *gone*, what the hell."
msgstr "Now all the doors are *gone*, what the hell."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors unlocked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Thank you for using TempleOS.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors unlocked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Thank you for using TempleOS.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=lock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors locked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Warning: What is done cannot be undone.  This does not "
"represent a return to how things were.  You can never go back.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=lock\n"
"<color_light_green>Command accepted.\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors locked.\n"
"<color_light_green>Warning: What is done cannot be undone.  This does not "
"represent a return to how things were.  You can never go back.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Bad command or file name.\n"
"<color_light_green>What is done cannot be undone.  Please see prior user "
"warning.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Bad command or file name.\n"
"<color_light_green>What is done cannot be undone.  Please see prior user "
"warning.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "There must be some way to force the computer to do it."
msgstr "There must be some way to force the computer to do it."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock --force\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: Insufficient  confidence.\n"
"<color_light_green>Aborted: No forceable process.\n"
" @User > sudo doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Oh, is that how it will be?  Very well.\n"
"<color_light_green>Blood tax requested.\n"
"A drawer on the side of the terminal slides open, revealing a small, thin "
"needle.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&<color_light_green> @User > doorstatus --update=unlock --force\n"
"<color_light_green>Error: Insufficient  confidence.\n"
"<color_light_green>Aborted: No forceable process.\n"
" @User > sudo doorstatus --update=unlock\n"
"<color_light_green>Oh, is that how it will be?  Very well.\n"
"<color_light_green>Blood tax requested.\n"
"A drawer on the side of the terminal slides open, revealing a small, thin "
"needle.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[ Prick yourself on the needle ]"
msgstr "[ Prick yourself on the needle ]"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&As it enters your skin, the thin needle seems to pulse, greedily gulping "
"from your offered hand, and you feel abruptly dizzy and lightheaded.  It "
"feels like it took a *lot* of blood.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > Inflict --damage=lifeblood\n"
"<color_light_green>Processing contribution of reality ||||||||| 100%\n"
"<color_light_green>Nearby doors unlocked.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green> @User > _"
msgstr ""
"&As it enters your skin, the thin needle seems to pulse, greedily gulping "
"from your offered hand, and you feel abruptly dizzy and lightheaded.  It "
"feels like it took a *lot* of blood.\n"
"\n"
