msgstr "你从噩梦中惊醒过来，梦中一个看不见的狩猎者正缓慢地杀死你。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid "You awaken from a nightmare about killing those you love with your bare hands."
msgstr "你从噩梦中惊醒过来，梦中你亲手杀死了你的挚爱之人。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid "You awaken from a nightmare about being finally judged for your ill deeds."
msgstr "你从噩梦中惊醒过来，梦中你因为自己向来的恶行收到了最终审判。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You awaken from a nightmare.  Recent events had not come to pass, and you "
"were stuck in an office job."
msgstr "你从噩梦中惊醒过来，梦中最近这一切都没有发生，而你被困在一个办公室中当着文员。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You awaken from a nightmare.  This wasn't the end of the world… all those "
"innocents you've murdered."
msgstr "你从噩梦中惊醒过来，梦中这并不是世界末日……而被你杀死的都是无辜的人。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You awaken in a cold sweat, relieved that you weren't being eaten alive by "
"evil Twinkies."
msgstr "你在一身冷汗中惊醒，松了一口气——还好没被邪恶的奶油蛋糕卷给活吃了。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You awaken feeling hollow; you dreamed of your friends and family, only to "
"realize your new reality is the nightmare."
msgstr "你醒来后感觉心里空荡荡的；梦中的朋友与家人，不过是让你认清了，你如今的现实，才是真正的噩梦。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You abruptly awake, relief washes over you as you were no longer naked in the "
"street, and the zombies weren't laughing at you."
msgstr "你猛然醒来，一阵庆幸涌上心头——再也不必赤身裸体狂奔街头，丧尸再也不会嘲笑你了。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You feel something gently embrace you as you sleep.  You try to wake up and "
"see who it is, but you can't move or scream.  As teeth sink into your flesh, "
"you jerk awake."
msgstr "你在睡梦中感到有什么东西温柔地环抱住你。你想醒来并看清那是谁，但却发现自己无法移动也无法尖叫。随着牙齿深深刺入你的肌肤，你猛地惊醒过来。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You dream of a peaceful meadow, with singing birds and playing children.  A "
"sense of unease grows, as the children move around you.  You remember "
"grasping hands, flashing teeth, and ink-black eyes, holding you down, unable "
"to escape, before you wake up."
msgstr ""
"你在梦中置身于一片宁静的草地，鸟儿歌唱，孩子们嬉戏玩耍。然而，随着孩子们在你周围活动，不安的情绪逐渐滋长。你回想起紧握的手、闪烁的尖牙以及深黑如墨的眼睛，它"
"们将你牢牢压制住，令你无法逃脱，直至你从梦中惊醒。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"In your dream, you feel as if you are being watched.  A long, slimy appendage "
"snakes its way towards you, hauling you towards a dark, tooth-lined pit."
msgstr "在梦境中，你仿佛感到正被一双无形的眼睛窥视。一条湿滑而细长的触手蜿蜒伸向你，拽着你朝一个布满尖牙的黑暗深渊靠近。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"You dream that your ear is itchy.  You reach to scratch it, but when you do, "
"a flood of tiny spiders bursts out."
msgstr "你梦见自己的耳朵奇痒无比。你伸手去挠，但就在你触摸到耳朵的那一刻，一大群微小的蜘蛛突然从耳洞中蜂拥而出。"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "nightmares"
#. ~ When writing nightmares, take care to (1) ensure they are generic enough
#. that getting the same nightmare twice in a row isn't too weird, and (2)
#. that they don't assume anything about the person having them.  If your
#. nightmare reads like a horror story or creepypasta, it is probably going
#. too far. In general, avoid too much description.
msgid ""
"In your dream, you lie on an operating table, surrounded by doctors.  They "
"remove something from your body, then start yelling and screaming as the "
"thing they've cut out of you begins to tear them apart.  You find yourself "
"unable to move or even scream as it finishes with the doctors and comes for "
"you…"
msgstr ""
"在你的梦境中，你躺在手术台上，周围围满了医生。他们从你的体内取出某样东西，接着因为从你体内切除的物体开始撕裂他们而发出阵阵尖叫。当你看到它结束对医生们的攻击"
"并朝你逼近时，你发现自己无法动弹，甚至无法尖叫……"

#: data/json/snippets/nightmares.json
