#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Message of spell "afs_telepathic_confusion ( [Ψ]Sensory Deprivation )"
#. ~ Message of spell "telepathic_confusion ( [Ψ]Sensory Deprivation )"
msgid "You lock your target's mind away!"
msgstr "你封锁了目标的思维！"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Name of spell "afs_telepathic_confusion_blind"
msgid "[Ψ]Sensory Deprivation blind Effect"
msgstr "[Ψ]意识剥夺致盲效果"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Description of spell "afs_telepathic_confusion_blind ( [Ψ]Sensory
#. Deprivation blind Effect )"
msgid ""
"The is the part of the Sensory Deprivation that blinds the target.  It's a "
"bug if you have it."
msgstr "意识剥夺能力的一部分，使目标失明。拥有这个能力说明你出bug了。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/powers/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Name of spell "afs_telepathic_blast"
#. ~ Name of spell "telepathic_blast"
msgid "[Ψ]Synaptic Overload"
msgstr "[Ψ]突触过载"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Description of spell "afs_telepathic_blast ( [Ψ]Synaptic Overload )"
msgid ""
"Short-circuit and overwhelm a target's brain, causing extreme damage or "
"death.  Does not work on targets without living minds, such as robots."
msgstr ""
"Short-circuit and overwhelm a target's brain, causing extreme damage or "
"death.  Does not work on targets without living minds, such as robots."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/powers/telepathy.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy.json
#. ~ Message of spell "afs_telepathic_blast ( [Ψ]Synaptic Overload )"
#. ~ Message of spell "telepathic_blast ( [Ψ]Synaptic Overload )"
msgid "You assault the mind of your target!"
msgstr "你袭击了目标的意识！"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/powers/telepathy_concentration_eoc.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_AFS_TELEPATH_SHIELD_INITIATE"
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_TELEPATH_SHIELD_INITIATE"
msgid "You begin shielding your thoughts."
msgstr "你开始保护你的心智。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/powers/telepathy_concentration_eoc.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_AFS_TELEPATH_SENSE_MINDS_INITIATE"
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_TELEPATH_SENSE_MINDS_INITIATE"
msgid "You reach out with your powers, looking for nearby minds."
msgstr "你展开灵能场，感知附近的思维体。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/spells/psionics/telepathy_concentration_eocs.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_AFS_TELEPATH_SUGGESTION_INITIATE"
msgid "You prepare to subtly influence others' thoughts."
msgstr "You prepare to subtly influence others' thoughts."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "ultralight frame"
msgid_plural "ultralight frames"
msgstr[0] "超輕框架"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#. ~ Description of "ultralight frame"
msgid "A sturdy, lightweight frame made from titanium.  Useful for crafting."
msgstr "堅固的輕型框架，由鈦製成。用於製作。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "ultralight foldable frame"
msgid_plural "ultralight foldable frames"
msgstr[0] "摺疊式超輕型框架"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#. ~ Description of "ultralight foldable frame"
msgid "A sturdy, lightweight foldable frame made from titanium."
msgstr "堅固的輕型框架，由鈦製成。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#. ~ Description of "control station"
msgid ""
"A large and complex piloting station from a military vehicle, including a "
"camera station, steering tools, and electronics controls."
msgstr "軍用車輛上大型的複雜駕駛控制站，包括攝影監控系統、轉向工具與電子控制元件。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "quantum solar panel"
msgid_plural "quantum solar panels"
msgstr[0] "量子太陽能板"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#. ~ Description of "quantum solar panel"
msgid ""
"This solar panel is obviously cutting-edge technology and given where you "
"found it, it should probably provide a LOT of power.  It's covered in "
"strange-looking material, but the covering looks rather fragile; it doesn't "
"look like it could support a reinforcing sheet, either."
msgstr "这种太阳能电池板是尖端技术的产物，拥有极高的光电转换效能。但是它表面覆盖特殊材料让它非常脆弱，同时也无法进行强化加固。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "minireactor"
msgid_plural "minireactors"
msgstr[0] "微型反應爐"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#. ~ Description of "minireactor"
msgid "A small, portable plutonium reactor.  Handle with great care!"
msgstr "小型便携式钚反应堆，请轻拿轻放！"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "cargo trough"
msgstr "貨物槽"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cargo trough"
msgid ""
"This is little more than a sheet metal basin welded to the bottom of the "
"vehicle, extending below it.  Though it holds a lot of stuff, its shoddiness "
"makes it fragile."
msgstr "一个将薄钢板焊在车底向下凸出的金属盆。尽管它能装很多东西，但粗劣的焊接工艺使其结构脆弱。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "crude plating"
msgstr "粗製裝甲板"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "crude plating"
msgid ""
"A piece of sheet metal welded onto a vehicle as armor.  Thin, and not as "
"protective as proper armor, but it'll do if there's nothing else available."
msgstr "一片被焊接在载具外侧的薄钢板。太薄了以至于没法像正规装甲那么有效，但总比没有好。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "heavy ablative plating"
msgstr "heavy ablative plating"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "control station"
msgid ""
"A large and complex dashboard mounted with steering controls and several LCD "
"touch screens for controlling vehicle systems."
msgstr "一个巨大而复杂的仪表板，装有转向控制器和几块LCD触摸屏。你可以用它来控制载具。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "mounted external tank (200L)"
msgstr "懸掛式外置油箱（200 公升）"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "ultralight frame"
msgid ""
"An ultralight titanium framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on "
"it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size."
msgstr "一个超轻的钛合金框架。其他载具部件能够安装在它上面，在它四周增加新的车辆框架，就可以增加车辆大小。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "ultralight foldable frame"
msgid ""
"An ultralight titanium foldable framework.  Other vehicle components can be "
"mounted on it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the "
"vehicle's size."
msgstr "一个超轻的可折叠钛合金框架。其他载具部件能够安装在它上面，在它四周增加新的车辆框架，就可以增加车辆大小。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "quantum solar panel"
msgid ""
"An extremely high-performance solar panel.  Will recharge the vehicle's "
"electrical power when exposed to the sun.  Clouds will slow the recharge "
"speed.  Extremely fragile and cannot be armored."
msgstr "一块超高性能太阳能板。当暴露于阳光照射之下时，会缓慢地为车辆电池充电。云层遮挡会让充电速度更慢。非常容易损坏，且不能安装装甲。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "minireactor"
msgid ""
"A small nuclear reactor.  When loaded with plutonium cells and turned on, "
"will generate a lot of electrical power."
msgstr "一個小型核反應堆。當裝載鈽電池並開啟時, 會產生大量的電能。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "robot_carrier"
msgstr "機器人托架"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "robot_carrier"
msgid ""
"A cargo space for carrying robots.  'e'xamine it to capture a robot next to "
"you, or to release the robot currently contained.  When selecting a robot to "
"capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the part."
msgstr "一个运输机器人的货舱。按\"e\"查看该部件选择需要装载的机器人，或者卸下机器人。当选择装载机器人时，机器人需要紧挨着你。"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Atomic Compact"
msgstr "核子小型轎車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Atomic SUV"
msgstr "原子能休旅車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Atomic Car"
msgstr "原子能車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Robotic Taxi"
msgstr "機器人計程車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Armored Robot Carrier"
msgstr "裝甲機器人載體"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Atomic Sports Car"
msgstr "原子跑車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Enforcer Patrol Car"
msgstr "Enforcer Patrol Car"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Bubble Car"
msgstr "單人小車"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Light Cycle"
msgstr "Light Cycle"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicles.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicles.json
#. ~ Vehicle name
msgid "Lynx Explorer"
msgstr "猞猁探险家"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "strange object"
msgid "strange object"
msgid_plural "strange objects"
msgstr[0] "奇怪物品"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of "strange object"
msgid "An object of uncertain origin, unusually heavy for its size."
msgstr "一种来历不明的物体，对他的大小来说不同寻常地重。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It looks like a glob of white plastic streaked with bits of red and black has "
"melted over a jagged chunk of mixed scrap metals.  There are two large and "
"sharp pieces of metal jutting out from the side in parallel.  The metal is "
"very slightly, inexplicably slimy to the touch.  If you hold it up to your "
"ear, it emits a low, oscillating hum very quietly.  Unsettling…"
msgstr ""
"它看起来就像一团白色的塑料，上面有红色和黑色的条纹，在一大块参差不齐的混合废金属上融化了。有两块锋利的大金属片平行地从侧面伸出。金属非常轻微，摸起来莫名其妙"
"地粘糊糊的。如果你把它举到耳朵边，它会非常安静地发出一种低沉的、振荡的嗡嗡声。令人不安的…"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It's a brown, flaky rock just bigger than your fist.  Horrifically, what seem "
"to be small animal bones stick out of it at weird angles.  Something that "
"looks suspiciously like blood very slowly oozes out from between the layers "
"in the rock - almost imperceptibly slow - almost as if something living were "
"freshly crushed between the sedimentary layers.  But that would be impossible…"
msgstr ""
"它是一块棕色的薄片岩石，比你的拳头还大。令人毛骨悚然的是，看起来像是小动物的骨头以奇怪的角度从里面伸出来。一种看起来像血的东西从岩石的两层之间非常缓慢地渗出"
"-几乎察觉不到-几乎就像是沉积层之间新压碎的生物一样。但那是不可能的，…"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It's a small wooden cuboid with a large rectangular hole running from one "
"side to the other.  The wood is well-treated and it seems completely mundane "
"at first.\n"
"\n"
"If you look through the hole, everything looks normal.  It's only when you "
"wave your hand in front that you realize that you can't see yourself!  If you "
"stick your finger inside the hole, it doesn't seem to come out the other "
"side.  How is that possible?!"
msgstr ""
"它是一个小木制长方体，从一边到另一边有一个大的长方形洞。这块木头经过了很好的处理，乍看起来很普通。\n"
"\n"
"如果你从洞里看，一切看起来都很正常。只有当你在前面挥手时，你才会意识到你看不到自己！如果你把手指伸进洞里，它似乎不会从另一边出来。那件事怎么可能？!"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"You could be wrong, but it appears to be maybe 6 or 7 colorful glass bongs "
"fused together in a ball-shaped mess of melted glass, reminding you strangely "
"of an art exhibition you saw once.  When you pick up the object, you notice a "
"pale purple ooze trapped in the middle of the glass meld.  It's iridescent, "
"colloidal, and slightly viscous, although it doesn't remind you of any fluid "
"you've ever seen before."
msgstr ""
"你可能错了，但它似乎是六七个彩色玻璃棒融合在一起，形成一个球状的熔化玻璃，奇怪地让你想起你曾经看过的一次艺术展。当你拿起这个物体时，你会注意到玻璃熔块中间有"
"一个淡紫色的渗出物。它呈虹彩状，呈胶状，略有粘性，尽管它不会让你想起你以前见过的任何液体。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It's colored jet black and looks suspiciously like the ridged horn of a goat, "
"only seemingly studded with red gems and carved with inscriptions.  You're no "
"expert, but these inscriptions are unlike anything you've ever seen humans "
"make, with many geometric shapes inside squares that could be words or "
"characters.  There are thin, intricate lines weaving all over the horn, "
"curving in a way that you're sure could only be achieved with laser engraving "
"technology yet you feel certain they were not."
msgstr ""
"它的颜色是乌黑的，看起来很像山羊的脊角，只是表面上点缀着红色的宝石，上面刻着铭文。你不是专家，但这些铭文不同于你见过的人类制作的任何东西，方块中有许多几何形"
"状，可以是单词或字符。细细的、错综复杂的线条在牛角上到处编织，弯曲的方式你肯定只有用激光雕刻技术才能实现，但你肯定它们不是。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It appears like a normal book with a bright blue cover from a distance, but "
"when you pick the object up you notice it's simply a thick slab of some dense "
"material shaped like a book.  It's oddly stocky and brightly colored, "
"textured with low-resolution images almost like an object that fell straight "
"out of an old video game.  On the cover is just the number \"19\" and below "
"it the words \"A new bible by\" but there's no author listed.  In fact, "
"there's no other text on the entire object."
msgstr ""
"从远处看，它像一本封面亮蓝色的普通书，但当你拿起它时，你会发现它只是一个形状像书的、由某种致密材料制成的厚板。这个物体形状古怪，显得粗短，表面纹理如同低分辨"
"率的图像，几乎就像一个直接从老式电子游戏中掉出来的物体。封面上只有数字“19"
"”，下面写着“一本新的圣经”，但没有列出作者。事实上，整个物体上也没有其他文字了。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It seems to be a heavy chunk of light pink amber.  Suspended inside the amber "
"are… fossils?  You're unsure what to call them.\n"
"\n"
"One appears to be a small ball of hair with copper wires reaching out in one "
"direction, reminiscent of an amoeba reaching for something.  Another appears "
"to be a tiny fern, only made out of a highly iridescent metal, with blades "
"quite literally as thin as a razor.  A third, particularly horrifying one "
"appears to be the shrunken head of a human with a network of dark red nerves "
"instead of hair."
msgstr ""
"其中一个看起来是一团小毛发，铜丝朝一个方向伸出来，让人想起阿米巴伸手拿东西的样子。另一种看起来是一种微小的蕨类植物，只由一种高度虹彩的金属制成，刀片非常薄，"
"简直就像剃刀一样薄。第三张尤其令人恐惧的照片似乎是一个人的缩小的头部，它有一个暗红色的神经网络，而不是头发。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It seems almost like a children's toy has somehow melted into a solid chunk "
"of brass.  There are bright red, green, and yellow plastic pieces fused into "
"the sides and a very distinct purple button in the middle.  When you press "
"it, however, there's a sickening squelch and you can't help but feel like "
"you're pressing into a pile of ground meat protected by this metal outer "
"shell.  Disgusting."
msgstr ""
"这看起来就像一个儿童玩具不知何故熔化成了一大块坚硬的黄铜。两边融合了鲜红、绿色和黄色的塑料片，中间有一个非常明显的紫色纽扣。然而，当你按下它时，有一种令人作"
"呕的吱吱声，你不禁感觉像是在挤压一堆由金属外壳保护的绞肉。恶心死了。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It seems like a small, jagged rock uniformly and evenly covered in bright red "
"velvet.  You feel certain that the rock came to be this way through some "
"supernatural process.  When you hold it to your ear, it emits a very low, "
"oscillating hum.  Very strange."
msgstr ""
"它看起来像一块凹凸不平的小石头，均匀地覆盖着鲜红的天鹅绒。你肯定这块岩石是通过某种超自然的过程变成这样的。当你把它放在耳朵上时，它会发出一种非常低的、振荡的"
"嗡嗡声。非常奇怪。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/artifacts.json
#. ~ Description of variant "strange object" of item "strange object"
msgid ""
"It appears to be a small black box made out of some kind of hard metal.  "
"Although it has no discernable openings, you call it a box because when you "
"shake it you can feel things moving around inside.  Strangely, though, what's "
"inside always seems to be… changing.  One moment it's a liquid, the next it "
"feels like marbles or rocks, and then the next it feels like sand.\n"
"\n"
"Although probably inconsequential, the object emits a fairly strong odor of "
"ginger at all times."
msgstr ""
"它似乎是一个由某种硬质金属制成的小黑匣子。虽然它没有明显的开口，但你称它为盒子，因为当你摇动它时，你能感觉到里面有东西在移动。然而奇怪的是，里面的东西似乎总"
"是…不断变化。一会儿是液体，一会儿摸起来像弹珠或岩石，一会儿又摸起来像沙子。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded wall"
msgstr "褪色的墙"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded wall"
msgid ""
"A yellowed, numbingly monotonous wallpaper decorates these thin walls.  They "
"smell of mildew and have a faintly damp feel."
msgstr "一张泛黄且乏味的墙纸装饰着这些薄薄的墙壁。它们闻起来像是发霉了，有一种微湿的感觉。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded gray wall"
msgstr "褪色的灰色墙壁"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded gray wall"
msgid ""
"A drab gray drywall barrier with no finishing.  Feels almost damp to the "
"touch and smells faintly of cleaner chemicals."
msgstr "没有完成的单调灰色石膏板屏障。摸起来几乎是潮湿的，并且有淡淡的清洁用化学品的气味。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded carpet, overhead light"
msgstr "褪色的地毯，顶灯"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded carpet, overhead light"
msgid ""
"A slightly moist carpet, stained yellow with age.  Overhead, a fluorescent "
"light hums a little too loudly."
msgstr "略微潮湿的地毯，随着时间的推移褪为黄色。头顶上的荧光灯嗡嗡声有点太响了。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded carpet"
msgstr "褪色的地毯"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded carpet"
msgid "A slightly moist carpet, stained yellow with age."
msgstr "略微潮湿的地毯，随着时间的推移褪为黄色。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded tile, overhead light"
msgstr "褪色瓷砖，顶灯"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded tile, overhead light"
msgid ""
"These cheap white tiles, which seem to be plastic rather than actual ceramic, "
"are grayed with age and slightly warped at their corners.  Overhead, a "
"fluorescent light hums a little too loudly."
msgstr "这些廉价的白色瓷砖看起来是塑料的，而不是真正的陶瓷，随着年龄的增长而变灰，边角略微翘曲。头顶上，一盏荧光灯的嗡嗡声有点太大了。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "faded tile"
msgstr "褪色瓷砖"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "faded tile"
msgid ""
"These cheap white tiles, which seem to be plastic rather than actual ceramic, "
"are grayed with age and slightly warped at their corners."
msgstr "这些廉价的白色瓷砖看起来是塑料的，而不是真正的陶瓷，随着年龄的增长而变灰，边角略微翘曲。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "water cooler"
msgstr "饮水机"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "water cooler"
msgid ""
"A plastic jug of water mounted on a dispenser.  Normally dispenses hot water "
"in addition to cold, but not with the power out.  You could probably salvage "
"the unwieldy jug on top with little effort, but any water still in it would "
"spill."
msgstr "安装在饮水机上的塑料水罐。通常能够放出冰水和热水，但断电时就只有常温冷水了。你或许能不费吹灰之力抢救上面那个笨重的水罐，但是仍然在里面的任何水都会溢出。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "wobbling plastic!"
msgstr "塑料晃荡声！"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "water cooler jug"
msgid_plural "water cooler jugs"
msgstr[0] "桶装水罐"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "water cooler jug"
msgid ""
"A sizable blue plastic jug meant to hold and supply water in a water cooler "
"or similar dispenser.  Holds a lot of liquid, but unfortunately it doesn't "
"come with a cap, making it hard to carry around when full."
msgstr "一个相当大的蓝色塑料壶，用于在饮水机之类的地方盛水和供水。可容纳大量液体，但不幸的是它没有带盖，装满时很难随身携带。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "almond water"
msgid_plural "almond waters"
msgstr[0] "杏仁水"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "almond water"
msgid "A bottle of what looks like slightly-cloudy water."
msgstr "一瓶看上去略微浑浊的水。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "almond water bottle"
msgid_plural "almond water bottles"
msgstr[0] "杏仁水瓶"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "almond water bottle"
msgid "A sealed glass bottle, holding a slightly-cloudy liquid."
msgstr "密封的玻璃瓶，装有略微浑浊的液体。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  The date on it is so old it seems "
"actually impossible for it to have lasted this long in such good condition.  "
"Most of the information on there is shockingly uninteresting for an artifact "
"so old, but one thing catches your eye briefly."
msgstr "仅余单张的报纸。上面的日期如此久远，照理说不可能让它维持在如此良好的状态。在这古老遗物中的大多数信息都无趣地要命，然而其中一件事稍微引起了你的注意。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  The date on it suggests it's decades "
"old, but miraculously it appears to be much newer.  Most of the information "
"on there is terribly trivial, or out of date, but one thing catches your eye "
"briefly."
msgstr "仅余单张的报纸。上面的日期表明它已有几十年历史，但奇妙的是看起来显然新得多。其中大多数信息都非常琐碎或过时，但其中一件事稍微引起了你的注意。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  It doesn't look like any newspaper "
"you're familiar with and the text on it makes no sense…"
msgstr "一张报纸。它看上去和你之前见过的报纸都不像，上面的文字毫无意义……"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  It was printed a few years ago.  "
"Most of the information on there is terribly trivial, or out of date, but one "
"thing catches your eye briefly."
msgstr "一张报纸。上面的日期是好几年前的，能完整的保存下来真是蛮奇怪的。大多是些琐碎或者过时的信息。但有一件事吸引你的目光。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  There seems to be an important "
"article about a missing person."
msgstr "一张报纸。上面似乎印着一篇寻找失踪者的重要文章。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/items.json
#. ~ Description of "newspaper page"
msgid ""
"A single sheet of newspaper broadsheet.  It was printed within the last few "
"months.  Most of the information on there is terribly trivial, or out of "
"date, but one thing catches your eye briefly."
msgstr "一张报纸。上面的日期是好几个月前的，能完整的保存下来真是蛮奇怪的。大多是些琐碎或者过时的信息。但有一件事吸引你的目光。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/map_extras.json
#. ~ Name of map extra
msgid "Red room"
msgstr "红色房间"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/map_extras.json
#. ~ Description of map extra "Red room"
msgid "There's a red room here."
msgstr "这里有一个红色的房间。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/map_extras.json
#. ~ Name of map extra
msgid "Autodoc room"
msgstr "全自动医疗仪房间"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/map_extras.json
#. ~ Description of map extra "Autodoc room"
msgid "There's an autodoc here."
msgstr "这里有个全自动医疗仪。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/modinfo.json data/mods/Backrooms/scenarios.json
#. ~ MOD name
#. ~ Name of starting location "sloc_backrooms"
msgid "The Backrooms"
msgstr "後室（Backrooms）"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "The Backrooms"
msgid ""
"A strange place between dimensions traps you.  Can you survive among endless "
"halls of yellowed carpet and harshly humming fluorescents?\n"
"\n"
"Replaces all normal worldgen: no wilderness, no rivers, no cities, no farms, "
"no sky.  Just endless, winding indoor halls of mildewy carpeting, faded "
"drywall, desolate breakrooms and abandoned boardrooms.\n"
"\n"
"Recommended city size is 0.  Play Now!  (Default Scenario) is not supported."
msgstr ""
"介於維度之間的奇怪間將你困住了。你能在這無盡的發黃地毯和刺耳嗡嗡聲的螢光燈下生存嗎？\n"
"\n"
"取代了所有的普通世界生成：沒有荒野，沒有河流，沒有城市，沒有農場，沒有天空。只有無盡蜿蜒的室內走廊，發霉的地毯，褪色的牆壁，荒涼的休息室和被遺棄的會議室。\n"
"\n"
"推薦城市大小為0。不支持「馬上玩！」（預設劇情）。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "backroom chamber"
msgstr "后室房间"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "backroom stairs"
msgstr "backroom stairs"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"I took all the supplies.  I'm sorry.\""
msgstr "\"我带走了所有的补给。抱歉。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"Someday I will wake up.  Someday I will wake up.  Someday I will wake up.  "
"Someday I will\""
msgstr "\"总有一天我会醒来。总有一天我会醒来。总有一天我会醒来。总有一天我会\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"eat the walls\""
msgstr "\"吃墙去吧\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"STAY QUIET\""
msgstr "\"保持安静\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"pray that you find the same peace I have found\""
msgstr "\"祈祷你能找到和我一样的宁静\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"IF YOU MOVE IT WILL HEAR YOU\""
msgstr "\"如果你敢动，它会听见的\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"My name is Susan Li.  If you're reading this, I'm dead.  I leave everything "
"I own to\""
msgstr "\"我叫苏珊·李。如果你能读到这个，我应该已经死了。我把所有的东西都留在了\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"225 steps from the vending machines to the couch room…  Turn left…  141 "
"steps from the couch room to the portal…\""
msgstr "\"从自动售货机向沙发房走225步……左拐……在从沙发房朝传送门走141步……\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"Welcome to Hell :)\""
msgstr "\"欢迎来到地狱：）\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"know because I was wearing my watch.  Today was another bad day.  They "
"nearly saw me as I hauled wood back to the big room, and I lost half of it "
"running away.  Tomorrow, I plan\""
msgstr "\"知道是因为我戴着手表。今天又是糟糕的一天。当我把木柴拖回大房间时，差点被它们看到，逃跑时又丢了一半。明天，我计划\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"I AM IN A TOP SECRET FACILITY BUILT BY THE GOVERNMENT!!  I HAVE BEEN "
"ILLEGALLY KIDNAPPED!!  PLEASE HELP ME!!\""
msgstr "\"我在政府建造的最高机密设施里！！我被非法绑架了！！请帮帮我！！\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"What do you want?  Am I supposed to confess??  What am I waiting for???\""
msgstr "\"你想要什么？我应该忏悔吗？？我在等什么？？？\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"…602,651  602,652  602,653  602,654  602,655  602,656  602,657…\""
msgstr "\"……602,651 602,652 602,653 602,654 602,655 602,656 602,657……\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"I AM IN A SMALL ROOM WITH MANY DESKS.  I CAN'T STAY HERE.  COME FIND ME.\""
msgstr "\"我在一个有很多桌子的小房间里。我不能一直呆在这里。快来救救我。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"This note has a bunch of lines all over it.  It looks like it might be a map, "
"but nothing is labeled and you're already hopelessly lost."
msgstr "这张纸条上画着许多线。看起来它也许是张地图，但没有任何标记，你已经完全看糊涂了。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "This paper is covered in dried blood…  Gross."
msgstr "这张纸上满是干涸的血迹……真恶心。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "This note is covered with tally marks, front to back."
msgstr "这张纸条的正面到背面都画满了计数标记。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO\""
msgstr "\"不要不要不要不要不要不要不要\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"I KILLED THEM.  I HAD TO.\""
msgstr "\"我杀了他们。我必须杀。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid ""
"\"Casey Blumenthal.  Age 34.  Bangor, Maine.  Hotel receptionist.  The last "
"thing I remember was tripping on a power cord.\""
msgstr "\"凯西·布鲁门撒尔，34岁，缅因州，班戈市，酒店接待员。我记得的最后一件事是被一根电线绊倒。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"STOP FOLLOWING ME\""
msgstr "\"别再跟着我了\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"IT'S CHASING ME\""
msgstr "\"它在跟踪我\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"Abandon hope, all ye who read this.\""
msgstr "\"给所有读到纸条的人，放弃希望吧。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "This note just has scribbles on it."
msgstr "这张纸条上只有潦草的字迹。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"Let me out.  Let me out.  Let me out.  Let me OUT.  LET ME OUT.\""
msgstr "\"让我出去。让我出去。让我出去。让我出去。让我出去。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"STAY HERE\""
msgstr "\"留在这里\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_note"
msgid "\"I have been blessed.\""
msgstr "\"我走大运了。\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_ancient_news"
#. ~ This category is for news before 1950 and should adopt the tone of voice
#. of its era.
msgid ""
"CIGARET SHORTAGE EASILY EXPLAINED!  The cigaret industry says Americans are "
"smoking at the fastest rate in history - that's why there's a shortage!  The "
"final production figure will be 257 million in 1943, compared with 243 "
"million in 1942.  Add to this tax-free shipments to armed forces - which were "
"32 million this year and increasing, up from 8 million in 1942 - and "
"civilians would be struggling this year were it not for excellent crops!"
msgstr ""
"《香烟短缺原因详解！》烟草业代表近日表示，美国人吸烟率已达历史顶峰——这就是为什么会出现香烟短缺的原因！1943年的最终产量预计将达到2.57"
"亿根，而上年度数据为2.43亿根。再加上向军队输送的免税货物——今年为3200万根，比上年度的800"
"万根有所增加——如果不是因为今年作物丰收，民用需求将会很难满足！"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_ancient_news"
#. ~ This category is for news before 1950 and should adopt the tone of voice
#. of its era.
msgid ""
"STRIKE ORE NEAR KENDALL!  A special of the 15th to the Miner from Lewistown "
"states that there is much excitement around Kendall over the reported "
"striking of a hitherto unknown ore in the Fergus tract, extending out on the "
"flat from the Bullard property, and claims are being located in all "
"directions!  Potential experts on the unknown metal are to arrive in the week."
msgstr ""
"《肯德尔附近发现新矿石！》来自路易斯敦的矿工15"
"日的独家报道，肯德尔的人们对在弗格斯矿区发现迄今为止未知矿石感到无比兴奋，这些矿石从布拉德矿区延伸开来，据称到处都是！对未知金属的潜在用途进行研究的专家将于"
"本周抵达。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_ancient_news"
#. ~ This category is for news before 1950 and should adopt the tone of voice
#. of its era.
msgid ""
"THE WEATHER: Fair tonight and Wednesday.  THIS IS REAL COMFORT!  That is what "
"they say when they try one of TROUTMANS' Vudor chair hammocks, $3.50; ask to "
"see them!  Buy one of these for the Fourth of July: Flag, size 5x8 feet, pole "
"and rope ready to hang; price, while they last, $1.75 -- TROUTMANS'!"
msgstr ""
"天气预报：今晚至周三晴天。这可真让人舒心！任何一个尝试过特劳特曼的Vudor牌帆布椅的人都会这么说的，仅售3.5"
"美元；快来试试吧！七月四日买什么：国旗，尺寸5x8英尺（约1.5×2.4米），可挂在柱子和绳子上；价格，热销中，仅售1.75美元——特劳特曼！"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_very_old_news"
#. ~ This category is for news after 1950 until the time of Cataclysm lore and
#. should adopt the tone of voice of its era.
msgid ""
"ABRAMS CONFIDENT S. VIET TAKEOVER IS SUCCESS:  Gen. Creighton W. Adams, "
"commander of US troops in South Vietnam, praised the South Vietnamese army "
"today and said its forces have \"tremendous confidence\" in their continued "
"success.  The disappearance of Gen. Bessemer last month has \"not "
"disheartened the troops\", although Adams has admitted his death at enemy "
"hands is \"likely\"."
msgstr ""
"《阿布拉姆斯的南越秘密接管行动大获成功》美国驻南越部队指挥官克雷顿·W·亚当斯将军今天赞扬了南越军队，并表示其部队对继续取得成功\"充满信心\""
"。尽管亚当斯承认自己\"很可能\"死于敌人手中，但贝塞麦将军上月的失踪\"并没有让军队灰心\"。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_very_old_news"
#. ~ This category is for news after 1950 until the time of Cataclysm lore and
#. should adopt the tone of voice of its era.
msgid ""
"LUNCH MENUS:  MONDAY, February 16 - NO SCHOOL.  TUESDAY, February 17 - Corn "
"dog with catsup and mustard, potatoes au gratin, bread and butter, buttered "
"spinach, apple half, milk.  WEDNESDAY February 18 - Wildcat goulash, buttered "
"green beans, hot rolls and butter, orange jello with pears, milk.  THURSDAY, "
"February 19 - Tacos with cheese and lettuce, applesauce, milk.  FRIDAY, "
"February 20 - Creamed turkey over mashed potatoes, peanutbutter sandwiches, "
"cherry shortcake, chocolate milk."
msgstr ""
"午餐菜单：\n"
"2月16日，周一：无课。\n"
"2月17日，周二：玉米热狗配番茄酱和芥末、烤土豆、面包配黄油、黄油菠菜、半个苹果、牛奶。\n"
"2月18日，周三：野猫匈牙利汤、黄油青豆、辣面包黄油卷、橙子果冻配梨、牛奶。\n"
"2月19日，周四：墨西哥奶酪卷饼配生菜、苹果酱、牛奶。\n"
"2月20日，周五：奶油火鸡配土豆泥、花生酱三明治、樱桃酥饼、巧克力牛奶。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_very_old_news"
#. ~ This category is for news after 1950 until the time of Cataclysm lore and
#. should adopt the tone of voice of its era.
msgid ""
"ADMINISTRATIVE ASSISTANT SOUGHT:  Eberhard Technologies, Inc. is looking for "
"a full-time (37.5 hours) Administrative Assistant.  This position requires a "
"person with excellent organizational and computer skills, capable of "
"professional discretion in their daily life.  Extensive benefits offered.  "
"Send resume to thaskins@eberhardphoenix.com."
msgstr ""
"行政助理招聘：Eberhard科技股份有限公司正在寻找一名全职（37.5"
"小时）行政助理。这个职位需要一位具有出色组织能力和计算机技能，能够在日常生活中进行专业判断的人。提供各类福利奖金。请将简历发送至thaskins@eberh"
"ardphoenix.com。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_very_old_news"
#. ~ This category is for news after 1950 until the time of Cataclysm lore and
#. should adopt the tone of voice of its era.
msgid ""
"SEARCH FOR PILOT WHO SAW UFO, DISAPPEARED:  Authorities Wednesday called of a "
"ground, air, and sea search for a pilot who vanished after radioing that his "
"lightplane was being pursued by an unidentified flying object.  An air force "
"reconnaissance plane searched 1,000 square miles of ocean for George "
"Valentina and his Cessna 182.  At one point, Valentina radioed, \"It's not an "
"aircraft…  It's…\" before the transmission broke off.  Residents of King "
"Island have reported sightings of bright and trailing lights over the past "
"six weeks."
msgstr ""
"《搜救遭遇不明飞行物的失踪飞行员》当局星期三要求开展对一名飞行员的陆海空全面搜救行动，该名飞行员在用无线电报告其轻型飞机被不明飞行物追击后失踪。一架空军侦察"
"机在1000平方英里的海洋中搜寻乔治·瓦伦蒂纳和他的塞斯纳182型飞机。在传输中断之前，瓦伦蒂纳曾用无线电发出\"这不是飞机……这是……\""
"的通报。国王岛的居民报告称，在过去六周内，他们总能在空中看到一行明亮的尾灯。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_recent_news"
#. ~ This category roughly lines up with Cataclysm's news segments newer than
#. a few months and contains some of the same snippets.
msgid ""
"DRIVING ON A WING AND A PRAYER: A New England man has proven it is possible "
"to create a new car from scrap parts using almost nothing but duct tape.  "
"When asked why he had done it, his answer was \"Well, I didn't have a welder.\""
msgstr ""
"賭命駕駛: 一位新英格蘭人成功的利用一些破爛與廢棄材料做出一台車, 而且大部分的結構是用膠帶與鋼管組成。當被問及為什麼要這麼設計時, 他說 \"嗯, "
"因為我沒有一台焊接機\"。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_recent_news"
#. ~ This category roughly lines up with Cataclysm's news segments newer than
#. a few months and contains some of the same snippets.
msgid ""
"HALLOWAY ANNOUNCES SWEEPING BUDGET BILL.  As rhetoric surrounding national "
"defense spending ramps up, Senate Majority Leader Halloway has announced a "
"controversial bill that would cut over $700 billion from multiple federal "
"organizations, including arts funding and welfare.  He introduced the bill by "
"saying, \"We stand on the edge of a new age of science and discovery, and a "
"new age of danger from enemies abroad.  Hardworking Americans can benefit "
"most by getting involved in our new civilian science programs and making a "
"difference there.  No more sitting at home playing video games!\""
msgstr ""
"《Halloway公布预算清单》随着围绕国防开支的言论愈演愈烈，参议院多数党领袖Halloway宣布了一项极富争议的法案，将从多个联邦部门削减近7000"
"多亿美元经费，其中包括艺术基金和福利。他在介绍该法案时说：\""
"我们正站在一个科学和发现的新时代的前沿，同时也是一个面临国外敌人不断威胁的新时代。辛勤工作的美国人可以通过参与我们新的民用科学项目并在那里发挥作用而获得最大"
"的利益。不要再坐在家里玩电子游戏了！\""

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_recent_news"
#. ~ This category roughly lines up with Cataclysm's news segments newer than
#. a few months and contains some of the same snippets.
msgid ""
"COUNTRY MUSIC FESTIVAL STILL ON.  Predictions of inclement weather won't stop "
"Huey Brooks, owner of Brooks Entertainment, from putting on his famous "
"country music festival.  The event has moved to the Springfield Masonic "
"Center and begins two hours earlier, at 5PM.  As the whereabouts of "
"self-admitted \"party boy\" Jerry Kenny remain unknown, local legend Poppy "
"Summerfield has been brought in to fill his slot."
msgstr ""
"《乡村音乐节仍在举行》预测恶劣天气不会阻止布鲁克斯娱乐公司老板休伊·布鲁克斯举办他著名的乡村音乐节。活动已移至斯普林菲尔德共济会中心，并于两小时前下午5"
"点开始。由于自称为\"派对男孩\"的杰里·肯尼仍旧下落不明，当地传奇人物波比·萨默菲尔德被请来填补他的空缺。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_lost_people_news"
#. ~ This category is for 'lost person' classified ads and newspaper snippets
#. about people that have fallen into to the Backrooms, from any era.
msgid ""
"KIDNAPPING IN WESTFIELD?  After a week of intense searching, chasing leads "
"across the state, the Oriole County Sheriff's Department have still uncovered "
"no leads in the disappearance of Kasey Akron, 31, postal worker and mother of "
"two.  Akron disappeared without a trace while on the job in Westfield, a "
"small village with a population of only 824, on September 24th.  Her vehicle "
"was found still running, undelivered mail left inside.  Her mother tearfully "
"testified to the Oriole Free Press, \"Kasey was a happy and loved woman.  "
"Wherever she is, we know she wants to come home!\"  Detectives previously "
"suggested that Akron may have departed with someone she knew, but have not "
"made any arrests so far."
msgstr ""
"《西菲尔德绑架案？》经过一周的紧张搜索，在全州范围内追查线索，奥利奥尔县警长部门仍然没有发现31岁的邮递员、两个孩子的母亲凯西·阿克伦失踪的线索。9月24"
"日，阿克伦在西菲尔德，这个只有824"
"人口的小镇工作时，无影无踪地失踪了。她的车被人发现时引擎仍在工作，而邮件却一封未送。她的母亲含泪向《黄鹂自由报》作证说：\""
"凯西是一个快乐且惹人爱的姑娘。无论她在哪里，我们都知道她想回家！\"警探们此前曾暗示，阿克伦可能已经和某位熟人一同离开了，但到目前为止还没有逮捕任何人。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_lost_people_news"
#. ~ This category is for 'lost person' classified ads and newspaper snippets
#. about people that have fallen into to the Backrooms, from any era.
msgid ""
"MYSTERY IN DRESDEN: Nefarious happenings are nothing new for the "
"ever-tumultuous GDR, but the peculiar mystery of two missing actors has "
"captured international attention.  Nani Wolf and Angela Weiss were slated to "
"perform in mere moments, spotted entering their dressing room with fellow "
"company members testifying to every minute and every angle, but when the "
"curtain call came, they were nowhere to be found!  Region police are baffled, "
"but have concluded there was no sign of foul play.  The girls just "
"disappeared!"
msgstr ""
"《德累斯顿的谜团》对于动荡不安的民主德国（东德）来说，发生各种邪恶的事情并不稀奇，然而两名失踪演员的神秘故事引起了国际关注。纳尼·沃尔夫和安吉拉·韦斯在原定"
"表演即将开始之时，在众目睽睽下走进了更衣室，公司同事们从各个角度、各个时刻都能作证，但当该上场时，她们却无迹可寻！当地警方对此感到十分困惑，但得出结论认为，"
"目前没有任何违法痕迹。女孩们就这样消失了！"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_lost_people_news"
#. ~ This category is for 'lost person' classified ads and newspaper snippets
#. about people that have fallen into to the Backrooms, from any era.
msgid ""
"MISSING MAN: Gerald Bienkowski, age 47.  Disappeared: April 14.  Last seen "
"leaving Tony's Watering Hole in Burlington.  Believed to be of sound mind, "
"but possibly in danger.  If seen, contact local police.  Do not approach."
msgstr ""
"失踪男子：杰拉尔德·比恩科夫斯基，47岁。失踪时间：4月14"
"日。最后一次见到他是在伯灵顿托尼的水坑。据信心理健康，但可能十分危险。如果看到，请联系当地警方。不要靠近。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_lost_people_news"
#. ~ This category is for 'lost person' classified ads and newspaper snippets
#. about people that have fallen into to the Backrooms, from any era.
msgid ""
"MISSING WOMAN: Anne Demir, age 33.  Disappeared: May 3.  Last seen driving "
"SOUTH of Dallas on I-45 at 8:45pm.  NEW DETAILS HAVE RE-OPENED THIS "
"INVESTIGATION.  New witness footage confirms Demir's car driving SOUTH rather "
"than north, as previously reported."
msgstr ""
"失踪女子：安妮·德米尔，33岁。失踪时间：5月3日。最后一次被看到是晚上8:45驾驶在达拉斯南部的I-45"
"公路上。新的细节重新开启了这项调查。新的目击者录像证实，戴米尔的汽车是向南行驶，而不是之前报道的向北行驶。"

#: data/mods/Backrooms/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "backrooms_lost_people_news"
#. ~ This category is for 'lost person' classified ads and newspaper snippets
#. about people that have fallen into to the Backrooms, from any era.
msgid ""
"NO TRACE FOUND in search for missing Lisa Hawthorne and her boyfriend Shaun "
"after 58 Civil Air Patrol members spent three days scouring the area near "
"Twelve Mile Trail.  The couple's car was found roadside near the northern "
"trailhead and they were reported missing shortly after.  The couple were \"on "
"a daily hike in a place completely known to them\", says detective Aretha "
"Wesson, who personally knew the two intrepid young athletes."
msgstr ""
"《毫无踪迹》58"
"名民航巡逻队成员花了三天的时间在十二英里小径附近地区搜索，没有找到失踪的丽莎·霍桑和她的男友肖恩的踪迹。这对夫妇的汽车在北侧小径附近的路边被发现，不久后据报"
"失踪。警探阿雷莎·韦森说，这对夫妇\"每天都在一个他们完全熟悉的地方徒步旅行\"，他亲自认识这两位勇敢的年轻运动员。"

