#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_IG882_P"
msgid ""
"PATIENT MOSAIC latest update\n"
"I am pleased to report a major breakthrough in the process of personality "
"updating.  A73 volunteered to be the initial subject to test the updated "
"version of the PATIENT MOSAIC process.  Briefing her on the effects of the "
"process demonstrated by X89 did not deter her, as well as a visit to X89 in "
"the infirmary, and after two weeks of studying the process and practicing its "
"initial protocols, she prepared for her first major effort.  A73 had severe "
"arachnophobia stemming from several incidents in her childhood, which was the "
"proximate reason for her to volunteer for PATIENT MOSAIC.\n"
"\n"
"The process took most of a day and A73 completed it with no ill effects other "
"than hunger (an IV had been administered to prevent dehydration).  When the "
"process was completed, she unwent an MRI, showing no changes in the physical "
"structure of the brain.  Subsequent to the MRI, A73 voluntarily agreed to "
"submit to a test of her arachnophobia.  She showed no reaction to "
"high-definition images of spiders and was able to remain in close proximity "
"to a spider crawling across a table she was sitting at, and while she "
"declined the researcher's suggestion of allowing the spider to crawl on her "
"arm, her vitals showed no undue distress at the suggestion.\n"
"\n"
"Further testing is necessary to determine the conditions that led to such "
"disparate outcomes, but the results of A73's tests show exceptional promise.  "
"G59 has also expressed willingness to volunteer for PATIENT MOSAIC and I "
"believe we should grant the request.\n"
"Ronald Sanchez-Perez\n"
"Researcher"
